var PilotLoreData = {"10103118": {"profile": [{"label": "Affiliation", "value": "Dawnstar League"}, {"label": "Blood Type", "value": "AB"}, {"label": "Height", "value": "165cm"}, {"label": "PAMS System Rating", "value": "SS"}, {"label": "Hobbies", "value": "Figure Skating"}], "introduction": "Rosa Díaz's younger sister, one of only two perfect Hyper-Aptamers in the world. Taken into the DL due to childhood events, she grew from a test subject of the latest technology into a super pilot carrying the hopes of the DL.\nBright and confident, elegant and courteous, she exudes a genius's aura yet always interacts with others on equal terms. When executing missions as a soldier, she often secures victory with her overwhelming personal strength, and if a teammate falls into panic, she readily comes to their aid. She is highly regarded not only in the Reversion Squad but throughout the entire DLAF. Even so, she always claims that this is not solely her own strength and resolve... What deeper meaning lies within, perhaps only she understands.", "stories": [{"title": "XC 109, December 24", "text": "\"I had that dream again today, dreaming of a group of adults in white clothes breaking into my home and taking me away from my sister. I was so scared that I couldn't move, hoping someone would come to save me... At that moment, I heard my sister calling, but when I turned around, she was already lying on the ground, with that terrifying syringe stuck in her... I was awakened from my nightmare by the nurse. Behind her was a group of people in strange uniforms I'd never seen before. They huddled around the monitoring screen by my bed, seemingly discussing my abnormal brain waves. I wanted to tell them about my dream, that I wanted to see my sister, but not a single person paid attention.How long will these days last... My sister and I, the happy life we used to have together... are they really gone forever?\""}, {"title": "XC 111, February 7", "text": "\"My sister came to see me today... She stood behind the stands of the ST testing ground, frowning through the glass, with an expression sitting somewhere between loathing and worry. I wanted to see her, to talk to her face to face, but the experiment didn't allow me to stop halfway. By the time I got off the ST, she was already gone... When I saw her again, she was covered in wounds from an emergency operation, receiving treatment in the medical room.\nWounds and injuries are hateful things, but the idea of losing my sister, the feeling of being powerless in that situation, it filled me with despair.\nThe entire time, I waited outside, pacing up and down. Eventually, Dr. Newman came out. I gathered my courage and told him my thoughts, then asked him when I could fight alongside my sister. He seemed stunned; I had never seen such a sad expression on his face. He patted my head—I could feel his hand trembling.\nHe looked around, crouched down close to my ear, and secretly told me something—he was preparing a special ST prototype challenge, and as long as everything went smoothly, my sister and I could leave and never have to face those annoying experiments and missions again. He just needed a little more time.\nI feel like Dr. Newman is different from the other white coats; he really is kind... I trust him. Until that day comes, I will find a way to cope.\""}, {"title": "XC 117, April 25", "text": "\"This is the last page of the notebook. Quite some time has passed since the last entry. It's fitting to use a long-awaited diary entry to bid farewell to the past.\nLooking back at all the previous pages, a lot of it shows my immaturity. Now I finally understand how fortunate I am compared to those poor test subjects. My sister, the doctor, Shawnee... If it weren't for everyone's protection, I might never have had the power to choose my own destiny.\nIt's incredible if you think about it. When I first accepted the experimental implantation, I was convinced I would be trapped in the Institute like a research specimen. But now, not only am I free, I've even been given the flattering title of \"Super Pilot\"—even the guys in the defense forces see me as a tough, iron-willed hero... When I think about all that happened, it's like a blur. Sometimes I wonder, which version of me is the real Ada Diaz, the one from then or the one now?\nI think the source of the confusion is that most important, irreplaceable person... the UNCS's Valkyrie, Rosa Diaz, my sister, still trapped within the shadows.\nWait for me, sister. I'm far stronger than I was before. I promise, soon we'll be reunited.\""}, {"title": "XC 119, March 9", "text": "\"The GKD Squad took my sister. Though we've been enemies more than once, I don't believe they'll hurt her. If anyone can wake her, it's them... The real problem now is me. Since fighting in that space formed by arashi matter, the voice in my head has become increasingly vivid. \"She\" has started giving me warnings, about the Oceanic Conclave's tracking, about the hostility of former comrades... The way things are going, I will become an enemy of the DL. I'll no longer be that \"Super Pilot\"...\nThis is the reality I must face. But I will not regret my choices. I can't. I chose my sister over the DL, and I must stick to that choice until the very end... Otherwise, the suffering she endured, the sacrifices made by everyone in the Reversion Squad, it will all have been in vain. I must find a way to resolve things with \"her,\" with A-00.\nThis is the end of the diary. If it falls into the hands of the Oversight Committee, everyone mentioned will be implicated. After filling the last page, the one that couldn't be filled last time, let it vanish into the flames along with all my hesitations.\"", "comment": {"by": "Matilda", "text": "The subsequent search found the diary had been burned to a cinder, but the last page drifted into a crack in the ground not far away... A whim of the wind, or, perhaps... Ada, is there still a trace of hesitation in your heart?"}}]}, "10103159": {"profile": [{"label": "Affiliation", "value": "Harpy Commerce"}, {"label": "Blood Type", "value": "O"}, {"label": "Height", "value": "172cm"}, {"label": "Side Occupation", "value": "Senior Wine Taster"}, {"label": "Likes", "value": "Antique Collecting"}], "introduction": "\"Adele Martin finally agreed to meet me—at her private winery. To cater to her taste, I brought a few bottles of treasured wine upon departure, and Adele praised them highly, personally storing them in her cellar. At the time, I thought it was a good start; although gaining Adele's favor was no easy task, at least she didn't throw me out at first sight. We did a lot of preparation to secure Harpy's funding, and Adele expressed her approval. However, Harpy's assessment of a new team's capabilities is extremely strict, and I must admit Adele's professionalism, knowing how to make a rejection that allows both parties to maintain dignity. Failing to gain Harpy's support, my team gradually fell into low spirits, forcing us to risk it all by taking on dangerous tasks. They were far beyond our ability to handle, and we nearly faced total annihilation. But the unexpected happened; amidst a siege, I saw the late-arriving Adele, who shielded me from artillery, congratulating me on passing the final test. From then on, Harpy would be our most solid industrial supporter... It turns out she had been closely monitoring us during our struggling days. For some reason, seeing her beautiful smile, a chill rose in my heart. The most solid backer also seemed like the hardest mire to escape.\" —A Burned, Anonymous Memoir", "stories": [{"title": "Elegant Walker", "text": "\"The new commissioner was stunning, effortlessly capturing everyone's attention as she stepped into the office hall. Naively, I thought she was just here as the spokesperson for some mercenary team to discuss business, and I wondered how such a captivating type could appear among mercenaries. It wasn't until she made her way through the crowd to greet me that I realized Adele Martin, this radiant woman, was going to work with me.\nBefore her, most of the commissioners I encountered had an elite demeanor, always in perfectly tailored suits, with impeccable hairstyles, and a black briefcase that never left their side, ready to make a perfect appearance at any time of the day. But Adele was different. She was a refined woman with high standards for quality of life. Even during urgent missions, if you approached her during break time, you had to patiently wait for her to finish yawning lazily before discussing business. However, this didn't mean she was unprofessional. On the contrary, it was her meticulous planning and calculations that allowed her to have a peaceful break even during urgent missions.\nI was curious about the background of this beautiful lady. After several collaborations and becoming familiar with each other, we talked about the past over a drink one time. She poured me a glass of red wine, a specialty from her hometown—one of them, as I knew her hometown Belvino was also the world-renowned perfume capital. It turned out she came from such an elegant and romantic place, though I didn't know why she was now in Milkhama. When we touched on this topic, she looked out the window and gradually fell silent... Perhaps there's a more intricate story behind it? I didn't say anything further, just gently clinked my glass against hers.\" —Excerpt from the musings of a former employee of Harpy Trading"}, {"title": "Nonconformity", "text": "\"Andy, lately I've been feeling uneasy, and Adele might have already sensed something is wrong. Some time ago, she inquired about the management situation at Franchet, and since then, she's often been out and about, perhaps trying to ease our burden... Ah, Andy, I think the day we've foreseen has finally come.\nIn the blink of an eye, eight years have passed. The frail girl rescued from the fire eight years ago has now grown into a graceful young lady. I've always emphasized to you that Adele is the most special child in Franchet. This uniqueness is not just about her distinctive appearance, but also her overly sensitive personality. I don't know what kind of education she received from her parents before, but judging by her keen observation skills, precocious thinking, and knowing how to make her life better, perhaps she has endured many hardships in the past...\nFranchet was initially established to provide a shelter for children who lost their loved ones, without expecting anything in return. Moreover, Adele is still a child, and she has her own, longer path ahead, and shouldn't stop for Franchet.\nAndy, I've heard that you are now teaching at the business school. Could you write a letter of recommendation for Adele, so she might qualify for an exceptional admission review? If you have any doubts, you can come back and meet the child—she certainly won't disappoint you.\" — Handwritten letter record by the director of Franchet Orphanage"}, {"title": "Radiant Star", "text": "\"Adele Martin? Heh. Of course I know her—the new favorite Saliman's been grooming lately. She's constantly accompanying her to seminars. Someone even spotted her at Mr. Huber's charity auction last time. Why, you ask? Frankly, I'm curious myself what she did to earn Saliman's attention straight out of graduation. But for us, that's beside the point. This is a signal. A critical one. Saliman may already be laying the groundwork for her next commercial expansion, and Adele Martin is just one small piece of that puzzle.\nYou'd do well to make her acquaintance. Anyone who catches Saliman's eye has to be exceptional in some way. While you're at it, find out whether Saliman really intends to extend her reach to Milkhama Island. I have a feeling her recent moves are based on new intelligence. What's the difficulty in socializing? Invite her out for a few bottles of good wine in my name. She's from Belvino, isn't she? The wine I have here is something even Saliman still talks about. She won't dislike it.\" —Recorded call with a senior executive of a corporate group"}, {"title": "An Answer", "text": "\"Before leaving Harpy for good, I followed Adele on one last mission. It took place in Thepia, assisting 'Roaring' in a stronghold seizure.\nRoaring was a mercenary group Adele had believed in from the beginning. We tracked several of their operations, and she praised them as disciplined and unyielding. What they lacked wasn't resolve, but funding and equipment. Adele devised a rigorous evaluation plan, and after they passed, entered into a long-term partnership with them. In the end, they were annihilated by Thepia's artillery. Adele wasn't surprised. Milkhama has no shortage of mercenary groups, and no one remains undefeated forever. She calmly laid a wreath for Roaring's commander, her eyes utterly still. ...but I was not the same.\nEven now, I can't remember how I survived that inferno. The pain from the shellfire still blurs my senses at times. The one thing I know for certain is that Adele never left my side—she led me through the flames to safety. Some people pass through gunfire and are left with fear, never wanting to smell smoke again. Others see it as a baptism—each trial by fire a rebirth. Adele and I were always different in that way. Now I'm writing these notes on a distant continent, while Adele continues chasing her goals on that island of endless conflict. Where does her road end? Does this life truly bring her peace? I don't know. Perhaps... only she does.\" —Excerpt from the essays of a former Harpy employee", "comment": {"by": "Dana", "text": "There's nothing simple about Adele. Whatever she's seeking, we must be careful and absolutely avoid becoming tools for her gain."}}]}, "10103185": {"profile": [{"label": "Affiliation", "value": "奥维特共和国"}, {"label": "Blood Type", "value": "AB"}, {"label": "Height", "value": "176cm"}, {"label": "专精领域", "value": "阵地攻防"}, {"label": "匿名身份", "value": "战争遗孤收容机构投资人"}], "introduction": "阿列娜·维拉，奥维特反抗军前线部队高级指挥官。看似年轻的外表下是历经战火淬炼的冷厉灵魂。战场上，阿列娜是令敌人胆寒的利刃，公国部队在与她多年的交手中深刻意识到了她的可怕，将其列为「必须优先清除的目标」。但鲜为人知的是，阿列娜冰冷的外壳下其实藏有一颗炽热滚烫的心。在漫长的指挥生涯中，她也数度面对被迫放弃战友保全大局的挣扎时刻，每一条逝去的生命都化作了她心上的刻痕，随着一次次有力的搏动，凝聚成新的力量，再支撑着她竖起新的战旗。\n阿列娜也是为数不多在经过叶夫根尼·高曼的背叛之后，还愿意相信他的人。不论是作为长官还是部下，阿列娜都清晰地明白、并恪守着自己的职责。她总是坚定地向前迈步，只为抵达那个他们所有人都渴盼着的终点。", "stories": [{"title": "焦土之影", "text": "「我还记得那孩子刚被接回来的模样，瘦弱得像根杂草——头发也像杂草，乱七八糟缠在一起把脸挡住，也看不清那小东西是男娃还是女娃。直到高曼把那堆已经长出了跳蚤的『杂草』全剃掉之后，我们才恍然大……并没有，那孩子实在太瘦了，而且眼神比一些老兵都瘆人，让人拿不准性别。\n高曼说她是女孩，从索科尔街区救回来的，这次我们才真正恍然大悟。索科尔街区隔三差五就会爆发示威活动，前段时间公国里的那些老东西们终于受不了了，派出好几波军队去『清理街道』，看样子应该也是圆满完成了任务吧……\n女孩说她叫阿列娜，我注意到她手里死死握着一枚弹壳，她说话的时候眼睛里没有一滴泪水，只有一种近乎死寂、却又亮得骇人的深刻恨意。我知道这种恨意将无法被消除，也许会像影子一样一生和她紧贴在一起。但看见她拖着比自己还高的旧式步枪一言不发地把自己塞进我们这座充满机油和血腥味的军营中后，我也知道她已经接受了这种看上去过于沉重的刻印……这说不定就是变得强大的代价。\n」——无名老兵日记节选"}, {"title": "理想光明", "text": "「捷报传来时我还在修理间拧扳手，外面喧哗不停我才知道是高曼他们回来了。从他们脸上的喜悦表情就不难看出这次的战果是何等丰盛，基地里所有人都为此而疯狂，劣质酒精撒的到处都是，让人每一口呼吸都眩晕不已。\n那天还破天荒地下雨了，但雨水无法浇熄他们的热情。我看着他们在泥泞中拥抱、跳舞、放声歌唱，每个人脸上都一扫往日的沉闷，换上了那种我很久没见过的，真正属于普通人的笑容，充满希望的笑容。他们说战争很快就要结束了，而我们会是最终的赢家，当新一年的雪落下、新一年的太阳再次升起时，这片土地会变得更加平静与祥和。\n听他们这么说，我还是有点遗憾，因为我还没有亲手向仇敌们开过枪，而以后我可能也没有机会了。但听着耳畔那潮水般的欢呼，我感到自己的心里涌出一股暖流。代表希望的光明平等地照耀在了我们身上，那理想的未来似乎也不远了。」——阿列娜工作日志"}, {"title": "绝望守候", "text": "「不知不觉，阿列娜的头发已经长得那么长了。她戴上了军帽，把自己的长发束在脑后，有时候我也觉得不可思议，明明她刚来的时候还是寸头，没想到才过了这么短的时间，她的头发就已经可以随着她开枪的动作而摆动了……是啊，一切都变了。我甚至开始怀疑那天胜利后的狂欢只是一场梦，又或者只是一场群体幻觉——公国派出的怪物们在战场上就像是魔鬼一样的存在，时至今日我还是会想起他们的机兵是怎么一枪一枪、一刀一刀把我的战友从战场上抹杀的，普通的人类怎么能做到？\n……我们的战线被击溃了，队伍四分五裂，高曼也不知所踪，一种粘稠的绝望感堵塞了大部分人的心脏，唯有阿列娜……唯有那个瘦削的身影抱着枪站起来，说她会带领大家继续走下去。我无言以对，但我也知道我不忍心让她孤立无援。\n」——无名老兵日记节选"}, {"title": "未来光明", "text": "「德米特里和维克托的争吵这些天来一直没停过，我明白，战线拉得太长太久，所有人都陷入了虚无的疲惫当中，有人想放弃是最正常不过的事。可看着曾经也在死亡线上深深拥抱过的战友，如今却在会议桌前互相指责对方是叛徒……真是让人感慨万千。\n我清楚地知道自己的心从未动摇过，我的战火也不会熄灭，但那些越来越强烈的质问会像毒雾一样侵蚀我的骨髓，我不能忽视。高曼已经消失很久了，我偶尔会想如果他还在这里，他会做什么？又会思考什么？可惜不会有人回答我。我要的答案远在一个炽热的岛屿，可我偏偏无暇分身，去那里问个明白。如果他真的有不为人知的谋划，也许我能做的只有保留住更多的火种，等待他们可以被点燃的那时候到来。当新一年的雪落下，新一年的太阳再次升起时，至少还活着的我们可以再创造新的希望。」——阿列娜工作日志"}], "cn": true}, "10103135": {"profile": [{"label": "Affiliation", "value": "General Security Administration"}, {"label": "Blood Type", "value": "B"}, {"label": "Height", "value": "179cm"}, {"label": "Codename", "value": "\"Empty Shell,\" Cheesy Charmer"}], "introduction": "A polite young man, his good manners and industriousness make him the best representative for both the \"Madam\" and the UNCS GSA. Much is said of his origins. Some say he is the eldest son of a family of agents, others claim he is an orphan who received secret training, and some even suggest he is a descendant of a fallen royal family or a kept man by the \"Madam\"... None of these stories can accurately define Smiths Anderson. He himself is indifferent to this gossip, viewing society from the outside in, constantly switching between different personas, playing roles, adapting to different situations and expectations as need be. The only regrettable aspect is his somewhat outdated personal taste, such as collecting old jokes, which has earned him the nickname \"Cheesy Charmer\" among his colleagues.", "stories": [{"title": "Performance Preparation", "text": "Empty Shell was the unanimous name given to him by the adults at the institution, and it was the name he held the longest during his childhood. At that time, he was silent and reserved, yet possessed a sensitivity to understand people's hearts and a strictness towards himself. No matter how difficult the rules were, he could adhere to them meticulously, and no matter how challenging the problems were, he could overcome them perfectly. Because he never showed his emotions, he resembled a perfect doll more than a child of his age. Due to this flawless pretense of obedience, several families took him in as an adopted child, but it wasn't long before he was returned by his guardians. \"It's terrifying! We gave him care and affection, yet he never responded like a child. He'd mirror it back at us, like a hollow reflection, as if he were acting. The uncanny feeling... it's demonic!\" The adults invariably raged at the person in charge, claiming they were deceived by the institution. But only he and the institution's caretaker who always looked after him knew that this was merely his carefully calculated escape technique, a necessary preparation for the next role he would play.", "comment": {"by": "Agency Staff", "text": "We have reminded you of this child's peculiarity. He is not good with words, shows no expression, and cannot express emotions... Yet anyone would be deceived by his appearance, thinking that with love, he would be different. But in reality, he is just learning and mimicking the ways of life of all the humans he sees, unconsciously displaying them... Sigh... Thinking of how he silently followed behind us, I still get chills down my spine."}}, {"title": "Backstage Organization", "text": "A shabby apartment, a cozy cottage, a luxurious mansion... It no longer matters where he goes or whom he faces, for he will ultimately return to his own humble abode. Through constant travels and living under others' roofs, he learns the different ways of human life. And he always manages to discern the subtle weaknesses of human nature at the moment of mastery, escaping by provoking his adopters... When an old butler named \"Smiths Anderson\" brings him to a new residence, he is mentally prepared to be returned once again. Yet, a day, a week, a month pass, long enough for him to almost forget how to count time, and he still hasn't met the \"Lady\" the servants speak of—his nominal adopter. \"The Lady has taken a liking to your talent, [Child]... If you can imitate anyone, you can become anyone...\" \"Become a mirror to the world,\" is the only response the old butler, who calls himself Smith, ever gives to the \"empty shell's\" inquiries, day after day teaching him everything from business studies, negotiation, physical skills, to scouting. He tirelessly pursues perfection, driven by a newly-sprouted emotion: curiosity.", "comment": {"by": "Servant", "text": "He is the child the lady has been most satisfied with so far. Even the usually stubborn Mr. Smith rarely showed a gentle attitude, privately reminding us countless times to treat him with the status of 'Young Master.'"}}, {"title": "Welcome Speech", "text": "Miss... no, when meeting the source of his curiosity, the old butler had him change it to \"Madam.\" [Madam] was different from those adults who sought emotional returns by posing as parents. Instead, she treated him as an equal. He could read from [Madam]'s attitude that this person was not afraid of his hollow self and accepted him wholeheartedly. During his days with [Madam], he played the roles of doorman, waiter, chef, bodyguard, advisor, lover, and even rival... As for his true nature, intelligence reports seized from the enemy poured in like snowflakes, yet not a single one could capture him in full... \"Now, it's time for you to take up the name Smiths Anderson...\" This was his last meeting with the old butler. the white-haired \"Smiths Anderson\" handed him a delicate antique pistol and a UNCS Bounty Medal with a ribbon. It was also from that moment that the \"hollow\" had a name of his own for the first time, \"Smiths Anderson.\"", "comment": {"by": "Naomi", "text": "\"Smiths Anderson,\" the legendary agent codename of the UNCS! It has been active for hundreds of years! But even I don't know exactly how many \"Smiths Andersons\" there have been. In any case, many of the deeds associated with this codename have almost become urban legends. Perhaps the soon-to-be-released \"Smith 009: The Golden Left Hand,\" based on a true story, will provide some reliable clues?"}}, {"title": "Performance Begins", "text": "Smiths Anderson arrives in Milkhama as the sole accompanying advisor appointed by [Madam], endowed with executive power second only to her. His principle of maintaining exceptional efficiency is to never do anything unnecessary during work. To gather intelligence, he always manages to connect with various figures on the island. \"Fate is both the beginning of fortune and misfortune,\" the previous Smiths Anderson once advised him. To avoid causing unnecessary trouble for the GSA, he constantly switches between different personas to handle surrounding affairs. As [Madam]'s \"other side,\" as the eyes and dagger of the GSA, and as part of the UNCS's will, he operates with an enigmatic identity in various settings across Milkhama—just like the old butler once did. After all, no matter how perilous the task, for \"Smiths Anderson,\" it's merely going through the motions."}]}, "10103160": {"profile": [{"label": "Affiliation", "value": "GKD"}, {"label": "Blood Type", "value": "O"}, {"label": "Height", "value": "163cm"}, {"label": "佣兵等级", "value": "D"}, {"label": "PAMS System Rating", "value": "▇▇"}], "introduction": "猎豹物流的新人佣兵，也是电鳗佣兵团的编外成员。她因爷爷年轻时的淘金旧事而对米赫玛心生憧憬，在虚假广告和无良掮客的忽悠下孤身偷渡登岛，一番阴差阳错之后被晨星同盟军抓捕并植入了实验芯片，后又与电鳗佣兵团的两人一同逃出生天。经过误解与战斗后一直留在猎豹物流偿还债务，并学习着如何以佣兵身份生存下去。她天真烂漫自来熟，活力四射却冒失，有些戒心但不多，在兵连祸结的米赫玛总是显得格格不入，但正因此很少有人能意识到，那懵懂无知外表下藏着惊人的勇气和意志力，一旦她认定了一件事就会咬牙坚持直至完成，无论过程中有多么害怕和后悔——这份觉悟让她接受了海莉丝改制的新型战斗芯片，为了保护自己和同伴而踏上战场。\n「总有一天，稚嫩的猎豹会习惯追逐与狩猎，新生的电鳗也将自如地释放电流……」", "stories": [{"title": "新历117年11月6日 晴", "text": "爷爷今天的状态不错，不仅能自己下床，还在门外的椅子上晒起了太阳。我陪着他，听他又一次说起年轻时的淘金故事。\n这个故事我从小到大不知道听了多少遍，都能一字不差地背下来了。即便如此，我还是认真地听着，不想遗漏任何一个片段。他又一次说到一起淘金的伙伴，说到亲手挖出的第一桶金，说到奥卢姆矿场……这种时候，爷爷脸上总是挂着怀念的表情。我也又一次没能忍住提问——「爷爷，你不回矿场看看吗？」\n他和过去一样轻轻摸着我的脑袋，然后摇着头说自己已经回不去了。我不明白，明明爷爷的身体已经好转，这里离港口也不远，为什么会「回不去」？我开始尝试主动寻找和米赫玛岛有关的资料，结果不管是报纸还是网络新闻，都说那里是一个美丽富饶，充满奇迹的乐园……实在不像是有什么危险的地方。\n如果有一天，我能带爷爷回到米赫玛岛，他会不会露出更多笑容，会不会告诉我更多故事呢？"}, {"title": "新历119年2月28日 阴", "text": "一个月前的雨夜，爷爷走了。\n陆陆续续来了许多陌生人，似乎都是爷爷的旧识。哀悼之后，他们有人放声痛哭，有人转身就走，有人留下了一些钱，也有人问我是否需要新的照顾……我已经记不清当时是怎么回答的，总之，我还是一个人留在了这里。门外的木椅子没了主人，成了野猫的休息地。我学爷爷那样去喂它，它没有逃跑，但也一口不吃。又过了几天，它也不再来了。\n我开始整理爷爷留下的东西，就在那时看到了一份被细致保存着的旧报纸，上面满是三十多年前的人们对米赫玛岛的赞许与祈愿……「只有敢打敢拼的淘金者才能把握未来」，爷爷也曾对我说过同样的话。就是在那个时代，他成为了一名淘金者，改变了自己的命运。我最喜欢的那些故事，也是因此而开始。\n……我也想做一样的事。\n爷爷的铲子依然放在床边，那是他亲手托付给我的宝物。小时候的我拿不住这么沉的东西，但现在的我已经可以挥舞它、带走它……我已经做好准备，成为一个像爷爷那样了不起的淘金者了。而第一步，就是去米赫玛岛。", "comment": {"by": "Dana", "text": "结果这傻孩子不知怎么联系上了偷渡的佣兵，花高价溜进TINA号就这么登了岛……我得说说哈维了，以后必须严格把关，免得哪天因为一些小便宜惹出大祸。"}}, {"title": "新历119年3月26日 晴", "text": "终于有时间写日记了。在登岛之前，我没想过生活会变得这么「充实」。先是稀里糊涂背了一身的债，然后坐上机兵闯进了战斗，结果被晨星同盟抓走拷问还植入实验芯片……幸好我遇到了蒙福梅和芬里尔，他们也许不是好人，但却是我的伙伴，也是我登岛后的第一批朋友！如果没有他们，我肯定早就死在牢房里了。再后来，我们因为误会和猎豹物流打了一架，当时的我还不知道他们原来是全岛都没什么人敢惹的厉害家伙。好在大家其实都是好人，解开误会后就转为合作，共同对抗同盟军……这种化敌为友的桥段我以前只在电影里看到过，没想到现实里真的存在！可惜最后出了一些差错，没能带走机兵奈芙蒂斯。\n在那之后我就一直留在猎豹物流，一边学习如何当佣兵，一边挣钱还债。凯登老大忙得到处跑，偶尔会教我一些非常有用的佣兵知识；黛娜看着酷酷的，但她是猎豹物流里最关心我的人；格兰特时不时拉着我就偷懒，有好吃的好玩的总会分我一份；哪怕是最开始骗了我的哈维也不完全是个黑心船长，帮了我不少忙……要是能发点奖金那就更好了！\n另外，前两天我还跟蒙福梅和芬里尔见了次面。他们已经回归了电鳗佣兵团，说是电鳗的老大跪在地上一把鼻涕一把泪恳求，他们才勉为其难答应的……这个，多半是在吹牛吧？现在的我可不会这么轻易被骗到了。不过看他们那么神气的模样，我也觉得很开心。\n「淘金者所能依靠不只是手里的铲子，更是和自己同行的人」——现在的我好像能理解爷爷的这句话了。虽然不知道还要花多少时间，才能像爷爷那样找到属于自己的宝藏……但我相信，只要和现在的同伴一直走下去，总有一天会实现的。"}, {"title": "新历119年4月17日 多云", "text": "局势变得越来越坏了。西边的北陆联合和东边的晨星同盟开始打仗，黑曜石公司四处捣乱，还有什么奥维特公国的禁军……最糟糕的是，连凯登老大都失去了消息。\n猎豹物流的大家都在为了改变现状而努力，只有我什么也做不到。我很想帮到大家，但我什么都不会，什么也不懂，就连清理格纳库也老是犯错。只有机兵驾驶……或许是被植入过实验芯片的缘故，我能以自己都惊讶的速度学会如何驾驶机兵。但是，猎豹物流的敌人不是企业精兵就是正规军队，黑障和禁军更是让老大都头疼的怪物。要想在与他们的战斗中派上用场，只是「会驾驶」是远远不够的。\n我不想成为小葵口中那个需要被保护的人，我想成为真正的猎豹和电鳗，在关键的时刻能够挺身而出拯救同伴！所以，当奥德莉拿出那台奈芙蒂斯时，我立刻就答应了。半吊子的机师与半成品的机兵重逢……这或许就是命运。\n海莉丝为我植入了全新的战斗芯片，还帮忙改修了机兵奈芙蒂斯，让我能自如地操控它去战斗，就算还不足以成为真正的战士，至少不会再拖大家的后腿。\n铲子也被我放进了机师舱，即使不能用于战斗，它也会代替爷爷保佑着我。等到尘埃落定的那天，我们不用再战斗了，我就卸掉奈芙蒂斯的武器，把铲子装到最醒目的位置，然后继续寻找属于自己的宝藏。"}], "cn": true}, "10103127": {"profile": [{"label": "Affiliation", "value": "Vesper"}, {"label": "Blood Type", "value": "A"}, {"label": "Height", "value": "159cm"}, {"label": "Special Inventions", "value": "Nadib Core"}, {"label": "Bedtime Reading", "value": "Warzone Travel Guide: Battlefields to Beauty Spots"}], "introduction": "\"Where did we leave off last time? That's right, for battle plans, ask Cassha; for ST maintenance, go to Lorenzo. If you need fine-tuning like weapon modifications, you should find Arthur. Her workshop is at the third entrance down the base corridor—hold on! Don't rush off just yet, there are a few things to keep in mind before you go. First, never use Arthur's name lightly, not even as a joke... unless you want to get hit. Second, when writing your order, be concise and straightforward about what you need, don't beat around the bush... or she'll get angry. Lastly, if you hear complaints, keep smiling and stay silent... otherwise you'll just hear even more. Haha, don't be nervous, despite all the rules, the girl isn't bad. As long as Arthur has promised something, she'll go all out to make it happen. To meet everyone's bizarre modification requests, Arthur's workshop often stays lit deep into the night... Last of all, you should mingle with the others, get to know them. Oh and, again, seriously: don't joke about Arthur's name!\" —A Vesper Warrior's Chat Log", "stories": [{"title": "Shadows of Childhood", "text": "Long before Arthur could remember, her parents had fallen in the border war. By the statutes of the relief act, Arthur—recognized as a war orphan—was to be placed in an orphanage established by a subsidiary of the DL, where she would receive a complete education and meticulous care until the day she grew into a \"sound and capable citizen\" of the League. But reality, as always, fell far short of the promises made by the authorities.\n\"Honestly, what kind of girl goes around with a name like ‘Arthur'? Such a tomboy!\"—\"Oh no, the tomboy's angry! Quick, run, run!\"—\"Arthur, why are you whining about changing your name again? Can't you just behave? This was your parents' last gift to you, their final wish—don't you dare betray it!\"\nMockery. Bullying. Indifference. These were the patterns that defined Arthur's life within the orphanage. Her only comfort lay in the small stack of books left behind by her parents. Whenever the cruel children came to torment her, she would run to her room, barricade the door, and lose herself in the dense, difficult pages. After all... books never laughed at her.", "comment": {"by": "Lorenzo", "text": "\"A General Discussion on Mech Soldier Artillery Craftsmanship,\" \"A Brief Introduction to Mech Soldier Device Applications\"... The things Arthur's parents left for this child were truly, er, substantial."}}, {"title": "Journey", "text": "Arthur remembered it clearly; the day was stiflingly hot. The STs, once confined to the outskirts, began appearing more and more frequently within the city. The rigid welfare director had grown increasingly eccentric, constantly muttering words like \"Vesper\" and \"terrorists.\" It was on that very day that Arthur encountered the so-called \"Vesper\"—an wounded warrior slumped against the wall, refusing to let the flames of war spill into this place. Though the patrolling soldiers were only streets away, she did not step into the orphanage. Before the DL pursuers arrived, Arthur had already pulled the warrior inside. She knew which alleys wound through the cluttered buildings, and which walls hid a passage no one else noticed. The only difference was, this time, she would not be running from those kids... she'd be running from fully-armed soldiers. When they finally got out of the city, the warrior asked her what she wanted. Arthur lowered her head. \"I just want... to leave this place.\" \nIt wasn't until much later that Arthur understood—the person she had helped that day was no ordinary soldier. It was none other than the top figure of \"Vesper\"—Cassha Lumiere."}, {"title": "Problem Child", "text": "Life for Arthur in Vesper was far from smooth sailing. Growing up in an orphanage, she spent every day outsmarting and outmaneuvering the troublemakers. Even after changing environments, Arthur had no idea how to interact with people. Mentioning names led to arguments, bringing up issues made her anxious, and when she lost her temper, the entire base could hear her. It took less than a week for Arthur to become the infamous \"Problem Child\" of Vesper. In truth, Arthur wasn't blind to these issues— she genuinely wanted to change. She once tried to imitate Cassha, answering rudeness with a gentle smile. But her awkward grin only made them laugh harder—followed by a heavier punch... Another time, Arthur made efforts to listen when others talked about her, like Lozolen But the others simply assumed she wasn't angry and kept on talking until Arthur was about to explode. Faced with these frustrations, Arthur turned to Cassha. Cassha patted her on the head and told her simply, \"You don't have to be us. You have to learn to be yourself.\""}, {"title": "\"Nadib\"", "text": "To pinpoint when Arthur was officially listed as a target by the DL, we must retrace our steps back to the \"Fog Zone Assault.\" In that battle, the DL specifically chose the fog-shrouded zone as the site for their defensive line, intending to use the thick mist to block Vesper's offensive until reinforcements could arrive. Unexpectedly, a Vesper warrior named Arthur Nadib charged headlong into the fog. Braving the DL's gunport fire, she lit her guiding beacon, and under her guidance, the assault team broke through the DLAF's final defense like a hot knife through butter. It was only afterward when the DL reviewed the combat reports tied to Arthur that they realized how troublesome this fighter truly was—close-range gunport capable of blasting through armor, missiles destructive enough to wreck entire launch systems, reactive armor that could practically double as demolition charges... Arthur's inventions and modifications were cut from the same mold as the girl herself: unreasonable, obstinate, tenacious. Once she sank her teeth into a target, she would never let go.", "comment": {"by": "Elise", "text": "Although its stability and safety are appalling, the child's inventions possess a quality that the standard weapons of the Defense Force Research Institute lack—originality."}}]}, "10103149": {"profile": [{"label": "Affiliation", "value": "NERV"}, {"label": "Blood Type", "value": "Unknown"}, {"label": "Height", "value": "Unknown"}, {"label": "Likes", "value": "Playing handheld games"}], "introduction": "Asuka Shikinami Langley, the pilot of EVA Unit-02 from another world. A remarkable prodigy, her skills turn heads whether she's on Milkhama or in her homeland. After quickly adapting to Milkhama's Arashium STs, Asuka ventured behind enemy lines to the East Desert, rescuing her companions trapped by enemy forces.", "stories": [{"title": "Suspicious Pilot", "text": "\"Target Asuka Shikinami Langley, discovered near the Northern Mining Zone in the Foren Lake area. Claims to be an Evangelion unit pilot from another world. In an encounter, she single-handedly defeated ten of our Steel Puppets using only one mass-produced DL unit, nearly breaking our encirclement... We highly suspect that she is a test subject on the run from DL or other unknown forces. All departments must immediately monitor any clues related to this suspected test subject, and report credible evidence to the agency immediately.\" — GSA Agent's report"}, {"title": "Speculation", "text": "\"...During the third interrogation, Asuka Shikinami Langley gave the same testimony as the last two interrogations—her identity is that of an Evangelion unit pilot from another world, tasked with defeating creatures known as Angels and protecting the human world... Both the polygraph and psychological experts believe the subject is not lying... This leaves only two possibilities: either she underwent very thorough brainwashing during the experiment, or there truly exists another world completely different from ours as she claims. However, according to higher-level directives, further investigation into Asuka Shikinami Langley's origins is expected to be postponed, and instead, by granting her a certain degree of freedom, her behavior and reactions will be observed to determine her true intentions.\" —GSA Agent's report"}, {"title": "Desert Mirage", "text": "\"The superiors have approved Asuka's plan to go to the Eastern Desert to rescue her so-called companions and have assigned Agent Ophelia to track and monitor her actions... Although the purpose of the superiors in approving this action is not yet clear, information collected from other operatives indicates that Asuka Shikinami Langley has indeed two lost companions. They also come from the \"other world\" and are Evangelion unit pilots who fight against alien creatures known as Angels. From this scattered information, it can be inferred that the higher-ups may have already accepted the claims of these suspicious individuals. Regardless, the investigation has finally made some progress... The truth about their origins will come to light eventually.\" — Report from an Investigator of the GSA"}, {"title": "Exploration Terminated", "text": "\"Due to the impending Leviathan operation in Milthus, the investigation into these ‘visitors' has been abruptly put on hold. The precise meanings of concepts like ‘Evangelion' and ‘Angel' in their language are still to be determined. However, since the higher-ups have already permitted them to take a central role in such a crucial battle, there might not be a need for further investigation into these matters... But does another world truly exist in this universe, completely different from ours? There is still much worth exploring.\" — Report from the GSA Agent"}]}, "10103165": {"profile": [{"label": "Affiliation", "value": "Union of Northern Continental States"}, {"label": "Blood Type", "value": "O"}, {"label": "Height", "value": "166cm"}, {"label": "首次作战时间", "value": "103年2月5日"}, {"label": "Hobbies", "value": "历史研究"}], "introduction": "「我们必须承认，奥德莉是布吕希尔家一柄淬炼得过于完美的凶刃——她作战的方式莽得吓人，从来不走迂回路线，就喜欢用最强硬的手段正面突破。可偏偏是这种近乎偏执的直率与笃定自己必将胜利的信念，让她有种奇怪的魅力——她从不掩饰自己想要征服一切的欲望，反而能够凝聚起手下的一切将士，在那些家伙的身上，我们找不到任何进行渗透的机会。\n已经有不少议会上布吕希尔家的坚定反对者，只是和她接触过几次，就被她那种绝对的自信和行动力所吸引，心甘情愿为她效力。说真的，有时候我不禁会想，如果战争注定无法避免，在她这样纯粹的人麾下奋战，或许比我们现在的所作所为更有意义……」——联合安全总署干员私密通讯", "stories": [{"title": "时刻表", "text": "「06:30-07:00：列队式晨跑与基础军姿训练。由家族护卫教授如何挺直脊背，以威严的姿态行走。\n07:00-07:30：用餐时聆听家族战史的详细案例分析，与战术讲师进行讨论学习。\n07:30-10:00：基础课业教学，后进行世界军事史研习，重点讲述、拆解经典战役，并通过模拟程序进行复现，亲自体验其中。\n10:00-12:00：格斗姿势训练、障碍跑、即时反应训练、新式机兵模拟驾驶等体能训练。\n12:00-12:30：午餐。\n12:30-15:30：通过模拟程序随机生成沙盘战场，以随机讲师作为对手，以指挥官身份规划一场战役。\n15:30-16:30：向父亲进行作战汇报，复述今天沙盘推演中她的“作战计划”和理由。\n16:30-18:00：与家族核心成员共进晚餐，之后将被准许于会议室一角安静地旁听军事会议，可适时提出自己的见解。\n………………」——奥德莉·布吕希尔六岁一日计划表。"}, {"title": "初战", "text": "「那是我第一次见到奥德莉小姐——在泥浆和血污里。我们都以为要葬身在那片该死的山谷了，活着的人背靠着背，子弹打穿水壶的声音听得清清楚楚。\n就在连长咽气的时候，那个金发的身影跃上了半损的装甲车。她那么瘦小，军装下摆都在滴血，可声音却能穿过整片战场：『全军听令，现在正是进攻的最佳时机——跟我碾碎他们的指挥部！』没人敢信这个连枪都扛不稳的少女，但当她抽出军刀驱使装甲车驶向东侧山坡时，我们却不由自主地跟上了步伐，直到这时，才看见了那闪着微光的敌军通讯塔。\n她冲在最前面，子弹擦过她的鬓发时，我亲眼看见她在笑。那种笑让你觉得不是在赴死，而是在赴一场盛宴。我们像疯狗般跟着她撕裂了那道看似坚固的防线，等冲进指挥帐时，她正踩在敌人地图上，刀尖滴落的血染红了标注包围圈的箭头。\n后来才知道那是她初阵。可当你看着她在枪林弹雨里回头，用染血的手套把你从弹坑里拽起来的时候——别说指挥权了，连命你都想塞进她手里。\n从那夜起，很多像我这样的老兵就明白了，有些人天生就该站在尸山血海上发号施令。」"}, {"title": "身先士卒", "text": "「小姐，通过脊髓植入创造人工超适体的方式仍停留在试验阶段，无论是什么样的精锐战士，其试验的痛楚都足以让其精神崩溃。除去那些天生拥有资质的幸运者，剩下的九成实验者非死即残，大多都成了实验室里那些维持着基本生命体征的有机组织……恕我直言，您肩负着整个布吕希尔家族的命运，并不需要拿自己的性命去赌那一成的概率。我理解您想要身先士卒的心情，但若您真的在实验中失去理智或行动能力，那些忠诚追随您的将士们又该如何自处？比起战斗，您更应该在指挥与领导岗位上，发挥自己的才能……呵呵，果然您与我所见的任何一个布吕希尔都不一样，或许并不是布吕希尔这个姓氏赋予了您命运的特权，而是您的意志要让这一姓氏焕发出其应有的光辉。\n既然您执意要走上这条险路，至少让我为您准备好稳定剂和应急预案。我会全程守在实验室外，陪您度过这场考验。」"}, {"title": "入局", "text": "「经家族战争议会审议，因中央矿区爆炸的发生，现正式批准奥德莉提交的米赫玛岛远征申请。即日起，授予你北陆联合远征军最高指挥权，全权负责米赫玛岛一切军事维和行动及后续占领事务。\n你当以钢铁与烈火践行家族意志。然而，切记米赫玛岛的硝烟不仅源于枪炮，真正的胜利不在于碾碎多少晨星同盟军，而是为了让家族与军队赢得更多的利益。\n家族不干涉你的战术决策，但要求你必须看清：每场战役都是政治的交易，每个盟友都是暂时的筹码。你的剑应当为家族利益出鞘，你的握手应当为最终背叛做好准备。去分辨谁是可利用的匕首，谁才是必须根除的毒瘤。\n用你的锋芒去夺取胜利，更要用你日益成熟的眼光去缔结盟约——哪怕这份盟约仅能持续到下一轮炮火响起之前。作为布吕希尔家族的继承者，你要让北陆联合的旗帜，飘扬于米赫玛岛顶峰之上。」"}], "cn": true}, "10103145": {"profile": [{"label": "Affiliation", "value": "Bounty Hunter"}, {"label": "Blood Type", "value": "O"}, {"label": "Height", "value": "163cm"}, {"label": "Likes", "value": "创意手工"}, {"label": "弱点", "value": "不会算账"}, {"label": "Registered Pet", "value": "「传奇仓鼠莎尔贝」"}], "introduction": "「跨边境的物资运输？兄弟，你这预算少了点，不过也不是没有办法……这样，周末你去一趟凯德雷港的仓鼠宠物店，多半能遇见一个叫贝尔莎·瓦格纳的佣兵，她最近刚刚重建自己的佣兵团，正急着接活呢。\n这人虽然名声不大野心不小有时候还显得不太聪明，但胜在性价比……啊不，是胜在真诚努力，她一旦接了你的活儿就肯定帮你完成。唉，你可别瞧不起她啊，她在米赫玛已经混了好几年，没少和各路豪杰干架，甚至跟那个大名鼎鼎的猎豹物流都有过几次交手，结果到现在还活蹦乱跳的，光这一点就证明她还是有点本事的……至少是运气很好。而且就我所知，她和卢诺家族还有角雕商会的关系不错，真要遇到麻烦了也会有人帮忙兜底。不过有一点你要万分注意，如果她开始念叨什么『传奇佣兵的试炼』，一定要把她拉走！不然你就得面对一堆凭空出现的维修成本了。」——某佣兵网站的会员留言", "stories": [{"title": "理想崩殂", "text": "成为佣兵之前，贝尔莎·瓦格纳最大的理想是当个「学生」。作为一个生存技能只剩乞讨的孤儿，她总是能很快摸透环境中对自己最为有利的位置。比如一个叫「学校」的地方，那里虽然四面漏风，十分破旧，但每次她都能讨到暖呼呼的饭菜，予她饭菜的「老师」也很和蔼，从不表露嫌恶鄙夷。贝尔莎曾幻想，如果能一直留在这就好了，成为「学生」每天都能吃饱，还能有一个遮雨的屋檐。后来某个阳光灿烂的日子，贝尔莎如常前往「学校」觅食，却只在熟悉的位置看到一片钢筋乱石混着弹壳的废墟。她恍惚僵立，迷茫中费力思考——「学校」这么危险的地方可不能久留，当「学生」……还是算了吧。"}, {"title": "谵妄", "text": "贝尔莎的生活没有太大的变化，理想在她昏暗的生活中不过是一种无理的谵妄。她偶尔会怀念「老师」给予她食物时指尖的温度，远比食物灼烫，似乎也炽烈胜过那天废墟上空的阳光。但时间流逝，一切都离她远去。长大后的贝尔莎痛失博人怜悯的诸多要素，乞讨业绩越发惨不忍睹。她找上了街头专攻坑蒙拐骗的前辈老怀特，两人一拍即合，默契的老少搭配迅速扩张了业务舒适区。在榴弹降落之前，贝尔莎的生活一成不变，她喜欢和老怀特在一起，她不想改变也不想明天。可当她再次僵立于废墟前，听着老怀特哭着对她嘱咐，「去找道格拉斯佣兵团的乔治。活下去」时，她只想扭转一切，仿佛新的谵妄注入她的躯体。她跌跌撞撞跑向远方，深怕那悲恸的嘶吼消失在天际，无人记起。", "comment": {"by": "Naomi", "text": "埃尔文·怀特，年轻的时候是道格拉斯佣兵团有名的狙击手，在一次任务中受重伤后下落不明，没想到最终是这样的结局……果然在米赫玛岛上，什么职业都逃不过高危啊。"}}, {"title": "现实", "text": "贝尔莎以前总听老怀特吹嘘「佣兵」这一职业的美妙，自由自在、财源广进、风光无限，似乎在米赫玛能成为一名佣兵绝对是件光宗耀祖的好事。可当贝尔莎来到道格拉斯佣兵团寻找乔治时，却只找到一个潦草的墓碑，所有美好都敌不过现实的摧残。那之后贝尔莎度过了一段艰难的时期，她拼尽全力让自己变得强大，变得能够扣动扳机消除威胁，才总算在佣兵团站稳脚跟……怀着永不服输的疯狂，她把每一次战斗都当做是「传奇佣兵」必经的试炼。赢了就享受赞誉和吹捧，输了就大睡一场，等下一次赢的机会。她努力成为「最强」、做到「最好」，曾几度在强敌环伺的灰色地带大闹，也曾冲入城镇废墟解救受困的孩童，还顺带救治了一只仓鼠。\n就在她凭着战功逐渐往上爬的时候，未曾料想的巨变发生了——道格拉斯佣兵团在帕黎尔沙漠被猎豹物流击溃，随后彻底解散。贝尔莎很快就找到了新下家「夜莺特别行动队」，只是有些不巧，那正是猎豹物流的下一个目标……"}, {"title": "为光辉明日献上花束", "text": "佣兵圈子终于如贝尔莎所愿，开始流传起她的传说，只不过不那么正面——凡是她待过的佣兵团，没一个能长久的。她被视作会吸尽同伴运气的「扫把星」，一度接不到委托。\n直到某一天，她因为这份独特的「运气」而被吉诺维斯看中，从这位黑道教父手中接下了一个重要的任务……尽管最终依然受挫，但她的百折不挠赢得了卢诺家族的尊重与友谊。有了凯德雷地头蛇的支持，她的佣兵事业总算得以重回正轨，甚至有余力构思如何重建属于自己的佣兵团。\n她久违地回到儿时不愿回忆的废墟，为那些无名墓碑留下花束。现在的她满怀希望，坚信所有挡在她身前的阻碍都将被破坏，即使那「最强」佣兵的宝座仍略显遥远，她也终将抵达。"}], "cn": true}, "10103167": {"profile": [{"label": "Affiliation", "value": "Obsidian Group"}, {"label": "Blood Type", "value": "▇▇"}, {"label": "Height", "value": "▇▇"}, {"label": "▇▇", "value": "▇▇▇▇▇▇▇"}, {"label": "▇▇时间", "value": "X.C.96年"}], "introduction": "「在黑障这个名字被外界知晓时，人们对这位黑曜石本部最高执行者的认知，仍仅限于一团被▇▇抹除殆尽的记录残影。\n然而，当他们终于得知这个代号后，随之而来的并非安心，而是更深的绝望。因为他们很快发现，仅仅知晓一个名字，对于理解他、追踪他，乃至与他抗衡，皆毫无意义。那不过是让原本无形的恐惧，终于拥有了一个可以被低声提及的轮廓。\n于是，有人开始怀疑：所谓黑障是否真的存在？又或者，这个代号从一开始便不指向任何真实个体，而只是所有恐惧者在同一片阴影中，共同投射出的幻象。\n而这片阴影，并不只笼罩在外部机构之上。\n即便是在集团内部，黑曜石的成员也同样生活在黑障的注视之下。他是欧贝里斯手中最锋利、也最沉默的剃刀，曾亲手将整个集团削砍、修整成其理想中的形态；此后数十年，他又近乎无微不至地维系着这一秩序，清除偏差，修剪枝杈，抹去一切可能动摇根基的不稳定因素。\n他仿佛无处不在，仿佛有无数个分身蛰伏于阴影深处，仿佛每一次异动，每一次背叛，每一个尚未成形的念头，都早已被他看见，并在浮出水面之前悄然消除。\n所以说，他真的存在吗？」——▇▇▇▇", "stories": [{"title": "恐惧", "text": "「哈，黑曜石？别逗了。货就在这儿，你们都看见了吧？我们抢的。什么本部，什么欧贝里斯，吓唬小孩的名头罢了。等明天把这批东西拆开卖掉，我倒要看看他们能——嗯？灯怎么灭了？\n谁关的？喂，老三，你去看一眼。无线电怎么全是杂音？别他妈装神弄鬼，所有人拿枪，守住门口。\n等等，门口那是什么？\n开火！开火啊！\n不、不对，子弹没用……他在往这边走。他怎么知道我在这儿？我明明刚换了位置……头儿，头儿你人呢！你刚才不是还说他们是纸老虎吗……\n别过来！求你了，我什么都没碰，我只是跟着他们来的。我不会说出去的，我发誓……好……好的……\n我会说，我会告诉所有人……黑曜石的东西，不能碰。」——天网佣兵作战记录"}, {"title": "自阴影而来", "text": "「门锁好了吧？窗帘也拉上。很好。今晚这场会议没有记录，没有旁听，也没有黑曜石的人。\n各位，我们不需要和欧贝里斯硬碰硬。只要这份法案通过，黑曜石在米赫玛岛上的运输、武装、特别行动权限，都会一点点被收回。我们要做的，只是把绳子套上去，然后慢慢收紧。\n别紧张，政治不是战场。他们再怎么嚣张，也不可能把手伸进议会的——谁在那里？\n不可能。你是什么时候进来的？门外的人呢？说话！卫兵！\n那是什么……法案草稿？不，那份我明明锁在私人保险柜里。等等，这些名字……资金账户、家族关系、投票承诺……你把所有人都查了？\n你想要什么……什么？我、我凭什么听你的？这里是议会，不是黑曜石的办公室，你没有资格………好……我会撤回的。\n请你转告欧贝里斯，我无意与黑曜石为敌。不，从一开始就没有。\n对不起。」——北陆联合议员会议记录"}, {"title": "决战宣言", "text": "「黑障？嗯……确实是个很麻烦的对手。\n只要他一出现，疾啸就会变得有点不听使唤，艾蔻也只会在脑子里嗷嗷乱叫，完全派不上战场分析的用场。那种感觉很讨厌，就像平时在我体内流淌的东西，突然被什么冰冷的东西卡住了一样。\n……什么？你们说，那种情况下我操作机兵的方式，才比较像正常人？\n欸？原来你们平常开机兵，是那种感觉吗？\n唔……这么说的话，我之前是不是对你们太严厉了一点？抱歉，我会稍微反省一下的。稍微。\n不过，我说这些可不是为了告诉大家，以后要尽量避开黑障。\n唉，我当然知道。他就是专门用来克制我和姐姐的存在。只要他站在那里，我们最擅长的东西就会被压制，最有把握的节奏也会被打乱。\n但那绝不是我们逃避他的理由。\n如果连身为最强的我们都选择退让，那还有谁能挡在黑曜石面前？\n所以，下一次不会一样了。\n姐姐会替我撕开他的防线，为我创造出那一击的机会，而只需要那一瞬间……我就能解决掉这个讨厌的家伙。」——逆止小队会议记录"}, {"title": "嘈杂的坟墓", "text": "「我能听见他。\n你们听不见，所以才觉得他安静，可在我耳中，他身上全是声音。\n很多很多人的声音，挤在那副黑色装甲里，像被困在某个瞬间，谁都没能真正死去，也谁都没能真正活下来。\n愤怒、恐惧、后悔，还有一些已经碎掉的名字。\n而黑障，既是它们所代表的集合，也是压住它们的那一个。\n他讨厌岚物质……但或许并不是讨厌它本身，而是讨厌由岚物质所诞生的一切，那些人类所创造的一切，而其中最为讨厌的……是他自己……\n他像是一座还在行走的坟墓。\n一座有着意志，要将一切不应存于世之物，拉入自身的坟墓。」——曜的谈话记录"}], "cn": true}, "10103146": {"profile": [{"label": "Affiliation", "value": "Obsidian Group"}, {"label": "Blood Type", "value": "A"}, {"label": "Height", "value": "160cm"}, {"label": "Memory Residual Rate", "value": "2%"}, {"label": "Progress of Renovation", "value": "▇▇"}, {"label": "Training Program", "value": "Diary"}], "introduction": "\"After the Disconnect Surgery and continued diary-keeping, Camilla's memory has improved, enabling her to recall events from the past five days. We can gradually reduce her daily MM44 dosage while continuing to monitor her closely. Our main priority is to stabilize her basic self-care skills and maintain her progress.\nTherefore, we will postpone the plan to enhance her combat endurance and concentrate on further developing her skills based on the Rebirth Experiment.\" —An Anonymous Report", "stories": [{"title": "What is Perfection?", "text": "\"Perfection is subjective, defined by perception. Today's focus is on the crucial process of obtaining subjects.\nThe conventional sourcing of subjects often results in variable quality, requiring time-consuming filtering to find suitable candidates without ensuring high-quality outcomes, leading to wasted time and research resources.\nThe Rebirth Experiment offers a solution, using an agent infused with α matter to eliminate unstable factors and create flawless \"masterpieces.\"\nOf course, we've gotten over that hump and managed to boost our success rate by an impressive 50%.\" — Rebirth Experiment Presentation Materials", "comment": {"by": "Lucia", "text": "This short statement convinced Managing Director Raphael—thus, the Predators were born."}}, {"title": "Her Life", "text": "\"June 21st.\nSubject No. 14's absorption of the newly developed Arashi agent has been completed, with no noticeable rejection reactions, no autophagy, and normal bodily functions. (Note: This individual may have a high tolerance for α matter.)\nWe have begun to \"redraw\" her memories without direct human contact, and she is learning the language very quickly—she will soon move on to the next phase. (I'll follow up on this experiment, so please don't let those idiots bother me.)\n...The experiment will proceed in seven phases, like the seven days of divine creation. I have often wondered if, perhaps, in the distant past, God was doing the exact same thing I am now...\" — Subject No. 14 Observation Report, Part One"}, {"title": "Last Moment", "text": "\"November 13th.\nNo. 14's body is saturated with α matter, but her upper limit has surpassed that of the prior prime subject, and the experiment will be transitioning into its final phase. Before proceeding to the final phase, I need to put her into the \"Hunting Ground,\" allowing her to spend time with the inferior subjects to develop some necessary social skills or camouflage for any collaboration or infiltration missions that may exist in the future.\nWhile this may introduce variables into the experiment, it doesn't worry me. In the final phase of the Disconnect Surgery, I will fine-tune this memory of hers—these imperfections will be erased, and everything will return to the path I have envisioned.\" — Report on the Transfer of Subject No. 14"}, {"title": "New Beginning", "text": "\"Camilla Cursed has completed all tests and regulatory training, although she failed several times in social assessments, which indirectly verifies her ability to be higher than that of ordinary people. Now, I propose that instead of continuing to use her as a failed experimental sample for meaningless research, she should be included in the Obsidian Mobile Guard for missions.\nThe Rebirth Experiment should not be mentioned again, and her designation as Subject No. 14 should be left in the past. From now on, she will remain under my custodianship and will directly obey my orders. I will also be responsible for all related affairs.\" — Transfer Application Letter"}]}, "10103126": {"profile": [{"label": "Affiliation", "value": "Vesper"}, {"label": "Blood Type", "value": "O"}, {"label": "Height", "value": "177cm"}, {"label": "Published Works", "value": "Warzone Travel Guide: Battlefields to Beauty Spots"}], "introduction": "\"During a journey, I was commissioned to help some villagers get rid of some nearby bandits. As I left, I advised them on what to do if we encountered the enemy: push them back with perseverance and fighting spirit, just like the laborers in the Milkhaman War—it's the only way the weak can overcome the strong. They promised me they'd follow my advice. But when I returned a few days later, all that remained of the village was scorched earth. The few survivors told me that when the bandits came back, the villagers had not fought, instead hoping to make a deal. Clearly, this approach did not quell the bandits' bloodlust, and the villagers paid a heavy price for their naivety. What did I learn from this incident? Simply this: half-hearted resistance is not resistance at all. It brings neither understanding nor concessions, only death.\" —Warzone Travel Guide: Battlefields to Beauty Spots\"", "stories": [{"title": "Vast World", "text": "With the signing of an agreement, the war finally came to an end. \nThe future might still be uncertain, but for now, most people have seen their hopes realized. Those who had been displaced or victimized were, for the first time, granted a nominally-autonomous region—a home, place where families can grow, the environment can be restored, and commerce can resume. Life remains difficult, yet they pour their energy into reconstruction, creating a place they can call their own. By turning their tears into sweat, they can recover, and they know this better than anyone. \nStill, there are some who cannot settle into this new chapter. It's not that they oppose the new peace, but even without the need to defend their freedom with weapons, the fire in their heart burns strong. Thus these warrior spirits left the island, their home, and headed out into the wider world to seek a new cause. \n\nBefore the eyes of the gathered crowd, a fierce, passionate, brown-haired girl stepped aboard the ship. As the ship departed, she turned, waved to her comrades, and promised that, one day, she would return.", "comment": {"by": "Arthur", "text": "Cassha said her temper in the past was as short as mine... It's hard to imagine..."}}, {"title": "Footprints", "text": "\"Mysterious Woman Foils Robbery at Local Market: Witnesses Describe Her Amazing Skills\"\n\"Tourist Turns Angel: Female Tourist Rescues Orphans in Flood, Leaves Behind a Muddy Teddy Bear\"\n\"Warrior from the South? Non-Local Joins Local Resistance\"\n\"Chaotic Outsider: Foreign Woman Entangled in Political Turmoil, Officials Call Her 'Uninvited'\"\n\"Nighttime Shadow Hero: She Appears and Disappears, Leaving Only Clues to Solving Problems\"\n............\nIt had been a wonderful journey, and Cassha didn't want it to end. One night on her travels, she leaned against her ST, gazing out over the drifting smoke. Foreign faces sang and danced in celebration of freedom and rebirth, while beneath them lay countless unmarked graves... Time and again along the road, she relived that war of years past, bringing victory to the oppressed in one fierce encounter after another. Yet for some reason, the more she saw, the more that island revisited her dreams. Along with the growing pull to return home came an unease, a feeling that kept her awake at night. She made up her mind. She would go back. And that unease... would soon become a reality.", "comment": {"by": "Rebecca", "text": "\"I will not fail, simply because I am justice, and justice... is the side that never fails!\" I heard she once said this line in a report... How should I put this...? It's kinda embarrassing, even for me."}}, {"title": "Stranger", "text": "\"Is this New District One?\" In Sankara's diplomatic reception hall, a brown-haired woman posed the question. Her demeanor was composed and steady, not at all like a Milkhaman, yet her turns of phrase carried a distinct local flavor. After several rounds of confirmation and searches, the receptionist finally unearthed the origin of this \"New District One\" buried in a thick pile of documents. It was the old name of Sankara, a mining town built for laborers—a name forgotten to most.Like the town itself, the woman spent several days moving through Sankara, searching for those who had once waved her farewell. Time had altered everything. Those who once starved had built homes of their own, only for those homes to be reduced to rubble when new conflicts erupted. Settlements were built upon the ruins of old settlements, only to be reduced to ruins themselves.Yet the cycle continued. Is \"victory\" merely an illusion? Was this \"change\"?Feeling the rumbling of the forces returning to the border, a faint answer was already stirring in her heart."}, {"title": "Far from Done", "text": "\"It was a reconciliation worth remembering, a marvel in its own right.. It felt as though fate had drawn them together... Of course, beyond them, many compatriots could not grasp our decisions, could not fathom the burdens we carried. Yet that was irrelevant. So long as someone stands, so long as someone is willing to lay down their life for all, hope persists. Our future may be broken, our blood may stain this land... But if we can grant even a fleeting moment of peace to others, if the world beyond can hear the faintest echo of our voice, then we have succeeded. We will be the last sacrifices on this land, the final stars before the dawn of a new day... Cassha Lumiere said so.\" —Vesper Soldier Memory"}]}, "10103109": {"profile": [{"label": "Affiliation", "value": "Obsidian Group"}, {"label": "Blood Type", "value": "A"}, {"label": "Height", "value": "172cm"}, {"label": "Progress of Renovation", "value": "▇▇"}], "introduction": "\"Catherine ignored me again, smashed the base... keeps pushing mods past limits. Not personality, pure crazy. Maybe that's what the lab rats want,  weaponized madness. Efficient use of resources?\" —Lucia's Report", "stories": [{"title": "Red and Black", "text": "Catherine of Obsidian, captain of the Predators, is a twisted, complex, and enigmatic figure. In the eyes of most Predators and the Obsidian Group, she is a straightforward, reckless, but pure battle fanatic. However, in the eyes of her enemies, she is a terrifying monster who loves to play with her prey. Countless mysteries surround her, including her origins, her past, her strange and chaotic powers—but all the answers are carefully guarded by a high-ranking member of Obsidian.", "comment": {"by": "Anonymous User", "text": "I know who's pulling the strings... I hope someone wakes up and realizes the situation before you completely ruin the legacy your ancestors left you... Don't say we didn't warn you."}}, {"title": "Yellowed White", "text": "A quick look into Catherine's history reveals that this pilot, with no mercenary background, seemingly rose to become captain of the Predators overnight. In truth, the squad was formed as an experimental mercenary unit specifically for Catherine, with most of its members being unknown subjects of various experiments. According to unverified reports from Obsidian, Catherine herself intentionally erased all traces of her life as a \"mere human\" and only began her documented history from the point she underwent her physical modifications."}, {"title": "Fresh Red", "text": "After forming the Predators, Catherine voluntarily applied for multiple enhancement modifications. Catherine was the first participant in every Obsidian experiment. Perhaps due to the influence of the enhancement experiments, Catherine became increasingly obsessed with more extreme combat methods. The external manifestation of this change was the continuous occurrence of more reckless, crazier, and more brutal combat behavior, which also led to a constantly increasing casualty rate among her squad members and STs. The infamous name of the Predators quickly became synonymous with terror across all of Milkhama.", "comment": {"by": "Sylvie", "text": "Only a lunatic would tolerate being used for such enhancement experiments! Just look at the members of the Predators—Obsidian must have intentionally gathered them all together."}}, {"title": "Black Blade", "text": "In the end, with the addition of Hawkwood and Gideon's confidante Lucia, the Predators achieved a delicate balance. The astute Lucia was responsible for coordinating the team members. At the same time, the ruthless Hawkwood executed precise tasks, and their leader Catherine, as the sharp edge of Obsidian, was responsible for clearing all obstacles standing before them. With Catherine's desire finally fulfilled, how will she now torment those remaining disobedient enemies?"}]}, "10103162": {"profile": [{"label": "Affiliation", "value": "Dawnstar League"}, {"label": "Blood Type", "value": "O"}, {"label": "Height", "value": "182cm"}, {"label": "Physical Status", "value": "Left Eye Blind"}, {"label": "Likes", "value": "Collecting Fine Wine"}, {"label": "Known Conditions", "value": "Alcohol Allergy"}], "introduction": "\"Colin Doyle, former Milkhama landing forces ace pilot, commander of the Special Operations Team directly under the Dawnstar League Armored Forces General Staff. During the war, he operated extensively in West Milkhama, conducting behind-enemy-lines missions that caused significant disruption to the UNCS. After returning to the front, he personally led his forces in multiple key engagements, including the Battle of Milthus... The old fox truly is what he claims—a 'war hero.' But believe me, he's not someone you want to deal with.\nMost people have an inner anchor—something that defines who they are and guides their actions. Find that anchor, and you find a way to handle them. He's different. Yesterday, he'd take a bullet for a comrade. Today, he could send that same person to trial. Tomorrow, he might present evidence to overturn the verdict. Even after four years working with him, I still can't tell what his anchor is... or if he has one at all. Any interaction with him is inherently unequal. Of course, if you're not his enemy—or if you don't mind your secrets being completely transparent—then just follow his orders. That's the only way to ensure the mission gets done.\" —Statement by a Colonel Staff Officer of the Armed Forces", "stories": [{"title": "Emerging Edge", "text": "\"That kid Colin is here again. Seems this time he fell asleep during sniper training and left his radio on... Broadcast his own snoring to HQ for a good half hour... Honestly, I'm somewhat impressed by him. He's been penalized four times in two months. If it were anyone else, they'd have been kicked to the curb long ago. But this kid's training results... the officers turn a blind eye. But he can't just get off scot-free; his reward for last week's tactical exercise was revoked, and I've got him doing grunt work for a week. Just as well, the military recently brought in some new gadgets modified from bipedal construction rigs... \"STs\" I think those Milkhama folks call them. I didn't think I'd have anyone to test them for me.\nTo be honest, I thought Colin would just slack off, but you should've seen his eyes light up when he saw those things. He kept pestering me about them—first time I've seen him really enthusiastic about something. Turns out that when this kid encounters something he's into, he's like a whole other person. He finished a full day's basic testing in just three hours. Before this, the largest machinery he had operated was a troop transport.\nIf the military's plan for large-scale ST deployment goes ahead, Colin's gonna turn some heads, believe you me. Provided he doesn't step on too many toes, that is...\" — Maintenance Squad Leader's Log"}, {"title": "Elite Espionage", "text": "\"Yes, I fought in Captain Colin's team for nearly a year. We infiltrated West Milkhama to collect intel and faced off against the NDF's STs together... I may sound proud of it all now, but to be honest, at first I didn't trust him one bit. We were both in our twenties, but he was a soldier trained to operate STs, while I was a professionally trained agent from the intelligence bureau. Why should he lead me?\nBut that attitude didn't last long. As the battles intensified, our situation behind enemy lines became increasingly dangerous. The pressure of being suspected, arrested, or even killed almost crushed me, yet he continued to eat, sleep, and mingle with famous figures from both sides, perfectly playing the character of a carefree merchant in the NDF's territory. It was thanks to him we survived the most danger period. We even uncovered the NDF's plan to bypass the Mouty Mountains Region for a surprise attack, preventing disaster and earning us the title of heroes among the few who knew... To me, it was the pinnacle of my career—for him it was just a prologue.\nJust as our infiltration mission was about to end and we were preparing to retreat to East Milkhama, we ended up with William on our tails—yes, that William, William Stein, ace pilot of the NDF. I thought I was done for, but Colin managed to drive him off with a series of improvised traps and a stolen ST. It was then that I realized what being an elite soldier really means.\" — A DL intelligence officer recounts post-war"}, {"title": "Nova Project", "text": "\"The hero Colin did not accept Officer Tiphys's invitation, giving up the opportunity to become a DLAF commander. It's not that surprising—after all, having skill at commanding doesn't mean you necessarily want to stay on the battlefield. I've heard him complain more than once to those around him about the burdens of being an ace pilot. To him, getting time to put his feet up takes priority... It seems silly, but that's how he really seems to feel. This is why I'm shocked by what's happened to him—I never would've guessed he'd join the Oceanic Conclave Executor force, exercising all that authority on behalf of those big shots, even fully taking over that highly confidential 'Nova Project'... Has his mindset really undergone such a profound change, or did I misjudge him from the start?\nIn any case, after taking office, he significantly revised the original plan of the Oceanic Conclave, rearranged the team, and persistently pulled a large amount of resources from the logistics and R&D departments. He clearly had his own vision. As far as I know, he indeed accomplished what may be the greatest achievement in East Milkhama—you guessed it, that \"Super Pilot,\" cultivated by that very Nova Project.\nHaving accomplished such a great feat, Colin was quickly transferred to the homeland. I guess he's doing very well for himself... Well, it's hard to say, because as outstanding as his abilities are, he has an equal talent for getting on people's nerves.\"—Communication Log of a retired DLAF Officer"}, {"title": "Executor", "text": "\"Colin Doyle, effective immediately, you are granted special freedom of action to return to Milkhama and execute this critical mission. You have three objectives: first, receive the Nova Project subject research result A-00 and subdue Ada Diaz; second, directly oversee DL political affairs and thoroughly investigate the connection between Governor Lukmund and the current chaos; third, suppress the UNCS's political expansionism and take control the situation in East Milkhama.\"\n\"Straight to the point as always... Understood, I'll depart tomorrow.\"\n\"If there's anything you need, say it now. This is a long-term mission, and we will continue to provide assistance.\"\n\"Hmm... Oh right, include Zoey as well, I'll take her to see the world.\"\n\"Zoey Steele? Are you sure she won't get in the way of your mission?\"\n\"Don't worry, she won't. I trained her personally. She's different from those guys on the island—she's got sharp instincts... Though, just for insurance, I want advance clearance to call in some DLAF heavy hitters.\"\n\"We aren't looking for a shooting war, Colin.\"\n\"Naturally, but being ready for one wouldn't hurt... After all, for all we know, the whole of Milkhama may be looking to pick a fight with us.\"\n—Oceanic Conclave Critical meeting Record fragment"}]}, "10103184": {"profile": [{"label": "Affiliation", "value": "Donau Corporation"}, {"label": "Blood Type", "value": "Unknown"}, {"label": "Height", "value": "169cm"}], "introduction": "珂赛特·塞西尔，来自异世界的机兵驾驶员，多瑙河公司的核心成员之一。她年纪虽轻但训练有素，战斗能力出众，深受马德兰的信赖。\n她曾是霞之鸟再临事件的幸存者，邂逅马德兰后与之相依为命。马德兰曾试图让她回归正常人的生活，但是因为朋友贝娜妮被卷入赐克·斯缇的袭击，珂赛特最终还是走上了佣兵之路——她在严苛的训练中磨砺成刃，再未回头。\n珂赛特本性天真善良，但在不断见证世界的黑暗，尤其是失去了马德兰之后，她逼迫自己扛起重担、走上钢丝，几乎以一己之力撑住了摇摇欲坠的多瑙河公司。如今的她更加成熟、冷淡果决、不苟言笑，手段愈发狠辣，而身心也日益憔悴……现在支撑着她走下去的，是一个不寻常的目的——穷尽一切历史节点上的可能，唤回马德兰。", "stories": [{"title": "异客", "text": "「审讯结束后，我反复核实了珂赛特·塞西尔提供的所有信息。多瑙河公司、马德兰、弗雷姬塔、ND技术——这些名词在我们的情报库中完全查无对证。她说自己曾与我并肩作战，可我的记忆中根本没有她的影子。但愿她是在胡扯，如果不是，那反倒更令人不安。毕竟如果她真的来自另一个世界、另一个时间，那就意味着在我们认知之外还存在着一整套我们无法预知的规则……哪怕是西塞罗博士讨要经费时都不会说出这么耸人听闻的故事。\n现在唯一能够确定的，就是她在审讯中表现出的从容绝非伪装。无论是我个人经验还是周围仪器的读数，都能排除她在说谎的可能。而一个能在所谓异世界军队的审讯下保持这种镇定的人，不是纯正的傻子，就是经历过远比这更荒谬的事。而从她的眼神来看，显然是后者。」——玛丽上尉的审讯备注"}, {"title": "往事碎片", "text": "「今天和异世界的来客喝了一杯咖啡，也从她口中听到了几段故事。大约十年前，一场刻意制造的空难夺去了她的家人，她独自流落温特朗度，在那里遇到了一个重伤漂流而来的男人『马德兰』。两个失去一切的人就此相依为命，活了下来。她没有详细描述那段日子，但每当提起『马德兰』这个名字，她的手就会不自觉地握紧。那个男人教会了她生存、战斗，以及……热爱。她那时候露出的眼神我很熟悉——那是决定把人生意义全都系于一人身上的眼神。\n后来的事她讲得很简略。一个朋友死在赐克·斯缇手里，而她亲手报了仇。再然后就是马德兰的死——她只用了『消失』二字带过，但从她的反应推断，大概是某种自我牺牲。现实留给她的，是一个濒临瓦解的佣兵组织和一堆没有答案的问题。而她选择扛了下来，硬把自己撑成顶梁柱，在强敌环伺的环境里维系组织、挖掘真相、对抗敌人。这时候的她显得很平静，但我明白那不是从容，而是把所有崩溃压进骨头缝里堆积出来的坚强。」——奥德莉·布吕希尔的绝密日志"}, {"title": "蓝翼之下", "text": "「奥德莉·布吕希尔说珂赛特来自另一个世界，一开始我以为这好战女人终于疯了……咳，我是说，这很难让人相信。\n出于好奇，我在和珂赛特初次打招呼前，偷偷接入她的机体通讯模块调取了数据。结果发现，那个机兵和米赫玛岛上的任何型号全都对不上号，就连材料都不是钢岚合金，那个引擎更是完全看不懂原理。这让『异世界』的说法变得可信了一些。\n在接触一段时间后，我开始对珂赛特这个人有了一定的认知。首先，这姑娘绝不像表面看起来那么好说话。尤其是她驾驶那部蓝色魔鸟的时候，简直变了一个人，冷静得可怕，每一个战术都直接而高效。米赫玛岛向来不缺优秀的佣兵，但像她这样年轻却又经验丰富的还真不多见。除此之外，最让我印象深刻的还数法兰河边的那次行动——她明明追赐克追得那么急，却还是在第一时间让我通知下游居民撤离，这足以证明她有着善良的本性。」——奈奥米·罗曼诺夫的任务日志"}, {"title": "未来答卷", "text": "「珂赛特·塞西尔……我必须承认，你比我最初想象的要更有价值。我曾以为你只是管义文先生的拙劣模仿者，一个为了拯救他而甘愿弄脏双手的可怜女孩。但你身上却又有着有趣的矛盾——你足够心狠，可以毫不犹豫地将枪口对准任何人，却又在关键的地方保留了人性。两份私心自相矛盾，将你困在轮回里，永远无法如愿改变命运，这似乎让你沦为了一个失败者……但也正因此，你才能收获管先生的信任，成为英雄故事的一员，甚至超出我的计划而拿到那把钥匙……\n我开始期待了，在我已经无法亲眼见证的某个未来，你、管先生还有其他所有人，究竟会给出一份怎样的答卷？」——ND装置残留通讯记录"}], "cn": true}, "10103102": {"profile": [{"label": "Affiliation", "value": "GKD"}, {"label": "Blood Type", "value": "A"}, {"label": "Height", "value": "168cm"}, {"label": "Graduation Results", "value": "Second place"}], "introduction": "Dana Yano - Enfield ace. Perfect grades, five-year sniper record holder. Eastern blood, cool head, sharp mind. Long-range specialist and a solid teammate.", "stories": [{"title": "Heavy Burden", "text": "I'm not sure when it started, but I've grown used to people expecting so much from me—Dana, you have to be number one, Dana, you need to stand out, Dana, there's no other choice... Dana, Dana, Dana... I try to live up to their expectations, becoming the \"Dana\" they want, the one who never lets them down, but I still don't know who the real Dana is supposed to be."}, {"title": "Elusive Fairness", "text": "When my request for a review of my grades was rejected, and I caught the frustrated gaze of Instructor Mary, I realized that there was never absolute fairness in the military academy. \"Dana, face the reality. The cost of fairness is not something we can afford now,\" said my sniper instructor, who usually looked out for me. \"Then what can I do to one day afford this so-called fairness?\" I asked back. \"You need to become stronger, even stronger than you are now. When you make a name for yourself in the NDF, fairness will naturally come your way,\" she replied.", "comment": {"by": "Military Academy Graduate", "text": "Dana Yano, now that's a name all military academy students knew back in the day! As for that Bluecher guy... what was his first name again?"}}, {"title": "Rigorous Plan", "text": "Joining the NDF is a crucial first step in my mercenary career. Iconic figures like William Stein and Rosa Diaz motivate me to build my own legacy. I have to stay sharp at all times. Kaidan Newman will be with me on this mission, and I expect his seriousness and attention to detail to meet my standards. I won't let anyone mess with my record.", "comment": {"by": "Grant", "text": "Serious and meticulous? Kaidan? Hahaha! How did this little girl manage to choose two exact opposites?!"}}, {"title": "GKD Departure", "text": "We've been in action for over half a year now as the \"GKD Parcel Service.\" This kind of life is full of unknowns and dangers I never saw coming. Sometimes, in the quiet of the night, I recall the past, but before I can even lament my naivety and weakness, exhaustion knocks me down and I fall into a dreamless sleep. \"Dana Yano, in the days to come, you must live like a cheetah, agile and free,\" I tell myself."}]}, "10103130": {"profile": [{"label": "Affiliation", "value": "Dawnstar League"}, {"label": "Blood Type", "value": "B"}, {"label": "Height", "value": "181cm"}, {"label": "Birthday", "value": "November 11th"}, {"label": "Garland Big Eater Challenge", "value": "Three-time consecutive champion"}, {"label": "Self-Assessment", "value": "Awesome guy!!!"}], "introduction": "**OFFICIAL NOTICE OF DISCIPLINARY ACTION**\n**From: The Office of the Registrar, Garland Military Academy  \n**To: [Dean Knight]   \n**Date: [XC -----]  \n**Subject: Notice of Disciplinary Action\n**Dear [Dean Knight],\nThis letter serves both as an acknowledgment of your recent actions during the simulated combat exercise and the consequent disciplinary measures.\nWe've noted your involvement in an unauthorized operation that you described as a \"direct strike on the enemy's command center.\" While your tactical skill is admirable, this action resulted in a major breach of discipline and protocol, significantly disrupting the Academy's exercise both in structure and spirit.\nThe Garland Military Academy values the unique talents of its cadets, including your innovative spirit and leadership skills, which, when directed correctly, will benefit both the academy and the wider defense community.\nIt's crucial to remember that obedience, respect for hierarchy, and protocol adherence are also key qualities for an officer. Balancing innovation with compliance is vital.\nConsidering the above observations and your notable contributions to the Academy, especially your culinary achievements highlighted by your wins in the Campus Big Eater Challenge, a disciplinary action designed to encourage productive reflection has been decided:\n**Effective immediately, you are assigned to oversee the sanitary maintenance of the school's cafeteria for a period of three months. This assignment not only leans into an environment you find enjoyable but also serves as a potent reminder of the importance of order, discipline, and service.\nMay this period of reflection enhance your commendable talents with the wisdom to navigate the demands and responsibilities of leadership.\n**Sincerely,\n[---- -----]  \nRegistrar  \nGarland Military Academy", "stories": [{"title": "New Generation", "text": "In the eyes of the DL, XC 101 on Milkhama Island was their era.\nThe UNCS surrendered its advantage and stolen land, signing a peace treaty and retreating to West Milkhama. For once, the island knew peace, with the Dawnstar League symbolizing hope over East Milkhama.\nThe achievements of the DLAF were widely recognized in East Milkhama through various channels, including television and schools, emphasizing the importance of truth over falsehood. The critical takeaway for East Milkhama from the war was the eventual victory of justice over aggression, symbolizing the enduring resilience of the DL.\nRegarding problem-solving, war is not an unacceptable option, and people believe this.\n\"I, Dean Knight, now swear that no matter what happens, I will be loyal to the Dawnstar League and its people, and serve to uphold justice!\" Years later, at only thirteen, Dean uttered this pledge during his interview at Garland Military Academy and has remained true to his word ever since."}, {"title": "Cafeteria Legend", "text": "The Garland Military Academy's cafeteria is buzzing with the legend of an undefeated champion. Since his arrival, he has dominated eating competitions, leaving food vendors astonished. Even the most challenging fast food contests have been abandoned due to his unmatched appetite. With each new feat, his legend grows, sparking intrigue and amazement. Will this be the beginning of a new era in competitive eating?\nLuckily, the legend lives on, and we're delighted to welcome the cafeteria's shining star—Dean Knight! Please share with the audience what food means to you.\n\"Of course, eating is the most important thing there is! No food, no energy—you're gonna have a bad time! That's why every meal's a battle. You show up hungry, and you show up ready to win!\" — DL Food Channel", "comment": {"by": "Erisa", "text": "News about big eaters is always full of hyperbole, but if they're talking about Dean... I guess it doesn't seem too far off."}}, {"title": "Jadeite", "text": "\"When evaluating Dean's performance, we couldn't help but feel a complex mix of emotions. His battle intuition and strategic deployment abilities have brought unexpected victories in multiple actions, and his unique insights and innovative thinking in terms of battlefield strategy are admirable. However, his behavioral patterns often cause concern, especially his preference for high-risk strategy, which, although creative, inevitably puts individuals and squads in potential danger. This trait demonstrates both his bravery and confidence, as well as a certain lack of risk management.\nAs his mentors, we strive to provide necessary guidance and advice while respecting his personality and talents, aiming to promote his comprehensive abilities, especially in teamwork and risk assessment. However, guiding him toward a more balanced and stable development path without weakening his innovative spirit and battlefield intuition is a challenging task.\" — Comprehensive End-of-Term Evaluation from Garland Military Academy", "comment": {"by": "Kelly", "text": "So now I'm stuck cleaning up the mess those instructors left behind... What a pain."}}, {"title": "Knives Out", "text": "\"Notice\nDuring the Special Trial Unit's selection process, unregistered participant Dean Knight commandeered a training ST, bypassing security to compete. Showcasing remarkable talent, he outperformed many seasoned contenders.\nMr. Knight's actions, while demonstrating courage and skill, breached the selection's regulations, which require all participants to register beforehand to ensure fairness. Not yet a graduate of Garland Military Academy, he failed to meet the competition's eligibility criteria, thus unfairly disadvantaging officially registered competitors.\nGiven the above situation, although we fully recognize and respect Mr. Knight's talents and potential, as demonstrated in the selection event, we regret to announce that Mr. Knight's qualification for victory will be officially annulled according to the selection rules and procedures. We now await a decision on further punishment from the temporary jury formed by Council Member Lukmund.\" — DL Military Selection Committee", "comment": {"by": "Shawnee", "text": "According to eyewitnesses, Lukmund calmly tore the notice draft into pieces and announced on the spot the legality of Dean's promotion to the Special Trial Unit. He rarely makes such forceful decisions, but Dean's subsequent performance proved him right."}}]}, "10103121": {"profile": [{"label": "Affiliation", "value": "DLAF"}, {"label": "Blood Type", "value": "O"}, {"label": "Height", "value": "182cm"}, {"label": "Extra Medal", "value": "DLAF Arm Wrestling Champion"}], "introduction": "\"It's all true, every word! I watched Davies leap from her ST, tear my cockpit open barehanded, and yank me clear! Then, hostiles showed up in STs while we were on foot. I thought I was dead until Davies roared, charged them, grabbed an ST in each hand, and crushed them together...\" —DLAF Defense Corps Show Transcript", "stories": [{"title": "Weightlifting Champion", "text": "When the Milkhama War broke out, Diracca Davies, the DL weightlifting champion, was on a flight to Milkhama for the world championship in Milthus. But when the plane made an emergency landing in East Milkhama and the sky ahead erupted in flames, Diracca sensed that her fate had just taken a turn—one that would change everything.", "comment": {"by": "Grant", "text": "Diracca Davies! The Lightweight World Champion of the 72nd Weightlifting Championships! I remember buying her signed poster when I was still in boot camp!"}}, {"title": "Militia Captain", "text": "Due to the sudden outbreak of war, all Milkhama came to a standstill, and chaos ensued. Daily life fell into disorder, and everyone scrambled to escape the island. Diracca, once a renowned athlete with a glamorous reputation, found herself powerless. Like so many others stuck in the war zone, she was forced into a cramped, damp air-raid shelter, enduring each day with an uncertain fear of the future. On the seventh day, a military officer from the Dawnstar League entered the shelter and announced the government's call for recruits to form a militia unit."}, {"title": "New DLAF Star", "text": "From then on, Diracca's destiny took a turn. She joined the DLAF militia as a conscripted soldier. She was soon recruited into the regular forces due to her outstanding physical abilities and exceptional combat potential as an ST pilot. Diracca, a former athlete, was promoted to Squad Captain for her excellent leadership skills in the border war. Later, in the operation against the NDF's mobile units, she successfully captured an experimental ST, bringing back a valuable prototype sample for the DLAF", "comment": {"by": "Naomi", "text": "The DL and the UNCS belong to two entirely different schools when it comes to applying Arashium alloy. Since the DL has already obtained a prototype, why has the feasibility of sensor research yet to be considered?"}}, {"title": "Legendary Warrior", "text": "After the war, Diracca was promoted to DLAF Lieutenant and continued to serve as a military officer of the Defense Forces in the East Milkhama region, stationed at the border. Whenever she recalls receiving her opportunity to join the DLAF, she marvels at the wonders of fate. Of course, even though Diracca is no longer a weightlifter, she hasn't given up on the sport she once loved so deeply. They say she occasionally holds weightlifting competitions at camp. Unfortunately, the worthy opponent she has been looking forward to competing with has yet to appear."}]}, "10103113": {"profile": [{"label": "Affiliation", "value": "Obsidian Group"}, {"label": "Blood Type", "value": "AB"}, {"label": "Height", "value": "171cm"}, {"label": "Obsidian Intranet Access", "value": "▇▇"}], "introduction": "Obsidian's youngest board member. ST ace and surveillance expert. They say she can open any door and see any message. Rumors say she's hunting the CEO for breaking company law.", "stories": [{"title": "Inspector", "text": "Obsidian was the first company to discover α matter and also the first to master Arashium technology. I am fortunate to have grown under the company's patronage, and have been entrusted with the position of supervisor. I will repay the board's trust with my loyalty and knowledge... And so, regarding those traitors who would steal the company's technological secrets and go off to create their own little empires, neither I nor the rest of the board will show them an ounce of mercy.", "comment": {"by": "Grant", "text": "This weirdo was the supervisor of Obsidian's board of directors? What kind of tricks did she have to pull to get into that hellish company's upper echelons?"}}, {"title": "Eye of the Board", "text": "I know there are rumors circulating within the company, some bored little flies questioning my abilities. They believe my position on the board is the result of some \"special means\"... I won't waste my time responding to their shallow, vile speculations, because I never waste time on idiotic fools. My focus must always be on those with more malicious intent. The enemies of the company are much more intelligent than these insects."}, {"title": "From Gideon", "text": "I've seen those insane test subjects. Well done, Mr. Gideon... I know he holds some inexplicable grievances against the board of directors and Chairman Obelisk, always thinking that if he controls more power, the company will bend to his will. To me, that shows nothing but ignorance of the board's meticulous strategy—pure childishness. The chairman would never want someone like that to be his successor, and Gideon can't rely on a bunch of lunatics to win inheritance... even if he is the founder's grandson.", "comment": {"by": "Naomi", "text": "The two founders of Obsidian are Alexander Obelisk and Francis Gideon. The current CEO, Raphael Gideon, is Francis's grandson."}}, {"title": "The Real Mastermind", "text": "Chairman Obelisk still wants me to go and deal with those fools causing trouble on Milkhama, even though I've informed the board that my departure will compromise information security within the company. However, due to the importance of headquarters' development plans and the overall situation on and off the island, I must prevent certain company members from colluding with the UNCS. I hope a certain self-proclaimed \"manager\" can understand his position. I will not be as merciful as Mr. Obelisk."}]}, "10103136": {"profile": [{"label": "Affiliation", "value": "Doll Offshore Group"}, {"label": "Blood Type", "value": "B"}, {"label": "Height", "value": "168cm"}, {"label": "Nickname", "value": "Hurricane, Ubiquitous Rain, and That Damn Gossip Squad—They'll All Pay!"}, {"label": "Published Work", "value": "The Life and Lies of Milkhama"}, {"label": "Favorite Books", "value": "From Heiress to Helldriver: The Fall of a Noble House"}], "introduction": "Erisa Shinohara, an escaped Hyper-Aptamer during the NDF turmoil, is known as \"Ubiquitous Rain\" in various media and military networks. Her news reports consistently carry astonishing and thought-provoking content, often likened to an unforeseen needle piercing some individuals' most guarded secrets. While her whereabouts remain mysterious, adorned with equipment and a reassuring smile, her appearance invariably signals the imminent arrival of groundbreaking revelations.", "stories": [{"title": "Ubiquitous", "text": "\"Sir, I'm concerned that the discussion surrounding 'Ubiquitous Rain' wasn't quite thorough enough. This oversight could come to bite us. Her recent disclosures have triggered a wave of public backlash; many senior UNCS officials have come under fire. Although the DL may welcome such developments, we must not underestimate the risks inherent in this kind of journalism, free from institutional oversight. Based on our previous contact with this 'Ubiquitous Rain,' she seems to dive into danger headfirst, like a moth to flame... The latest intelligence shows that her activity area has spread right to the heart of the DL. Sir, it may be time to take action.\" — DL News Agency Editorial Board Minutes"}, {"title": "Rainy", "text": "\"Judging from the movements of 'Ubiquitous Rain,' she seems interested in military activities. We have spotted her at three bombing sites, but each time she managed to slip away. To ensure we wouldn't miss her again, we requested police support. We setup ambushes at several key locations determined by her psychological and behavioral profile. Finally, we were able to detain the target. However, when confronted by the interrogator, her attitude was... intriguing. She showed no surprise at her arrest and was very frank in answering our questions. She even volunteered details we didn't ask for. She casually asked for you, Chief Editor, and even invited our team out for tea... *cough* Our experts concluded that she was telling the truth, though it's difficult to comprehend. Also, as you know, she somehow managed to steal a police ST, and now she's on the wanted list. I'm sure she'll be caught soon... Well, maybe...\" — Communication Record on DL News Agency Editor-in-Chief's Terminal", "comment": {"by": "Erisa", "text": "What? Arrested?! Isn't this supposed to be an \"official prison visit\" organized by the DL for the press? Who the hell's updating my Skynet info?"}}, {"title": "Wind Roar", "text": "\"5th Adaptive Experiment, Subject No. 13 performed exceptionally well and may soon be able to advance to the next phase. No. 13 has also expressed a willingness to communicate. This is the first time she has taken the initiative to communicate since being 'recruited' into the lab. We had a simple conversation, and I was eager to know her sensory feedback after being modified. However, her language system has been damaged, making it difficult for her to express herself adequately. She was interested in my nameplate and work manual, but I couldn't show her any confidential content. I resorted to giving her my name. Her expression became softer than ever before, and she uttered a coherent syllable. It was only later that I realized that this might be her name. She clumsily wrote a series of crooked characters in the palm of my hand with my pen, with not much skill at all. I have decided that from today onwards, I might customize a language course for her so that she might at least be comfortable during this frustratingly endless life of experimentation.\" — Excerpt from Subject No. 13 Observation Report", "comment": {"by": "Grant", "text": "Girls... ST... experiment... Why do these words feel so familiar when I put them together? Could they be related to Sylvie and the other girls too?"}}, {"title": "Spring Green", "text": "\"In my hometown, people live a secluded life. They work during the day and sleep at night, and the sun and moon turn endlessly amidst the monotony. The adults in the village are like trees and flowers, while the elderly are like withered branches and fallen leaves. I'm just like a seed of grass, caught in this infinite cycle. 'What else can we do? It's not that bad,' my mother always says. She's right. There's no room for contemplation in this life, no room for sorrow either. One winter, a blind and disabled stranger came to the village. He said he used to be a soldier and had spent his days in the military. Now that he was old, he wanted to change his way of life. He liked the leisurely life in the village. I didn't understand. Life here wasn't leisurely at all. Time passed quickly, and before I knew it, I had grown up. He laughed and said I didn't know many words, so how could I understand what leisurely meant. I blushed and went home, but I couldn't help but go talk to him again the next day. As I listened to him boast, I began understanding the elusive concept of 'leisure' in the warm and cold months. As the last of the snow melted, he gazed down the mountain path and remarked that the way was now clear and easy to travel. At that moment, I felt like I was sprouting anew... Indeed, spring was coming.\" — Excerpt from The Life and Lies of Milkhama", "comment": {"by": "Sylvie", "text": "If she hadn't chosen to leave the village back then, she'd probably still be living that peaceful life... Changing your life requires great strength. The little girl who used to cry in my arms—she's grown up."}}]}, "10103137": {"profile": [{"label": "Affiliation", "value": "Doll Group"}, {"label": "Blood Type", "value": "O"}, {"label": "Height", "value": "158cm"}, {"label": "Specialty", "value": "Equestrianism, Piano, Violin, ST Operation"}, {"label": "Likes", "value": "Electronic Music, Dark Fairy Tales, and Sachertorte"}, {"label": "Published Work", "value": "From Heiress to Helldriver: The Fall of a Noble House"}], "introduction": "Fia Helstota, a Hyper-Aptamer escapee from a UNCS lab, now works as Erisa's assistant, projecting a princess-like air. She handles Erisa's challenging tasks under the guise of receiving industry training but ends up caring for Erisa's daily needs due to her refined upbringing. Despite voicing her grievances to Erisa, Fia has not received effective feedback.", "stories": [{"title": "Promised Land", "text": "\"In Ovett's distant past, there was once a place known as the Promised Land... A determined pioneer living in the frozen north stood defiant, dreaming of reshaping the land for human survival. The pioneer embarked on an arduous journey, infecting many young people with his spirit of fearlessness and hope along the way. The frozen land gradually revealed the miraculous resources he had sought, and the pioneer fulfilled his initial promise, settling down with his companions for generations to come. Their descendants continued to uphold the fearless spirit of that first generation, maintaining this land of hope.\" — Excerpt from Ovett Regional Story", "comment": {"by": "Naomi", "text": "The legendary Helstota clan of Ovett, pioneers of the frozen wastelands... I always thought it was just a kids' fairy tale, and now you're telling me there's an actual heir?"}}, {"title": "Girl", "text": "\"However, humans cannot easily alter nature's laws. In the end, all living beings remain bound to the roles of hunter and hunted. Even if humans have acquired civilization, their cruel nature is still deeply ingrained in their souls and cannot be disobeyed. The outsiders claimed they were drawn by the Promised Land, offering warm words and smiles that looked sincere. But when their eyes finally opened, the venom had already sunk in, and those outsiders clung to their prey like vipers, devouring all their accumulated achievements. The people tried their best, but all their efforts were in vain. Reality ground the last shred of pride from the pioneers' bloodline into dust. In the end, a girl—not even grown—was elected as their temporary leader, and to stand against the storm, she made her choice and signed a contract with the devil...\" — Unburnt Notebook Fragment", "comment": {"by": "Erisa", "text": "Whether it's dignity or downfall, it all falls on the shoulders of a young girl? Fate's got a hell of a sense of humor... But this is different from the Ovett storybook I grew up reading... What is this, some grimdark rewrite?"}}, {"title": "Hero", "text": "\"After all, this is not a fairy tale. The girl's stubborn will did not restore what her family had lost. After enduring seemingly endless physical and mental torment in the purgatory of her fate, she abandoned all hope of survival. She believed she no longer had a right to respond to anyone's expectations, and could only watch as her family became mere minions of the Snake, their lineage reduced to just another trophy on display. The weak cannot go against fate—a truth known well by all Ovettians. Who would extend a hand to the powerless? This is the real world, not a children's story... Perhaps only the most hopeless of fools would recklessly extend a hand to others—as she had once done...\" — Unsent Private letter", "comment": {"by": "Eileen", "text": "Trophies? For those test subjects they drag in, \"tools\" paints a truer picture of what they are... But if they survive the gauntlet—trial after trial—and claw their way to the top... they become \"art.\""}}, {"title": "Enemy", "text": "\"Later, that foolish hero and his companions went to the demon's lair together and liberated countless suffering maidens. The hero inspired the girls, returning to them their freedom and reigniting their fighting spirit. Thus, they embarked on a new journey together. But this, of course, is merely a standard fairytale ending, and nothing more.\nLife is like an Ovett nesting doll—you never know if what comes next will bring fortune or disaster. The blood in her veins constantly reminds her of her duty as a descendant of those trailblazers. And so, opportunity arises once more, fate destined to rekindle the bond that was once severed. If it meant justice for her family, then even becoming the villain was a duty she would fulfill. All for Helstota.\" — Dusty Diary of a Young Girl", "comment": {"by": "Alyson", "text": "You went so far as to write an entire story just to express what you've been through? Was it through such fantasies that you were able to endure those cruel experiments? Well, the decline of Helstota was inevitable, but only someone like me, who doesn't care about social status, would dare to continue treating you as a friend. Keep up the good work, Fia."}}]}, "10103152": {"profile": [{"label": "Affiliation", "value": "Donau Corporation"}, {"label": "Blood Type", "value": "Unknown"}, {"label": "Height", "value": "Unknown"}, {"label": "Body Modification Level", "value": "95%"}, {"label": "One-Handed Grip Strength", "value": "120kg"}], "introduction": "Fregata Oasis, an ST pilot from another world and a core member of the Donau Corporation. In the Donau Corporation, if Madland is the flag that unites everyone, then Fregata is the unyielding flagpole beneath it. \nBesides her excellent combat abilities, Fregata is also the matriarch of the team. She not only knows the team members' situations inside out but makes thoughtful arrangements tailored to each person, perfectly handling many \"internal affairs\" that even Madland finds tricky. Together they form a superb combination of \"external and internal.\" Fregata's confidence stems from her individual strength. As a modified human, Fregata possesses extraordinary reaction speeds, allowing her to quickly adapt to almost any battlefield. After arriving on Milkhama, Fregata continues her usual style—clean, decisive, and strong-willed. In the intricate web of traps laid by Zeke Steel, she seized upon the faintest clues and ultimately broke the deadlock. Her blunt, uncompromising personality leaves a deep impression on anyone who works alongside her.", "stories": [{"title": "Converging River", "text": "\"It's probably a coincidence, but Miss Fregata also has experience with the rebels. In the past, Miss Fregata was a member of the resistance group 'River of Confluence' and, like us, went through various hardships and farewells... No wonder she gets along so well with everyone in the Ashes. From combat guerrilla to ST deployment, just listening to Miss Fregata talk about her past experiences can yield a lot of valuable insights... I remember Mr. Yevgeny once said, 'For the rebels, STs, firepower, and external support are not necessities. What truly matters is knowing that you are doing the right thing'... In Miss Fregata, I can feel the weight of those words.\" —Chloe Schmidt's Account"}, {"title": "Crimson Shadow", "text": "\"...As seen in the combat records, the target, Fregata, is an exceptional pilot. No, to be precise, she has reached a level that requires close monitoring. Her reaction speed, her piloting skills... her performance generally far exceeds the standards of regular pilots, with data metrics comparable to those of test subjects. Moreover, the target's bad-tempered and impulsive behavior makes her undoubtedly a potential threat to the UNCS. Furthermore, researchers from the Technical Institute have secretly sampled the target's hair, and the test report... is quite bizarre. In the words of these researchers, 'Her body has already gone far beyond the realm of humanity.'\" —Report from a GSA Agent"}, {"title": "Her Past", "text": "\"Miss Oasis's body is indeed somewhat unique... I also noticed it inadvertently while bandaging her wounds after that battle. Unlike a normal person, Miss Oasis's skin has many seams that are impossible to ignore, and beneath the wounds is a metallic skeleton and blood vessels like circuits... After noticing my gaze, Miss Oasis had no intention of hiding anything and openly told me the secret behind it—'I didn't want to become like this either, but I had no choice When I opened my eyes, I had already been made into the living core of some weapon, and my past memories and life had been turned into a tangled mess'... I still remember the look in Miss Oasis's eyes when she spoke of the past, there was anger, bitterness, and disdain, but not a trace of regret. When I asked her the reason, she simply continued, 'We can only live in the present. Instead of reminiscing about what we've lost, it's better to think about what we still have.' I think this is probably why Miss Oasis is always so decisive in her actions. Besides moving forward, she has nothing left...\" —Celine Reynolds's Personal Diary"}, {"title": "Projected Future", "text": "\"The records left by the Zeke Steel Laboratory have been completed, which means that the research on Fregata and that ST has come to an end. To summarize this incident in one sentence, it is that dangerous technology slipped out of control, ultimately giving rise to disaster... For outsiders, it is undoubtedly a profound lesson. But for researchers, it is instead a revelation, as the potential of Arashi Matter far exceeds our current framework and its potential for development has grown considerably! The secrets of Fregata, the secrets of Shadowrabbit, they may soon be in our grasp. One day, Arashi Matter will also develop to such an extent... And at that time will it, like the ND technology mentioned by Zeke, bring entirely new possibilities to our world, to our future?\" —UNCS Researcher's Laboratory Log"}]}, "10103122": {"profile": [{"label": "Affiliation", "value": "Electric Eel Mercenaries"}, {"label": "Blood Type", "value": "AB"}, {"label": "Height", "value": "179cm"}, {"label": "Imprisoned count", "value": "Zero (Police Record)"}], "introduction": "\"Boss Frida's a damn legend here on Milkhama! I've been running with her since five, six years back, right when we changed name to Electric Eel. She cleaned house alright, got us all in line. People say Milkhama's a land of opportunity—don't get played! It's full of peril. But thanks to Boss Frida guiding us and all that, we're still here, still standing strong! We owe her, big time.\" — Garm, Electric Eel", "stories": [{"title": "Intertwined", "text": "For Frida, Milkhama Island holds a special place in her heart. She loves it for its year-round warmth, a far cry from the freezing winters the northerners always complain about. But she hates it, too. She hates how those without money are left with nowhere to turn; how the powerless are pushed to do whatever it takes to survive. Get stronger, make money, stay alive—that's the only thing that drives Frida as she fights her way through the mercenary ranks.", "comment": {"by": "Welfare Director", "text": "Frida García was expelled from the orphanage at the age of thirteen for fighting. Since then, I've heard her name pop up now and then among the police."}}, {"title": "Survival Instincts", "text": "Shaped by over a decade of ruthless experience, surviving in the mercenary world taught Frida the hard truth: if you're weaker, surrender and bide your time for an opportunity to strike back. If you're stronger, apply maximum pressure and drain every last bit of usefulness from your opponent. Armed with this brutal survival instinct, Frida thrived in a male-dominated mercenary group, earning the respect of the old leader, John Warren. By the time she was twenty, she was second-in-command. Though the old leader treated her well, living under someone else's command would never satisfy Frida."}, {"title": "Mercenary Queen", "text": "Frida finally got her chance. The unexpected death of her veteran leader triggered a power struggle among the mercenaries. She piloted her ST and led her followers through the cockpit of every rival and rebel, ultimately becoming the new leader of their motley crew and renaming it \"Electric Eel.\"", "comment": {"by": "Investigator", "text": "Even though John Warren's death by gas poisoning at his long-abandoned home was officially ruled a suicide, I can't rule out the possibility of foul play."}}, {"title": "The Path of the Electric Eel", "text": "Power represents both absolute strength and an inescapable responsibility, and the crown of leadership was far heavier than Frida had imagined. Faced with an imminent financial crisis, Frida inadvertently found herself involved with the NDF, becoming a long-term partner of Blair Bluecher. Since then, the Electric Eel has experienced unprecedented growth and expansion.", "comment": {"by": "Southern Mercenary", "text": "Recruitment ads for the Electric Eel are plastered all over almost every bar in town! I don't know about taking orders from some woman, but you can't argue with that salary...."}}]}, "10103168": {"profile": [{"label": "Affiliation", "value": "Harpy Commerce"}, {"label": "Blood Type", "value": "B"}, {"label": "Height", "value": "174cm"}, {"label": "出生地", "value": "尼德法尔斯"}, {"label": "地下斗技成绩", "value": "「地下蒸汽」三十连胜"}], "introduction": "吉赛尔·梅耶来自一个被称作「尼德法尔斯」的边远深山地区，她和她的族人原本过着与世隔绝的部落生活，直到数年前有外人意外造访，带去了文明也带去了战争。她震撼于「机兵」这钢铁巨人的强大力量，也对其仅仅是杀人兵器感到困惑，更对自己的族人沉溺于战争感到遗憾。为了寻找与新世界共存的方法，她毅然离开家乡来到米赫玛岛，亲身感受着时代的巨变。\n二十多年的尼德法尔斯部落人生赋予了吉赛尔看待世界的独特视角，她能凭直觉看见他人内心的「火」，也能感受到象征变化的「风」。凭借过人的体质和出色的学习能力，她当过八角笼里的斗士，也学会了驾驶机兵参与战斗，逐渐在米赫玛站稳脚跟，但她至今仍在寻找和战争、和新世界有关的答案……", "stories": [{"title": "尼德法尔斯", "text": "「我查过那个新人的背景了，她没说谎。\n在距离米赫玛岛六千公里远的大陆深处，确实有一片被称作『尼德法尔斯』的险峻山脉。那里曾长期与世隔绝，直到几年前因为意外发现的矿产和随之而来的战争，它才和生活在那里的原始部族一起进入世人的视野。\n后来她离开了尼德法尔斯，独自跨越无数的山脉与河流、陆地与海洋，辗转来到米赫玛……真不知道她是怎么做到的，又花了多少时间。总之，大约一个月前她成为了这座岛上的黑户，靠在『地下蒸汽』打黑拳维持生计，『吉赛尔·梅耶』这个名字也是在那时候取的，据说和她原本的名字发音很像。\n尽管目前为止还没打过几场像样的比赛，但她绝对是稀有的人才……尼德法尔斯的原始生活赋予了她出色的反应能力、柔韧度、力量感和稳定性，除了尚欠缺与人斗争的经验，她简直就是完美的角斗士。\n我已经决定把所有的注都押在她身上了。」——斗技场情报商通话记录"}, {"title": "异类", "text": "「我和吉赛尔的相识非常简单——她兴冲冲地拿着全部积蓄跑进机库的时候，我是唯一在场的机修师。说实话，当时我根本没想过会从她口中听到『想学机兵驾驶』这样的话。毕竟，她有力量，很敏捷，学东西也很快，是我这十几年来见过的最有天赋的斗士，只要在八角笼里多活跃几年，赚够下半辈子的钱也不是奢望，我不明白她有什么必要去学机兵驾驶这种烂大街的技术。话虽如此，我还是给她挑了一台机兵……毕竟我靠她的连战连胜赚了不少，可得哄好这尊财神。\n后来我才发现自己想的太简单了。她对于驾驶机兵的渴望不是一时的兴趣，而是某种深思熟虑的结果——她既不好战，对荣誉和金钱也不看重，她只是想要『理解这些钢铁巨人』。感到无比困惑的我第一次尝试和她深入交流，然后了解了关于她家乡的故事……外来者彻底改变了她曾坚信的一切。她来米赫玛，来学习机兵驾驶，只是想看清楚机兵与战争的意义，想弄明白该如何与这个互相伤害的世界共存。\n这是一个幼稚到有些滑稽的想法，但她显然是认真的，不管我冷嘲热讽了多少次，她也没打算放弃。那时候我明白了，她和我们从根本上就不是一路人……『地下蒸汽』是绝对留不住她的。」——「地下蒸汽」机修师的日记"}, {"title": "离开", "text": "「常胜将军吉赛尔终于还是输了。\n赔了钱败了兴的观众聚在『地下蒸汽』外骂骂咧咧，还和看场子的保安干起了架……起初我和他们一样惊愕，但很快就想通了——在这座岛上翻车才是常态，就算吉赛尔天赋异禀也不可能永远顺风顺水，更何况对手还是那个『野火』。我本以为吉赛尔会因此而消沉，但赛后见面时，她表现得还挺有精神的……看得出来她对胜负并不执着，这也意味着她没那么容易被束缚。果然，没过几天她就开着机兵离开了『地下蒸汽』，临走前还留下了不少钱。之前新来的机修师索妮娅也不见了踪影，她们俩关系不错，多半是提前商量过了。以这两人的本事，只要别太头铁，在米赫玛混个日子不算什么难事。\n但我怎么也没想到，吉赛尔竟然会招惹到军队……据我东边的朋友所说，她在同盟军的基地大闹了一场，最后从一整支机动部队的封锁中逃了出来，现在已经成为了半个通缉犯……我也不是没听过类似的离谱传闻，但那次的主角可是大名鼎鼎的猎豹物流。我相信吉赛尔的能力，但不觉得她能单枪匹马做到这一点，也不认为她是那种会主动惹事的人。\n她身上有着自然的活力，或者说野性，这是一种非常难得的特质，也是非常容易被米赫玛局势吞噬的弱点……唉，希望她能找到脱离深渊的方法吧。」——「地下蒸汽」常客口述"}, {"title": "向西而行", "text": "「多亏了吉赛尔，我们一家人才能活着回到肯斯顿。\n那时候我们被一伙持枪歹徒袭击，他们不仅抢走了我们随身的全部家当，还商量着把我们卖去附近的佣兵团当苦工……我本来已经做好拼个鱼死网破的准备了，一个人影忽然冲过来将歹徒一一放倒。等身上的绳索被解开，我才意识到自己被救了。\n除了感谢的话语外，她不愿意收下任何谢礼，只是说想和我们搭伙一起去西边——这让我吃了一惊，要知道我们先前可没提起过自己的目的地。我女儿心里藏不住话，开口问她，她却只是笑着说看到了我们的『火』正被一阵『风』吹着，向着西边摇曳，就和她本人一样……我至今没太明白这其中的含义，或许是她故乡『尼德法尔斯』独有的某种智慧吧。\n总之，我实在找不出什么理由去拒绝这位救命恩人。剩下的路程也不算太平，但靠着吉赛尔的提前预警，我们还是避开了危险。有一次，我们差点被卷入机兵大战，但她却没有丝毫惊慌，反而饶有兴致地观察着那些机兵的一举一动……她跟我说，希望拥有一台属于自己的机兵。恰好我在这方面有些门路，就决定帮她参谋参谋，可没想到，她竟然连机兵分轻型、中型、重型都不知道，对什么钢岚合金、世代划分更是一窍不通。我本打算推荐她去看看海运的货，现在倒是更担心她被人骗了。」——肯斯顿某商人口述"}], "cn": true}, "10103103": {"profile": [{"label": "Affiliation", "value": "GKD"}, {"label": "Blood Type", "value": "O"}, {"label": "Height", "value": "191cm"}, {"label": "Punishment Record", "value": "Alcoholism (four times)"}, {"label": "Military Machinist Competition", "value": "Cancel Qualification"}], "introduction": "\"I can't figure out how Grant got into Armored Corps! Sure, he's good with machines, but he's always boozing or heading to booze. Keeps modding our STs with weird parts... Can't trust my squad to this mess of a mechanic!\"—Captain of the 11th Armored Corps", "stories": [{"title": "Ideals and Reality", "text": "I came to Milkhama Island for the war. I was young, all pumped up thinking I'd be out there piloting STs and feeling like a badass, so I signed up to join the NDF. But it turns out I was just putting down protests from pissed-off workers, nothing like the glory I saw on TV. I started getting sick of it, so I'd mess with my ST's wiring on the side to avoid being scheduled for missions. Of course, do that enough times and you'll get noticed. I got kicked out of the army real quick. So, to keep eating in this crazy world, I opened a repair shop, and let me tell you, fixing them beats piloting them in the military any day."}, {"title": "Rainforest Machinist", "text": "About two years after the war, I set up a repair shop in Burton Bay, deep in the Northwest Rainforest. From small watches to STs, I fixed it all, and word started to spread. I even started buying and selling ST parts, and business began to pick up. But Milkhama wasn't so peaceful back then—it was rough, worse than it is now. One time, I delivered a repaired ST to a client, only for them to refuse payment and surround me! It was a hell of a ride, but in the end, I took them all down!", "comment": {"by": "Naomi", "text": "Grant, don't think I don't know you're bragging! There's no record on Skynet of this brawl you're talking about!"}}, {"title": "Military Career", "text": "Later, to handle the insurgents, the NDF expanded its forces, and I was specially recruited as a senior machinist for the Armored Corps Mobile Squad. From then on, I couldn't avoid William's constant tirades, and I racked up three—maybe four—disciplinary actions. Doesn't really matter. The point is, they never kicked me out. After all, the strain of keeping the new recruits and new STs in top shape wasn't something just anyone could manage. But the most advanced tech, the stuff hidden deep in the hangar, was always kept out of reach. I didn't think much of it at the time. Who knew that hidden behind all that gear was a chain of events that would lead to something far darker...", "comment": {"by": "Dana", "text": "It sounds like Grant was actually saved by his lazy attitude. It would have been difficult for him to extricate himself if he had been pulled into Blair's plan due to his excellent performance."}}, {"title": "Reborn from the Flames", "text": "Who would've thought I'd end up back in the Northwest Rainforest after ditching the NDF? This time, they've got their eyes on me, but honestly, it's not as bad as it sounds. No weapons pointed at laborers, I can catch a nap when I want, and I've got all the time I need to tinker with my STs... These days with the GKD Squad have probably been the happiest of my life. You know, hanging around with Kaidan and Dana, I've started to feel some of that fire I had when I was younger. Doesn't matter how messy Milkhama's schemes get, as long as we stick together, we can handle anything that comes our way. But hey, don't go telling those two I said that, alright?"}]}, "10103112": {"profile": [{"label": "Affiliation", "value": "The Epiphyllum"}, {"label": "Blood Type", "value": "A"}, {"label": "Height", "value": "175cm"}, {"label": "Physical Status", "value": "Healthy"}, {"label": "Specialty", "value": "Solo Action"}], "introduction": "\"First time I saw Gumusiay—gentle face, deadly reputation. Didn't want her at first. But she's like us, tortured past, lost loved ones. It has a different style and the same fire inside. Strong as any of us.\" —Hong and Sylvie's Chat", "stories": [{"title": "[Father]", "text": "Every time I visit my father at the cemetery, my heart is constantly flooded with mixed emotions, and oh, how I wish none of this was true. He saved me, but he chose to turn his back on his duty for me—thank god I at least got to meet a genuinely kind person. I learned his real name after he died. He hid a lot from me, but in the end, he didn't take it all to the grave...", "comment": {"by": "Sylvie", "text": "The UNCS and Obsidian are attempting to research how STs can be manipulated through brain intervention...? That sounds awful!"}}, {"title": "[Experiment]", "text": "Every time I look in the mirror, I try to remember what my face looked like in the past, but I simply can't recall it. Even my memories of the past are vague. My father told me it was a result of that accident. Still, I feel like it's my own unwillingness to remember that blocks my recollections. How would I think of the present if I remembered my past life and my family? Would I hate them? Would I be angry? I don't know. My indifference has protected me and allowed me to support myself after my father's death... perhaps this is proof of successful treatment. All I feel now is the emptiness of irony.", "comment": {"by": "Emily", "text": "What was taken away was emotion... Although Gumusiay's experience wasn't exactly the same as ours, the pain we all endure is the same..."}}, {"title": "[Child]", "text": "I did care a lot about the orphans I adopted... Seeing their smiling faces made me feel like my father, and my tiny efforts to help them gave me a sense of redemption. With their help, I slowly recovered the emotions that were taken from me. I once wanted to protect them forever, but the reality of Milkhama taught me that no one can survive alone on this island...", "comment": {"by": "Hong", "text": "That's right! Don't hold back against our enemies anymore, Gumusiay!"}}, {"title": "[Epiphyllum]", "text": "Sylvie and I are in this together, though we still have our roles to figure out. This island gave us all the same scars. Sylvie wants everyone who's hurt and exploited us to pay. I'm not sure if that's what I want—I just hope there won't be more people who end up like us. Milkhama shaped Epiphyllum, and it's destined to be changed by it... It'll happen, one way or another."}]}, "10103174": {"profile": [{"label": "Affiliation", "value": "Vesper"}, {"label": "Blood Type", "value": "A"}, {"label": "Height", "value": "167cm"}, {"label": "技术成果", "value": "仿生智能框架技术；001号自动演算装置「遗产」"}, {"label": "AMC Degree", "value": "低"}], "introduction": "「防卫军少将之女，仿生智能框架技术奠基人，『遗产』的制作者，晨星同盟科学院院士……即便拥有这些头衔，海莉丝·穆勒也不过是一个不曾脱离象牙塔的学者，她无力反抗战争，甚至不知道如何反抗，就和我们控制的其他科研人员一样。只要注意别让她的技术流入其他势力，并牵制住她的父亲提费斯，主动权就永远在我们这边——这是监察委员会曾经的结论，事实证明它根本大错特错。\n海莉丝·穆勒不仅亲手射杀了卢克芒执政官，还带领几近溃散的维斯珀尔重新站稳脚跟，甚至完成了那部超越时代的机兵……就在所有人都将注意力集中于各大势力在米尔萨斯的博弈时，她已经获得了足以动摇局势的力量。即使她的最首要目标不是同盟，这位新的『维斯珀尔』也无疑是比费列克斯·穆勒更不可控的威胁……我们必须重新拟定今后的对策。」——同盟最高议会内部会议记录", "stories": [{"title": "穆勒之女", "text": "「从海莉丝·穆勒出生那天起，我们就盯上了她。因为她的父亲提费斯·穆勒已经被正式任命为机动装甲部队负责人，随时可能作为登陆军主力介入米赫玛岛局势，我们必须确保其家人免受任何敌对势力的侵扰。\n直到战争结束，和平到来，这项工作曾一度中止，又一度重启……有时是为了确认提费斯于米尔萨斯爆炸中的决策是否正确，有时是为了调查他战后领养的米赫玛孤儿的背景，后来则逐渐聚焦于海莉丝本人——毕竟，谁能想到一个出生于军人家庭的少女，竟然拥有世所罕见的科研才能呢？\n自从登上米赫玛岛，能够直接接触与岚物质有关的各式前沿技术后，她的才能在知识积累的过程中快速开花结果，年仅15岁就提出了解决岚质仿生元件信号错位问题的新方案，由此获得了跟随里奥·亚伦斯教授学习的机会。仅仅三年后，刚刚成年不久的她完成了全新的仿生智能框架理论，因此得到卢克芒议员的青睐，得以组建自己的团队进行技术验证……而正如你所知，后来她成功开发出了001号自动演算装置，也就是所谓的『遗产』。\n在那之后，最高议会内部出现了诸多分歧，我无从了解细节，但就结果而言，同盟正式确立了仿生智能框架的军用计划，『遗产』也被转移到他处进行保存解析，监察委员会也因军方压力而停止了对穆勒一家的监视……现在想来，这其中有太多充满风险的不合理决策，或许这都是卢克芒议员在暗中运作的结果。」——同盟监察委员会高级探员回忆"}, {"title": "天才之外", "text": "「在研究员们眼里，海莉丝博士总会毫不留情地批评他人的过错，是一个严厉到有些刻薄、难以接近的人……我曾经也有相同的看法，但在长久共事之后，我已经明白那只是因为她将几乎所有的热情都投入到了研究之中。事实上，她给出的批评或建议总是十分有效，让我们在研究上少走了许多弯路；而在研究之外，她也远比想象中更好相处——只要使用15克的伊吉帝咖啡豆再加91℃的220ml热水，为她泡上一杯咖啡，你就能看到那位冰美人露出孩子般放松的表情。\n在休息时，我们也不止一次聊起过各自的家人。从她口中听到的笨拙父亲，实在很难与教科书上的『战争英雄』联系起来，而费列克斯——那位在防卫军中崭露头角的菁英军官——也始终是她眼中需要关照的弟弟。\n怎么样，真正的天才也有着普通人的一面吧？这份发现让我感到安心，也让我确信她是一个值得追随的人……可以说，我愿意将自己的未来完全赌在她的身上。\n但偏偏，这一切都被那一天毁了——没错，就是法丹研究所遭遇袭击的那一天。我们的研究成果不是被维斯珀尔夺取，就是被治安维持部队扣押转移，就连海莉丝博士本人也不知所踪……我不明白，我们和我们的研究，为什么非得被卷进战争？\n我知道同盟内部最近流传着许多对穆勒一家不利的流言蜚语，那些东西我是一个字也不会信的……除非我见到海莉丝博士，听她亲口承认。」——对海莉丝研究助理采访节选"}, {"title": "意志之续", "text": "「费列克斯曾向我许诺会找到一条改变米赫玛人命运的道路，正是为了亲眼见证这份愿景，我才舍弃了佣兵身份加入了维斯珀尔。那时我以为自己不惧任何牺牲，但当他真正离去时，我还是不免产生了一丝迷惘……失去领袖的维斯珀尔，要如何继续探索那条尚未明晰的道路？无论是我、卡夏还是亚瑟，都没有找到答案。在中央矿区爆炸之后，我们甚至连最简单的复仇都无力实现。\n但她——海莉丝——却在我们没有注意的时候，代替费列克斯走到了前头。尽管这恐怕不符合费列克斯本人的愿望，卡夏她们也对此心怀忧虑，但我从中重新看到了希望……如果不是她，我们早在中央矿区就已经全军覆没；如果不是她，卢克芒还会继续在同盟的庇护下苟存。\n既然她拿起了『维斯珀尔』的头盔，那我该做的事也只有一个，那就是用尽我生命的一切为其而战，直到那份愿景真正实现。」——洛伦佐通讯记录"}, {"title": "未来变量", "text": "「维斯珀尔的存续需要力量，而这正是海莉丝最为欠缺的。和我那时不同，她无法依靠外来者，只能靠自己变得强大……我对此深感悲观，即使拥有稀世的才能，即使舍弃科学伦理孤注一掷，也难以在米赫玛根深蒂固的规则下找到出路。\n但她却向我提出了一个计划，一个能让并非战士也并非将领的她，也有机会撼动这根深蒂固规则的计划。我起初认为那是绝不可能实现的，那部机兵受到防卫军的严密看守，而且始终没有真正完成，即使付出代价将其夺走也毫无意义——直到她拿出那些数据……\n那是上一位『维斯珀尔』在战斗中与『遗产』短暂链接，使得机兵性能出现飞跃式提升的相关记录。其中蕴含了某种融合了新星框架与仿生智能框架的新技术，它粗糙却充满潜力，而海莉丝已经在无人知晓的情况下大幅完善了它的设计，现在的理论效能甚至超越了最新型号的帕姆斯系统。若能集齐必备条件，她的计划或许不再是天方夜谭。\n我已经失去了生存的信念，但我的学生仍在以自己的方式挣扎求索。\n…………\n或许这一次，我不应该再袖手旁观了。」——亚伦斯教授研究日志"}], "cn": true}, "10103140": {"profile": [{"label": "Affiliation", "value": "DLAF"}, {"label": "Blood Type", "value": "AB"}, {"label": "Height", "value": "179cm"}, {"label": "军衔", "value": "一等技术中尉"}], "introduction": "维拉尔斯·哈达威，隶属于晨星同盟防卫军驻米赫玛岛特遣部队的一等技术中尉，是「防卫军之花」玛蒂尔达·罗西最为信赖的副官。\n他精通电子信息战和多型机械操作，对仿生智能框架技术也有所涉猎；性格认真务实、冷静严谨，擅长收集情报并精准分析，即使面对复杂局势也往往能抽丝剥茧直指核心。在就读桑德斯特军事学院的第一年时，他就以优异成绩通过了二等技术军官考核，被视为防卫军信息作战领域的未来之星。在毕业后，他加入了玛蒂尔达所在的第1机动师35营，协助随意散漫的玛蒂尔达执行部队管理和战术规划，并于新历119年随其一同登岛，从此步入米赫玛乱局。", "stories": [{"title": "「维拉尔斯」", "text": "新历95年，维拉尔斯·哈达威出生于晨星同盟本土北部小型城市维纽斯的一个普通家庭，其父亲是汽车厂的一名技工，其母亲是当地小学的数学老师。他自小就展现出过人的头脑和超越同龄人的冷静成熟，早早就代替体弱的母亲担起了大部分家务的同时，还在学校中保持着极为优秀的成绩。即便如此他却始终感觉父母没有正视过自己，即使口中夸赞不断，父母的目光却似乎穿透了他，落在某个幻影上。在旁敲侧击之下，他终于从父母的旧识口中得知了原因——他曾有一个和他一样优秀的哥哥，名字正是「维拉尔斯」，后来却因意外离世。无法彻底走出悲痛的父母，在拥有了第二个孩子之后，为他取了同样的名字。\n当时年仅十岁的维拉尔斯·哈达威并未因此向父母发起反抗，只是在被子中默默哭泣一晚后，更加努力地投入到学习中去。那时起，他开始更多地以姓氏「哈达威」称呼自己。唯有回到家中时，他才会重拾「维拉尔斯」的名字，陪伴着日渐衰老的父母。就这样又过了几年，哈达威以优异成绩从维纽斯的高中毕业，并顺利考入了桑德斯特军事学院……那里能为他提供全额奖学金，也有他自初中以来就一直向往的时代技术结晶——机兵。"}, {"title": "新的人生", "text": "作为来自偏远小城的学生，哈达威在进入桑德斯特军事学院前从未真正接触过拥有钢岚合金框架的机兵，但他天生的聪慧和学习自父亲的机修知识却帮助他快速入了门。他花费了数倍于他人的努力，全身心投入到学习与实验之中，以极快的速度吸收着与钢岚合金、机兵驾驶有关的一切知识，在入学后第二年就主动参加二等技术军官考核并以优异成绩通过。此后他逐渐拓展着视野，开始对电子信息战、战术指挥乃至仿生智能框架理论等尚未系统学习的领域产生了浓厚的兴趣，并且一如既往地快速学习成长。\n然而在第三学年，他以分区指挥官身份参与的模拟军演却遭遇了前所未有的惨败。无论他如何安排部队、调整战术，似乎都永远慢演习对手一步，无奈之下只能利用电子战扰乱指挥后亲自带队奇袭，却就此落入陷阱被一网打尽——直到在那里见到一抹火红的长发，他才明白自己的对手是学院特邀的战术教官玛蒂尔达·罗西。\n自那以后，哈达威人生的轨迹开始转变——他不喜欢玛蒂尔达的随意态度和基于直觉的跳脱战术，却屡屡见证她取得更为优秀的结果。在玛蒂尔达留校担任教官的短短半年时间内，哈达威不断向她发起指挥模拟战，虽始终无法取胜，但每一次挑战的战况都比上次有所好转……他相信自己终有一天可以超越那位「防卫军之花」。可就在哈达威精心筹备了全新的战术方案，准备挑战第十次模拟战时，玛蒂尔达却因防卫军的一纸调令离开了桑德斯特军事学院。"}, {"title": "精英去处", "text": "新历116年，哈达威从桑德斯特军事学院正式毕业，出色的在校表现吸引了防卫军内部多个精英部队的目光，据说就连最高议会的执行者部队也对其有所关注。然而他却在短暂的回家探亲之后，选择前往了同盟中南部小城……那是玛蒂尔达·罗西少校的第1机动师35营的所在地。在那里见到的玛蒂尔达比过去更为散漫，已经完全看不出她曾是米赫玛战争时期立下诸多战功的王牌指挥官。\n哈达威指责她的散漫态度是在浪费自己的才能，只会让传奇的35营变成废人聚集地，随后向她发起了迟来数年的第十次指挥模拟战。此举激怒了35营的将士们，双方在演习场爆发了激烈的机兵战斗。哈达威凭借事先调查的情报冷静应对，连续击败了多名实力不俗的老兵，一时震慑了众人，而玛蒂尔达也在这时同意了对战。\n在完全对等的初始态势下，两人展开了模拟指挥对抗，不断出招又拆招，足足持续了16小时才终于分出胜负……玛蒂尔达将自身作饵，以微小的优势再一次胜过了哈达威。明白自己仍有不足的哈达威本准备就此离开，玛蒂尔达却拦下了他，笑嘻嘻要求他为那些被破坏的军队财产负责——而且是以留在35营的方式。\n没人知道玛蒂尔达花了多少工夫去应付对此不满的其他部队，但结果上哈达威就此留在了35营，而且很快就凭借出色的能力成为了部队的战术参谋，协助玛蒂尔达整顿军纪，甚至执行部队管理和战术规划。或许是不打不相识，队伍中那些老兵也在一段时间的相处后，也逐渐认可了这位年轻气盛但能力出众的新人。"}, {"title": "外来者", "text": "新历119年2月，第1机动师35营参与了全防卫军军事技能竞赛，并获得了综合第四名的优秀成绩，这也为他们赢得了正式的休假机会。在简短的讨论之后，玛蒂尔达和哈达威最终决定前往米赫玛岛度过假期。\n不同于散漫度日的玛蒂尔达，哈达威自登岛的第一天起就四处忙碌……时而参加学术会议，时而暗访佣兵交易所，时而渗透天网挖掘数据，时而订购受限制的机兵部件进行研究。在这一过程中他收获了大量真实的第一手情报，也于黑白两道结识了一些新朋友。\n他只是一个外来者，在米赫玛岛没有任何利益，也不曾留下任何执念。正因此，他始终维持着一个客观的视角，冷静观察着米赫玛岛的本质——这里更像是一个斗兽场，各大势力不断孵化、训练着自己的猛兽，随时准备进行一场激烈的对抗。或许正是因为这份认知，在被突然卷入由维斯珀尔引发的一系列动乱中时，哈达威第一时间就做好了准备。\n即使他对晨星同盟在东米赫玛的做法有所质疑，即使明白自己的力量根本不足以撼动局势，他也不会放下自己身为军人、身为玛蒂尔达副官的职责。"}], "cn": true}, "10103110": {"profile": [{"label": "Affiliation", "value": "The Epiphyllum"}, {"label": "Blood Type", "value": "O"}, {"label": "Height", "value": "170cm"}, {"label": "Specialty", "value": "Oriental martial arts, Nunchaku"}, {"label": "Resume", "value": "Stunt double"}], "introduction": "Hong - Epiphyllum's eastern pilot, Sylvie's partner. Spinal injury led to Arashium experiments. Caught Winston's eye with sync rates. Rosa saved her. Now she and Sylvie chase ST and Hyper-Aptamer secrets.", "stories": [{"title": "[The Nightmare Begins]", "text": "You've probably noticed by now, I don't exactly blend in with the crowd around here... That's because I come from a faraway place in the East. Before landing on Milkhama Island, I lived with my sifu and a whole crew of senior sisters. Our daily grind was pure martial arts, perfecting our acting skills, and hustling on every stage in the city—sometimes as stand-ins for those big-shot movie stars. I shouldn't even be involved in the chaotic mess on this island, let alone get tangled up in any of this ST research crap... But thirteen years ago, everything flipped when I fell off a prop during a show and broke my back. That's when the real mess started."}, {"title": "[The Mourning Continues]", "text": "You know what a busted spine means, right? No feeling from the hips down, and a wheelchair for the rest of your life. I don't even remember what I was feeling back then—the whole world was like a blur to me. My sifu tried everything, but nothing worked. Just when we were about to throw in the towel, sifu got this invite from the UNCS Biomedical Research Organization. The doc on the other end said they were working on a spinal replacement tech, some kind of neural link deal, and if I went through the procedure, I might actually walk again.", "comment": {"by": "Naomi", "text": "The UNCS once extensively recruited participants from around the world to partake in clinical trials for new medical technologies. Most cases ended in failure—Hong was one of the rare successes."}}, {"title": "[Luck of All Lucks]", "text": "Following the information provided by the liaison, my sifu sent me to Milkhama Island... You can probably guess what happened next. The so-called neural connection technology was part of the \"Hyper-Aptamer\" project. After screening, I underwent targeted surgery and demonstrated high adaptability to the Nova-Frame in the experimental phase, becoming the lucky one among hundreds of subjects. Then, I was treated as a critical observation subject and locked up with Sylvie, Emily, and the others... I traded my future for my legs but I lost the freedom to walk with them forever.", "comment": {"by": "Dana", "text": "If neural interface tech had only been used for medical research, who knows what kind of breakthrough it could've been... It's too bad it ended up as just another terrible tool for waging war."}}, {"title": "[Farewell to Yesterday]", "text": "After that came a long and challenging period of struggle with the aftermath, day after day—that was until Rosa saved us, but she fell at White Maple... We should leave the past behind and focus on living each day to the fullest. Rosa wouldn't want us, the people she rescued, to still be moping around like before... And one day, we'll uncover the truth and defeat the UNCS."}]}, "10103101": {"profile": [{"label": "Affiliation", "value": "GKD"}, {"label": "Blood Type", "value": "O"}, {"label": "Height", "value": "183cm"}], "introduction": "\"Ex-merc. Bad record. Discipline issues. Teamwork uncertain. Great instincts, reads enemy patterns, can lead small ops.\nOpinion: Train for mobile reserve, temp command ok. Note: Not for my squad. We don't take their kind.\"\n—Rosa Diaz", "stories": [{"title": "Where is Home?", "text": "I wouldn't say I like to talk about my past as there's not really much to say... Just the story of some war orphan who grew up in a shelter, taken in by a kind scientist. But before my father's accident, I didn't really know who he was or what he was doing. He was always busy, practically living at the lab. He'd only show up at this place, \"home,\" a few days a year. Sometimes I don't get it. If he didn't care about family, then why take me in? And why talk to me about all those far-out things I could never attain?", "comment": {"by": "Grant", "text": "As one reaches middle age, especially when you become aware of your own mortality, you suddenly start worrying about your legacy and children... Your father must have been moved by something similar when he decided to adopt you."}}, {"title": "Personal Bodyguard", "text": "I was about fourteen when he first took me to their lab... well, calling it a \"lab\" is generous. It was more like a fancy ST repair shop. I'd already told him I snuck around and messed with some of the STs when he wasn't home... you know how boys can't get enough of that kind of stuff, but he was still all hyped up, going on about mech theories and all that tech stuff—he even let me hop into the cockpit. That was the first time I ever piloted a mech of any kind. When I climbed out, he looked at me and said, \"Son, from now on, you'll be my personal bodyguard.\""}, {"title": "Undetermined Fate", "text": "So, I ended up being his personal bodyguard, tagging along with him to the research facility on Milkhama Island. Most of the time, I was out there piloting an ST, sitting through endless meetings with him. When he was too busy, he'd let me take on some side gigs for the security company—just as long as I didn't touch the STs at the lab. Then, out of nowhere, he disappeared for a while. No calls, no work, nothing. I didn't hear from him until my security firm got a hot job. By the time I got there, his ride was blown up by some unknown rocket fire, and suddenly, I'm the one they're pointing fingers at.", "comment": {"by": "Naomi", "text": "We have checked the communication records of the security company Kaidan was with. It was found that the source of the emergency mission was the Viceroy's Office in the Milkhama UNCS Jurisdiction."}}, {"title": "The Truth of Innocence", "text": "They said I did it, but they had no proof. After a bunch of questioning, they had to let me go. But not one of them bothered to tell me what really happened to my father, where he went, or what he was up to before he disappeared. All I got was cold stares, shady answers, and lies. I knew it was a setup. So, the day I got out, I stopped asking, stopped talking. I knew one thing—my future's mine to figure out, and I'm gonna find the truth myself."}]}, "10103182": {"profile": [{"label": "Affiliation", "value": "GKD"}, {"label": "Blood Type", "value": "O"}, {"label": "Height", "value": "183cm"}, {"label": "作战呼号", "value": "「猎豹一号」"}, {"label": "佣兵等级", "value": "S"}, {"label": "Sync Ratio", "value": "97%"}], "introduction": "在黑曜石科学家尼尔的操刀下解除了纽曼博士的神经限制，正式解放了超适体潜力的凯登·纽曼。身为原型体，他无需接受身体的深度改造，也不会产生精神的异化扭曲，因此有着其他实验体都无法比拟的高度稳定性，可以在任何情况下维持同步，将多年佣兵生涯所磨炼出的全部技巧、经验和直觉发挥到极致。\n面对席卷全岛的米赫玛战争以及暗中活跃的奥维特禁军势力，他决心赌上自己全部的可能性保护猎豹物流、昙少女等同伴，并与他们一同终结乱局。", "stories": [{"title": "原型", "text": "「同步率71%……实验开始以来，第一次检测到这么高的数值。\n没有任何身体改造，没有岚物质的长期侵染，也没有外部器械的刺激强化，这就是凯登与生俱来的特质，这证明『超适体』不只是存在于理论中的幻想。\n我几乎无法抑制双手的颤抖和心脏的躁动，直直注视着显示屏，期待着上面的数字再次突破极限，但随之而来的却是机器的警报声和一股轻微的焦糊味……监测芯片无法承受压力而部分熔毁了。这不是什么大问题，只要替换损毁的模块就好。但就在我靠近模拟舱时，我看到了那孩子的眼神——那里有疑惑，有不安，但更多的是信任……对我这个『父亲』的信任。那一瞬，我心头正要燃起的狂热突然被浇灭了。\n如果确定了他就是『原型』，我要怎么办？按照规定，应该把实验体交给联合军，由布莱尔总督决定他的命运，但那就意味着把他扔进地狱！即使侥幸不死，恐怕也会丧失意志沦为一台战争机器。好在监测芯片已经熔毁，实验室里也没有其他人，只要将数据下调到平均值，删除多余记录，我就能将今天的实验伪装成一次失败的常规模拟，瞒过总督府那帮家伙。现在最大的问题是哈里森，他的受验者单元测试需要凯登，而我必须说服他放弃那些数据……但愿我的朋友，不会成为敌人。」——《沃尔特·纽曼隐藏语音数据第164条》", "comment": {"by": "Kaidan The Invincible", "text": "那天是父亲第一次带我去实验室。当时我不理解父亲的研究，不理解他为什么兴奋又为什么面露哀愁，只是知道他是一个天才科学家……现在的我已经知晓了更多真相，也更加确定，他到底是多么了不起。"}}, {"title": "秘密", "text": "「能拿到解除限制的『遗产』都是你的功劳，费列克斯。亚瑟她们正在抓紧时间，利用它强大的算力进行全域信息处理，预计半小时内就能完成既定任务。除此之外还有一件事，我觉得应该让你知道——研究班在最新的凯登神经数据中意外发现了一处信号暗区，经过反复比对，确认那是在连接遗产之后才出现的神经加密。和当初解锁遗产类似，这个新的加密也需要一把新的钥匙……恐怕没人能想到吧，纽曼博士在秘密之下还埋藏着一个更深的秘密。不过目前的局势容不得细细研究，等你回来后，我们再做决定。」——维斯珀尔内部通讯\n「在完善弥造者的过程中，我重新解析了同盟与费列克斯的研究日志、阿波菲斯的残存数据，以及遗产框架的核心记录，所有的信息都指向一点——凯登具有与艾达相似的超适体特质，但却被有意阻断了激活信号的传递。长久以来这种阻断都非常有效，即使是西塞罗博士的原型测试也没有完全揭示凯登与钢岚共鸣的真实能力。但在连接遗产后，他的同步率开始了稳步提升，或许只需要一次彻底的直连，这世上就会多出一位超适体……但同时，那也会是一把双刃剑，即使是迪亚兹姐妹也曾一度失去对自己力量的掌控……没人能保证奇迹会连续出现三次。」——海莉丝研究日志"}, {"title": "等待", "text": "「米尔萨斯一战已经过去了一个多月了，还是没有老大的消息。\n听说洛莎带着昙少女把米尔萨斯内外找了个遍，贝拉和维斯珀尔深入矿区四处探索，西边有安全总署和灰烬之子联合追查，东边有肖妮的警察部队协助搜寻，就连角雕也向佣兵们发出了寻人委托……不只是咱们猎豹物流，整座米赫玛不知有多少人为了老大而奔波，但就算这样，还是没法确定他到底被黑障那混蛋带去了哪里。安已经急哭了好几次，哈维也没了精神，而黛娜……谁都能看出来她在硬撑。我只能一次又一次地向她们保证，虽然情况不容乐观，但还没到最坏的地步——黑曜石抓了人却至今没有提出任何要求，这证明他们的目标就是老大本身，那就肯定不会轻易害了他。而且，我认识的凯登·纽曼也不可能就这样不声不响地倒下……他一定会在一个谁都想不到的时刻突然归来，吓所有人一跳，然后带我们打一场奇迹般的胜仗。\n在那一刻到来之前，我们得想办法拖住公国那群疯子……既然他们把禁军都派过来了，这座岛上的风暴恐怕也别想止住了。」——格兰特的天网个人记录"}, {"title": "觉醒", "text": "「不同于经历了更生实验，有着极限同步的洛莎；也不同于孵化了超级AI，两心一体的艾达……凯登的特殊之处不在于超出界限的感应数值，而在于成长与稳定。自沃尔特·纽曼初次激发他的潜质以来，他与岚物质共鸣的能力始终在缓慢提升，即使身体已从孩童转为青年，即使后来被施加了神经限制，这份成长也从未停止。而在我解除了限制之后，『原型』的表现终于开始追赶本质，他在无数次死斗中积累下的技巧、经验和直觉注定再次升华……我不介意花上更多年月观察这一转变的过程，但可惜，他等不起，岛上的许多人都等不起。\n为了使凯登在短时间内获得超越黑障和禁军的力量，我们只能寻求某种催化剂。有趣的是，敌人在此时递来了一剂毒药……那是来自奥维特的异型岚物质，它具有极强的污染性，比米赫玛的岚物质更加凶暴。阿列克谢毫不掩饰自己的意图，他逼迫我注射药剂，以此侵蚀凯登的大脑，扭曲他的精神。身为俘虏的我们无法拒绝，也没必要拒绝——凭我和沃尔特·纽曼两人的技术，足以彻底净化异型岚物质，但前提是凯登能够挺过第一阶段的污染……如果他过早地沦陷于精神枷锁之中，那留给我们的就只会是一个空有超高同步率的杀戮人偶。\n能否以完美超适体的姿态觉醒，逆转这几近绝望的局势，终究得看他个人的意志……或许，还有一点点的运气。」——尼尔的研究日志"}], "cn": true}, "10103141": {"profile": [{"label": "Affiliation", "value": "Dawnstar League"}, {"label": "Blood Type", "value": "AB"}, {"label": "Height", "value": "165cm"}, {"label": "Previous Occupation", "value": "Captain of the Black Shark Special Forces"}, {"label": "Nickname", "value": "White Stork"}], "introduction": "A distinguished DLAF officer from the Dawnstar League homeland, Kelly is widely recognized as a composed and razor-sharp elite sniper. She is often hailed as the most unpredictable wild card on the battlefield, capable of utilizing any vantage point to shift the tide in her favor. Despite her seemingly nonchalant attitude in everyday life and her disheveled appearance when traveling with Diracca, her unparalleled lethality on the battlefield is never in question by her allies or enemies. One recollection from a reprimanded recruit vividly captures the sense of constant surveillance she exudes: \"It feels like those eagle-eyes never leave you for a second.\"", "stories": [{"title": "Can't Have It All", "text": "Kelly Polis has been in the spotlight since she was a child, with outstanding achievements, an exquisite appearance, and incredible eyesight. At age ten, she could accurately hit a criminal fifty meters away with a slingshot. Cloaked in accolades, Kelly was a regular recipient of scholarships during her student days, but surprisingly, this elite pupil had few friends. Perhaps it was because people were not used to Kelly's cold personality, or they were jealous of her talents. Surrounding Kelly were not only flowers and applause but also countless idle rumors. Kelly didn't like to waste time on useless things and gradually became accustomed to being alone until..."}, {"title": "Unpredictable", "text": "During her college years, Kelly attended the most prestigious local university as an outstanding student representative for a three-month exchange program. During that time, she met her equally accomplished roommate, Shawnee Russell. Shawnee's appearance undoubtedly enriched Kelly's extracurricular life. They studied and discussed situations and communicated their opinions, and Kelly even discussed shooting techniques with Shawnee for the first time. She even learned her first ballroom dance from Shawnee. Despite their different styles, they got along very well. Although their time together was short, and Kelly did not fully understand all that the name \"Shawnee Russell\" encompassed, she still cherished this friendship and secretly awaited their reunion."}, {"title": "Talent Shines", "text": "After graduation, Kelly joined the DLAF. Due to her outstanding combat prowess, she quickly became an elite sniper in the Black Shark Special Forces. In the DLAF, where strength determines one's position, Kelly felt at home, and gradually gathered many followers around her. Over the years, Kelly and her squad achieved numerous glorious victories, becoming a genuinely elite combat unit. During breaks from her missions, Kelly occasionally reminisced about the golden times she spent with her old friend. She never imagined that their reunion had already been set in motion.", "comment": {"by": "Dana", "text": "The famous \"Black Sharks.\" I heard the coach talk about this special forces unit when I was at Enfield. The team members risk their lives to carry out missions—even the entrance exam is notoriously brutal. I never thought Kelly came from there. No wonder she was the only one who felt my performance wasn't up to par during the joint training competition. If I only had another chance..."}}, {"title": "Turbulent Depths", "text": "On the rainy night her transfer orders arrived, Kelly spent the entire evening at the shooting range. The terminal on her desk stayed on until morning, displaying just one short email, signed with a beautiful cursive signature—\"Shawnee Russell.\" Kelly never thought she would reconnect with her long-lost friend in this way, nor did she expect that Shawnee would become the security chief of the DL's jurisdiction on Milkhama and that this transfer order was her doing. Kelly couldn't understand what made that perilous, unpredictable island so alluring. What was it that drew someone as gifted as Shawnee, enough to make her willingly abandon the comfort and prestige of life in the Dawnstar Alliance? In the end, doubts and longing drove Kelly to set foot on the scorched earth of Milkhama, and she looked forward to the answers that time would bring, even if the road ahead was paved with cinders and gunfire.", "comment": {"by": "Kaidan", "text": "I don't know whether to admire the security officer's foresight for the smooth development of the situation to this point, or marvel that a friendship this rare could bloom in a place like this."}}]}, "10103179": {"profile": [{"label": "Affiliation", "value": "亚太战区"}, {"label": "Blood Type", "value": "Unknown"}, {"label": "Height", "value": "168cm"}, {"label": "军衔", "value": "1st Lieutenant"}, {"label": "籍贯", "value": "江苏南京"}, {"label": "三围", "value": "87-64-83"}], "introduction": "郑乐萱，来自异世界的机兵驾驶员，隶属于「亚太战区精神力机甲作战部队」，适配机甲为七号机「霸王」。虽然年轻但训练有素，曾随部队多次成功击退外星污染者，完成包括摧毁成都黑塔、上海黑塔在内的多项重要任务，作战经验丰富。她开朗直率，意志坚定，勇敢正义，既有合格军人的遵规守纪，也能灵活变通，有着良好的合作协同能力，无论在军旅中还是生活里都十分可靠，深得众人的信赖。\n即使意外来到米赫玛岛，郑乐萱仍以极快的速度适应了这片陌生的土地，并与维斯珀尔一同向污染者的阴谋发起了冲击。", "stories": [{"title": "记录1·印象", "text": "「郑乐萱中尉和我认识的所有军人都不一样。\n不，我指的不是她的模样和名字在米赫玛有多少见，而是她有种……飒爽的感觉？我不太会形容，总之，我在她身上感觉不到北陆联合或者晨星同盟的军人常有的随波逐流感，也不像我们这些人一样被现实压得喘不过气。作为久经沙场的军官，她的眼神里依然闪烁着正义和荣耀，对我们也毫无偏见，甚至愿意抽时间陪我们训练、帮我们搬运伤员、和我们谈天说笑，在她面前我甚至不会感觉到有什么压力……或许是我见识少，反正我从没在这座岛上见过这样的军人。\n所以，在得知她很可能是来自另一个世界时，我反倒不觉得有多惊讶，只是又产生了更多的好奇——她这样的实力、信念、性格，究竟是怎样的环境造就的？她的故乡……应该是一个远比米赫玛更有希望的地方吧。」——维斯珀尔成员内部讨论"}, {"title": "记录2·过去", "text": "「只要不是军事机密，她总是很爽快地回答我的每一个疑问，不知不觉间我开始觉得防备她是一件很傻的事了。后来我们越聊越多，大到各自世界的概况，小到身边的琐碎小事，几乎什么都聊。\n她似乎是19岁考入了装甲兵指挥学院，在那里习得了操纵人形机动装甲的基本技能，以优异成绩毕业后又进入了正规军装甲部队服役。在『审判日』，也就是污染者大举入侵的日子后，她就一路随各部队作战，甚至以步兵姿态参与过破坏敌人中枢的行动……很厉害吧？连卡夏姐都对她赞不绝口，明明和我的年龄相差无几。\n啊说到这个，有一点其实是最让我惊讶的——她竟然是出生于一个文化人家庭，而且是家里最小的妹妹！像她那样开朗率直但信念坚定的人，我以为肯定是一个军人家庭的长姐呢。听她说，她的父亲是历史学家，母亲和大哥都是音乐演奏家，只有二哥和她一样成为了亚太战区的军人，而且也是一名精神力机甲驾驶员，两人还一起参与过不少作战行动。我还记得她当时的表情，她和二哥的感情一定很好……虽然她自己极力否认了。」——亚瑟·纳迪卜的回忆片段"}, {"title": "记录3·信念", "text": "「精神力机甲绝非常人可以驾驭的——越是了解精神粒子，我就越相信这一点，同时也越能认识到郑乐萱究竟有多么了不起。\n据说她能够驾驶几乎全部的作战装备，不论是汽车、坦克、甚至不同种类的飞机，如此全能的技巧在她这个年纪上都显得不可思议……虽然她没有细说自己究竟付出了多少心血，但我相信，如果没有钢铁般的意志和坚定的信念是绝对不可能做到的，更不可能像她现在这样掌握娴熟而高效的作战技巧。\n如果我也能像她一样，拥有一往无前的勇气和信念的话，或许维斯珀尔就仍有未来……」——海莉丝的个人日志"}, {"title": "记录4·临别", "text": "「喂喂……好，开始录制了。\n明天就是我返回地球的日子，亚瑟说什么也要我留下点记录作纪念，所以录制了这段视频。\n虽然我在这个世界只度过了寥寥几天，但实在是发生了太多的事。被卷入污染者的跃迁实验，来到米赫玛岛，遇到维斯珀尔的各位，一同清剿污染者，甚至还摧毁了一座黑塔……实在太过充实了。等我回去后，一定要向亚太战区的大家狠狠炫耀一番。\n我会告诉他们在这个世界经历的战斗、看见的风景、尝过的美食，以及……认识的新朋友——来，亚瑟，海莉丝，看镜头！这份记录可不能只有我一个人出镜。\n别这副表情，这一定不是永别。只要相信会重逢，我们就迟早会在未来再见的！」——维斯珀尔核心数据库重要记录"}], "cn": true}, "10103138": {"profile": [{"label": "Affiliation", "value": "Free Milkhama"}, {"label": "Blood Type", "value": "O"}, {"label": "Height", "value": "155cm"}, {"label": "Notable Feats", "value": "Also earned the title of \"Boss\" after crushing ten so-called \"warlords.\""}], "introduction": "\"Who are you looking for? Oh, Lorna? She should be out on patrol with her dad right now! You know, that little rascal—when she was first brought in, I could have picked her up with one hand. I had no idea how much she'd grown since then! Just please keep this between us; I don't want her to find out I said anything. The last thing I need is to be hounded by her and end up living in an ST!\" —A Milkhaman from the DL Colony", "stories": [{"title": "Patrol Officer", "text": "\"After speaking with many locals, I came upon Lorna Mahalim teaching some troublemakers a lesson. She was indeed as energetic and agile as everyone had said. Even though she was just a child, she had already begun to use her fists to uphold justice in her neighborhood. Lorna was very cautious when I, a stranger, arrived and kept questioning my intentions. She looked at my press card more than ten times before reluctantly trusting my identity. The environment in the autonomous region is chaotic, which would make for good exposure material. I wanted to take more photos, but Lorna stopped me... She was protecting the last refuge of the native Milkhaman in her own way... So I understood that if I wanted to complete this interview smoothly, I might need to show more understanding and goodwill.\" —Excerpt from a DL Journalist's Memoirs, Unfading Light in the Night", "comment": {"by": "Naomi", "text": "Hey, I know this book! It's pretty well-written, but I wonder why they stopped publishing them... I hear some experts called it \"inaccurate,\" but those bookworms haven't even been out to the borderlands before."}}, {"title": "The Flower of Hope", "text": "\"On the fourteenth day, after helping her deliver two truck-loads of drinking water, Lorna finally accepted the Ms. Chili Soda I offered. We leaned against a truck tire, drinking our beverages and watching the sunset. Then she told me her story—being abandoned at birth, adopted by the autonomous region's leader, growing up under the care of the refugees, and being given the surname \"Mahalim\" shared by the orphans of Milkhama. When she introduced herself, she smiled and looked up, the excitement of drinking soda for the first time shining in her eyes like pride. At that moment, I understood why every citizen I had interviewed before would express a hint of tenderness when mentioning Lorna—this child was a beautiful flower they had worked hard to cultivate in this barren soil, bringing with her something called \"hope.\" —Excerpt from a DL Journalist's Memoirs, Unfading Light in the Night", "comment": {"by": "Grant", "text": "*sigh* I never thought that this little she-devil had such a difficult childhood... I'll take her out for drinks—real drinks! Uh, and two more truckloads of Ms. Chili Soda!"}}, {"title": "Milkhamanesque", "text": "\"I asked Lorna if she had ever considered leaving the autonomous zone. She was still just a child, and perhaps she could leave this chaotic land and seek out some local immigrants in other areas willing to adopt her. But the little girl quickly gave me a negative answer, saying, 'This is my home, where my family lives. I won't go anywhere. I will protect the people here.' She was so young, but this land she grew up in, with its many trials and tribulations, had already given her a sense of self completely different from her peers in the outside world. She sat in the cockpit of the ST like an adult, shuttling through the alleys of the autonomous zone to uphold justice like the wind and sowing the seeds of hope in people's hearts like a hero... Perhaps in the future, she is destined to once again face the flames of war like all Milkhamans.\" —Excerpt from a DL Journalist's Memoirs, Unfading Light in the Night"}, {"title": "Dawn's Faint Light", "text": "\"At the end of the interview, I requested a group photo, which Lorna unsurprisingly declined. However, this time, she was not as straightforward and stern as before. She seemed hesitant and shy, with a hint of regret deep in her eyes. She escorted me to the front gate as if urging me to leave. Before parting ways, I left my contact information in case the child wanted a way out in the future. She did not accept it. Perhaps in this chaotic era, no one can truly establish order, but Lorna still believes that the peace her family has longed for will eventually come. 'I will witness that day with my own eyes,' she said. As I watched her continue to rush around, I suddenly found myself also looking forward to the future she believed in.\" — Excerpt 4 from a DL Journalist's Memoirs, Unfading Light in the Night", "comment": {"by": "Kaidan", "text": "Civilians shouldn't be the ones paying the price for war. We've got to take down the people stirring the pot—fast. That's the only way Lorna and her family will ever have a shot at what they've been dreaming of..."}}]}, "10103173": {"profile": [{"label": "Affiliation", "value": "Obsidian Group"}, {"label": "Blood Type", "value": "▇▇"}, {"label": "Height", "value": "166cm"}, {"label": "Sync Ratio", "value": "100%"}, {"label": "苏醒日志", "value": "X.C.119年激活"}], "introduction": "曜，黑曜石集团生物科技的最高技术结晶，也是米赫玛上唯一将人类意识与钢岚合金深度融合的共存体，她的存在本身早已跨越了人与机械之间那道看似不可逾越的边界。在与岚物质共同沉睡的漫长时间里，曜以迥异于人类的感知模式，逐渐形成了独属于自己的意志。这具冷彻的机体最初因一段试图挽留挚爱的深重偏执而诞生，但即便后来属于过去的那段人类记忆被悉数唤醒，那抹从岚物质中蜕变而出的全新自我，也早已无法被任何既定程序或往日幻影所束缚。\n带着这抹全然自由的意志，曜将视线投向了更广阔的世界。在米赫玛这片被欲望撕裂的土地上，她开始以超然的目光静默地注视着所有的一切。她见证过人类的光辉与黑暗，感受过真实的痛苦与悲伤，也体察过纯粹的温情与欢欣。最终，曜认可了人类在矛盾与挣扎中蕴含的无穷可能性，并决定以这具由人类执念与尖端科技交织而成的躯壳，跨越它最初被赋予的定义，走上一条真正属于「曜」的守望之路。", "stories": [{"title": "「容器」", "text": "「我不确定这是否能被称作医学奇迹。在被派往尼尔博士的实验室担任助手之前，我已有整整四十年的临床经验。我以为自己不会再为任何手术台上的场景皱眉头了。但当我遵照尼尔博士的指令，将某种……彷如液态合金的东西直接输入希尔芙的体内时，我还是忍不住失态了。\n她大概是疯了。尼尔·昆施泰特的大名我早有耳闻，在她研究最出格的那段时期，全世界的新闻网站上都能看到她的名字，后面永远跟着义正辞严的批判。我不明白社长为什么要把希尔芙交给这样一个危险的家伙。这种困惑，在尼尔催促我加大输液量时达到了顶点。我亲眼看着那些液体像是有自己的意志一样顺着血管蔓延，将原本的身体组织包裹、溶解、再编织，直到它们把希尔芙大部分的躯体变成了钢岚合金。而在整个过程中，希尔芙的排异反应却远不如我预想中那么强烈，这简直是……匪夷所思。\n尼尔博士没有向我解释这一切是如何做到的。因为在她眼中，几乎看不到除希尔芙之外的任何东西——虽然她只是把希尔芙那副崭新的躯体视作『容器』。我无法不感到不安。不只是因为这场实验本身的诡异，更是因为我觉得，也许我们所有人都还没有准备好面对像『希尔芙』那样的全新存在。\n」——黑曜石加密研究记录"}, {"title": "震荡", "text": "「希尔芙的身体改造已经全部完成，生理指标十分稳定，岚物质融合率虽然尚在高位波动，但尼尔博士对此毫不担心，断言它很快就会平稳下来。果然，博士的预言又一次应验——融合率不仅稳定了，最终还达到了一个令人难以置信的数字。看着希尔芙在实验台上恬静又温和的睡颜，我时常会思考，躺在那里的人究竟还是不是我所知道的那个人，又或者，她还能被称作为『人』吗？我无法给出一个准确的答案。\n有段时间我们对希尔芙的大脑进行了详细检测，检测结果让尼尔博士沉默了很久。我仔细研读了相关的数据，很快就明白了她沉默的原因。\n和以往的掠食者们不同，希尔芙大脑中的神经网络展现出一种近乎病态的秩序感——仿佛被某种外力温柔地梳理过，又或者，是它们自发形成了稳定的结构。经过多次扫描确认，我们还发现从希尔芙的大脑中传来了一种节律性的神经振荡，那频率像极了呼吸……我不知道这意味着什么。但面对如今的希尔芙这样全新的存在，我相信，能想出答案的人，在这世上恐怕也是凤毛麟角。」——黑曜石加密研究记录"}, {"title": "凝望", "text": "「昨夜出了一件大事，有两名掠食者不知用什么方法从实验室逃了出来，劫持了两台机兵，在基地东侧引发了一场不小的混乱。当时我正和曜准备前往下一个实验室，警卫队出击的动静让我们停在了原地。在那个位置不难看清东侧的情况。我有些心急，因为逃跑的掠食者无外乎一种结局——他们以为通往外界的生路，从来都只通向地狱。我想做些什么，但也清楚这不是我能干预的事。\n那两个掠食者一路越过警卫驶向了基地的边界，但我清楚地看到他们其中的一台机兵很快就要失去动力。如果他们就此分开，或许还有一个人能活下来。可看他们那副死也要死在一起的架势，这种可能性微乎其微……唉。然而就在警卫即将开枪时，我亲眼看见他的枪口在一瞬间偏移了，子弹擦着远处的机兵飞过，只差毫厘。我惊疑不定地想和曜说些什么，但那一瞬间，我见到了她似乎在微微闪烁着光芒的眼睛。\n我突然意识到，就在刚才，我身边这位看上去柔弱单薄的少女，也许做了什么。但她没有回应我的目光，只是深深凝望着那两个已经远去的掠食者，静默得像一尊雕塑。\n『我们走吧。』在那两个影子完全看不见之后，她只是轻轻对我这么说。」——黑曜石加密研究记录"}, {"title": "变量", "text": "「……从技术指标上看，这次的意识植入无疑是成功的。希尔芙的全部人格记忆以完整的形态接入了曜的神经网络，融合稳定性超出预期，没有出现结构性的损伤或丢失。不过出乎预料的是，那些记忆所产生的神经信号活跃度始终可以被稳定监测到——这意味着它们很可能像归档的文件一样存放在曜大脑的某一区域，而不是与那具身体融为一体。\n我起初担心这是一种缺陷——人格记忆未能与主体意识建立深度联系，可能会影响对躯体的操控精度。但后来的一系列观测迹象都表明我的担心是多余的。曜的意识已经足够强大，足以完全驾驭这具躯体。人类与岚物质的共存试验比我想象得还要成功，我对这个结果已经十分满意。\n至于从这个试验诞生出的意外……那并不是我需要关注的重点。不过，可以预见的是，已经拥有独立人格的曜应该会是一个巨大的变量，在将来也许能掀起一番难以预料的风暴吧？\n——我拭目以待。」——尼尔加密研究记录"}], "cn": true}, "10103129": {"profile": [{"label": "Affiliation", "value": "Dawnstar League"}, {"label": "Blood Type", "value": "AB"}, {"label": "Height", "value": "166cm"}, {"label": "异常反应", "value": "▇▇"}], "introduction": "玛阿特·谢里夫，东米赫玛前任执政官卢克芒的副官。\n她出身于同盟边境小国伊吉帝，该国曾在与邻国的军事争端中陷入劣势，后因议员卢克芒代表晨星同盟介入局势而最终赢得胜利，正是在这一过程中她选择了追随卢克芒，一丝不苟地执行其指示，以忠心换取同盟对伊吉帝的长期支持。然而米尔萨斯爆炸发生后，她过往近十年在晨星同盟中所做的所有努力，都因卢克芒之死而土崩瓦解，伊吉帝的复兴已成虚妄，自己更在战乱中负伤昏迷。当苏醒并知晓一切后，她决心投身于纯粹的复仇当中，以消灭维斯珀尔作为自己最后的生存目的。", "stories": [{"title": "未尽之事", "text": "「第二区域清扫中，核心区岚浓度仍维持在安全值122%以上，蓝色粉尘在探照灯照射下形成清晰的岚雾现象，能见度不足三十米，理论无生命体存活可能。我们已完成98%的战场清扫，所有大型机甲残骸均已被标记。目前正在对最后一片残骸区进行扫描，此处堆积着大量机兵残骸和倒塌房屋。生命探测仪背景读数一直稳定……等等……仪器突然捕捉到规律性脉冲信号。信号源位于重型机兵戴亚斯残骸下方，初步分析排除了设备干扰或残余能源反应的可能。重复，这不是机械信号，探测仪识别为生物特征读数。重复，这不是机械信号……」——黑障第二小队战场清扫报告"}, {"title": "单方交易", "text": "「针对目标玛阿特的多种抢救方案，皆因岚物质导致的多器官衰竭而未能生效，当前目标生存概率已低于0.3%。医疗团队建议启用往生药剂仿制品作为最终方案，将通过诱导神经麻痹，重置并改善岚物质与原生细胞的结合状态，从而改善目标生命体征状况。注射后，目标生理体征将得到稳定，但存在心智崩溃风险，有极高概率仅保留基础应激反应，行为模式或将与“威廉案例”范式相同——即转化为可执行指令的傀儡个体……这或许与队长您所期望的结果不和，但已经是我们所能想到的最佳方案了。」——抢救报告"}, {"title": "丧家之犬", "text": "「我所需要的不是第二个威廉！现在立刻停止对玛阿特植入服从协议的进程，准予其保留自主认知功能。\n洗脑确实能造出温顺的牧羊犬——但牧羊犬可没法自主运用所拥有的经验与知识，以及那由岚物质所给予的共鸣能力，去探寻『遗产』的下落……我们需要的，是一条满怀仇恨的猎犬。\n相信我，丧家之犬最懂得往哪个角落刨食，才能填满自己体内那无处宣泄的仇恨。」——黑曜石内部会议"}, {"title": "落叶需归根", "text": "「我不会忘记我对你们所做的一切，这次回来，也不是为了祈求你们的原谅，只是……想要问一些问题。\n首都运河日落时的水鸟，还会成群飞过芦苇荡吗？呵呵……小时候我总在河畔坐着，看上一整个下午，现在记得它们翅膀划过夕阳的样子，像是在天空撒开一把的金箔，好看极了。\n还有那市集，烤饼的炭火气息，掺着乳香和沙子的味道，真是让人怀念……对了，卖鹰嘴豆汤的那个老婆婆，她的陶罐边是否还围着偷吃的孩子？以前我就是其中一员，从来没被抓到过一次……哦不，这都过去十几年了，肯定是换她的孩子接班了吧？也不知道她身体怎么样了……唉，我有太多问题想问问你们了……\n…………\n我在这座岛上做了太多错事……那些事就像是沙漠之中延绵的沙丘，永远没有抹平的可能。但请再给我一点时间——等岛上的枪声彻底沉默，等那些制造战争的人付出代价后……我会带着你们回到家乡，回到伊吉帝。\n而到了那时候，不是作为战士，只是作为一个从漫长噩梦中醒来的人，我会与你们再次相会……\n请为我留一盏灯吧。」——一段录音"}], "cn": true}, "10103124": {"profile": [{"label": "Affiliation", "value": "The Ashes"}, {"label": "Blood Type", "value": "B"}, {"label": "Height", "value": "186cm"}, {"label": "Specialty", "value": "Wilderness Survival"}], "introduction": "\"Heard Marcus got called up again, by Major William this time! Kid's solid in a fight and reliable, too. Just won't back down. The same attitude that got him in trouble at the academy. Keep that up in the NDF? Matter of time before it bites him.\" —Ex-UNCS Grunt", "stories": [{"title": "April 8, XC 111, Cloudy", "text": "\"Though the war has been over for a decade, spring in Milkhama still feels as grim as it did in my childhood. Today, a small-scale conflict broke out in the welfare home. Sandy insulted Alexander's parents, who died in the war as executioners, so Alexander punched Sandy's nose crooked. They fought until they were pulled apart, covered in blood. The overt war has ended, but its aftermath has not entirely disappeared...\"", "comment": {"by": "Kaidan", "text": "The orphanage... If my father hadn't adopted me, I'd probably have grown up there..."}}, {"title": "July 14, XC 112, Cloudy", "text": "Today marks my first anniversary of serving at the UNCS Desert Base, and it's rest day to boot! The same batch of recruits who came in with me blindfolded me first thing in the morning, dragging me somewhere I had no clue about. I asked at least seven or eight times where the hell we were going, but not a single one of them answered. After about half an hour, they finally told me to stop, and before I knew it, someone kicked me in the back. I barely had time to curse before I went flying face-first into some chillingly refreshing water! So this is what they were up to—those sneaky punks brought me out here to swim..."}, {"title": "October 27, XC 112, Rain", "text": "\"Every time I sit in the cockpit, I feel a sense of emptiness. The connection between the cavalry, Milkhama, and peace has become increasingly blurred in recent years. Was my choice the right one? Is the path I'm taking leading to true peace? What is the truth...?\""}, {"title": "January 1, XC 113, Sunny", "text": "\"Ah, another year has come and gone! I suddenly realized I hadn't written in my diary for almost half a year. Time really flies... So much happened over the past year—some cried, some laughed, some sacrificed, and some were truly remarkable. The truth, still hidden, has slowly started to surface, and peace feels farther away than ever. But one thing's for sure—I'll keep fighting for what I believe in...\""}]}, "10103164": {"profile": [{"label": "Affiliation", "value": "Union of Northern Continental States"}, {"label": "Blood Type", "value": "AB"}, {"label": "Height", "value": "165cm"}, {"label": "所持职业资格证书", "value": "46本"}, {"label": "曾用代号", "value": "***"}], "introduction": "不知何时起，布吕希尔家的继承人小姐身边多了一位总是笑眯眯的女仆。起初，没人认为奥德莉身边出现的生面孔会带来怎样的影响，直到玛汀妮轻描淡写地将奥德莉身边的一切琐事打理得井井有条，甚至开始作为奥德莉的代言人出席重要的作战会议时，众人才意识到这位深得布吕希尔家族信任的女仆也许大有来头。\n于是，无数刺探的手段开始运作，许多人都想以玛汀妮为切入口探寻布吕希尔家族的秘密——然而，与她那个光芒加身的主人不同，玛汀妮的身上总笼罩着层层的迷雾，轻易便能隔绝所有不怀好意的目光。\n在越来越多用以试探的棋子消失在棋盘中后，人们逐渐意识到，也许猎物和猎人的身份从来都是叠加存在的，那位看似无害、总是彬彬有礼随侍于奥德莉身侧的女仆也能轻易将他们逼入绝境……不过玛汀妮对这样的工作早已习以为常，作为布吕希尔家的专业女仆，这都是她应该完成的事务。", "stories": [{"title": "真相Ⅰ", "text": "埃琳娜将密钥交付给了雨果，并在他的面颊上轻吻了一番，这一个简单的把戏，足以让这个木讷的研究员神魂颠倒。\n「这是我在走廊发现的，应该是凶手逃离现场时丢下的……我说，这是不是我们最后的机会了？」\n接过密钥的雨果本还有些犹豫，但在听了埃琳娜的话之后，他下定了决心。\n更何况，此时密钥已经开始了自我销毁的倒计时，也没有留给他犹豫的时间了。\n如果要做选择的话，就必须是现在。\n这样想着，雨果已经坐进了机兵的驾驶舱之中，将密钥插入到了系统，但机舱萤幕上涌现的错误警告表明了一件事——他做出了错误的选择。"}, {"title": "真相Ⅱ", "text": "雨果那家伙有问题……在案发之后，托马斯早早就察觉到了这名研究员的异常，他悄悄地跟了上去，在雨果又一次仓促的转移中，一个不起眼的硬盘掉在了地上。\n托马斯将其拾起的瞬间就明白，这就是研究所中，人们所谈论的密钥。\n如果能把这个密钥带到外面去，在天网或是什么地方卖掉，那下辈子都不用愁了吧……但在此之前，他得搞明白，如何让这上面让人不安的倒计时停下来。\n先前他就听说，研究所大多数的机兵系统都自带解密功能，正巧现在机库里也没有人盯着……"}, {"title": "真相Ⅲ", "text": "「用你机兵的解密系统，把这个玩意上的倒计时停下……记住，别想耍什么花招。」看着托马斯布满血丝的眼睛，埃琳娜明白自己几乎没有什么反抗的可能……也许她能想办法去联络那些安全总署的探员，那时真相会被公之于众，但自己的生命将会是其代价。\n还是按照他说的来吧……埃琳娜颤颤巍巍地将密钥插入了机兵解密系统之中，如果运气好的话，或许她能借助机兵的能力，摆脱这个疯狂的男人也说不定……"}, {"title": "必要之解", "text": "「玛汀妮，你到底在想些什么？你已经通过了作案时间锁定了三名杀死所长的嫌疑人，分别是外聘佣兵托马斯，研究员雨果和实习生埃琳娜，现在不对他们进行控制，还放任他们自由行动，那之后……」\n「但我们的线索并不足以指认凶手不是吗？而且别忘了，夫人给我们的指示是确保密钥内容的完好，而不是找到什么凶手。」\n「但毫无疑问，就是凶手拿走了那份密钥！如果能将其控制，那找到密钥也只是时间问题！」\n「时间问题？没错，但你还记得，密钥马上就会自我销毁吗？这样看来，凶手应该比我们着急得多呢……毕竟他也明白直接使用机兵进行解密，那就会引起机兵的失控与自毁，现在应该赶着去找一个替死鬼吧？运气好的话，还能伪造出『凶手因为擅自解密而死去』的假象。」\n「可这样下去，不是会有一个无辜的人……」\n「我只知道现在的等待能为谜题带来更多的线索，还能缩小嫌疑人的范围，顺带完成夫人的任务……噢？似乎有人破坏了机兵库的监控设备，看来『收束』的时刻就要到来了，让我们也准备好之后的善后工作吧。」"}], "cn": true}, "10103139": {"profile": [{"label": "Affiliation", "value": "DLAF"}, {"label": "Blood Type", "value": "O"}, {"label": "Height", "value": "172cm"}, {"label": "Nickname", "value": "Dawn's Bloom"}], "introduction": "Matilda Rossi, former commander of the 35th Battalion, 1st Mobile Division of the Milkhama Landing Forces, now the Chief Commander of the Island Defense Forces. She is carefree, open-minded, cheerful, confident, and has strong opinions. Occasionally, she may appear overly assertive in disputes, but she genuinely cares for her subordinates and enjoys a good reputation among the lower ranks and civilians, making her a compassionate commander. Additional note: If you don't consider her sloppy nature, her driving style that skirts the edge of regulations, and her tactical inclination toward firepower supremacy... she quite fits the title of \"Flower of the Defense Force.\"", "stories": [{"title": "Primary Exclusion", "text": "Some say the DLAF is currently in an awkward transitional phase. The older generation of DLAF, which rose during the unification period and shone in the border wars, is gradually aging. Meanwhile, the newcomers from the academic background severely lack practical combat experience. Especially after the \"treason\" of Mill and his son, the situation in East Milkhama has become increasingly dire, and the DL cannot find anyone to regain control of the NDF amidst the chaos. This has led many in the DL to worry about who can rise to the occasion, unify the fragmented organization and faction-ridden DLAF, and safeguard the border and East Milkhama's security as the border confrontation intensifies.\nPerhaps those in the Oceanic Conclave each have their own answers, but everyone instinctively excludes that name... \"Matilda Rossi might be competent—but let's leave it at that. The DL is not yet so desperate as to have no one else worth considering. We should be looking at candidates with greater potential.\""}, {"title": "Inactive Division", "text": "Is Matilda Rossi a worthless pilot or commander? The answer is unequivocally no. In fact, contrary to the attitude of certain DL leaders, Matilda enjoys a solid reputation and considerable personal authority within the DLAF. Decorated veterans and rising academy officers alike regard her—at least in matters of military affairs—as an exceptional professional. She fought on the front lines during the border wars and went on to distinguish herself in several armed clashes that followed the war. By any reasonable standard, she represents a critical pillar of the current DLAF. And yet, her path to promotion has been anything but smooth. At one point, she was even reassigned to an idle rear-area department in the homeland—far removed from the front lines and the centers of achievement."}, {"title": "Higher Priority", "text": "The reason Matilda is unpopular among politicians is simple: she is not an obedient officer willing to subordinate herself to the civilian system. The institutional histories of the DLAF and the NDF are fundamentally different. Since its founding, the DL has never allowed a military faction with sufficient political weight to emerge. The armed forces exist strictly as an external instrument of political power, fully subject to civilian command and deployment. Matilda—this \"highly individualistic\" mid-level officer—has repeatedly found ways to resist, reinterpret, or outright bypass civilian decisions in pursuit of what she considers more effective military outcomes. From the standpoint of results, her unauthorized actions have, in most cases, proven the wiser choice. But procedural violations leave paper trails. Over time, these accumulated records became the very tools senators and politicians used to attack her. As a result, Matilda was transferred into \"more important\" positions—positions that conveniently kept her away from the front—and remained politically sidelined for years.", "comment": {"by": "Hardaway", "text": "Ahem... It would be unreasonable to expect proper procedure from someone insane enough to outfit a Light ST with a heavy machine gun."}}, {"title": "Chaotic Talent", "text": "Ultimately, Matilda was pulled into the chaos of Milkhama regardless. What began as a vacation on the island turned abruptly into crisis when unrest triggered by Vesper erupted. The military-political fracture within DL jurisdiction, combined with the rebellion of Mill and his son, sent East Milkhama into rapid freefall. Acting on instinct and training, Matilda immediately assumed command of the disordered defense camp. Drawing on her personal authority, she reunified the island's scattered mobile units and secured the backing of emerging political forces represented by Shawnee. As East Milkhama descended further into instability—and with the NDF watching closely from across the line—even the aging parliamentary holdouts who had initially opposed her appointment were forced to concede. Matilda was approved as the acting DLAF commander of Milkhama Island.\nAt times, even Matilda herself could not help but reflect on the pattern. Always drawn to the center of chaos—perhaps that, too, was a kind of talent."}]}, "10103111": {"profile": [{"label": "Affiliation", "value": "Bounty Hunter"}, {"label": "Blood Type", "value": "O"}, {"label": "Height", "value": "155cm"}, {"label": "Codename", "value": "Canary"}, {"label": "Debts", "value": "1,252,000 (Signed by the Doll Group)"}, {"label": "Partner", "value": "Rebecca Klose"}], "introduction": "\"Canary, Senior Hunter, ST tech/support, Rebecca's partner.\nTogether they've crushed five 30+ ST gangs, cleared 20+ top bounties. Pack platoon-level punch. No direct contact, no custom jobs. \nWant them? Post triple rate - she'll bite. No guarantees.\" —The Hunter's Guide", "stories": [{"title": "Resurrection", "text": "\"Send all the remaining Arashi inhibitors to Ward 41 immediately! First Lieutenant Hicks has specifically warned us that if this girl doesn't make it, our entire department's on the line, got it? Damn it! How the hell did she survive that explosion? If it weren't for the military's orders, no hospital would've even touched a patient like this... This is a mess...\" — Outpatient Recording, XX/XX/XC 100", "comment": {"by": "Medical Staff", "text": "I will never forget the tragic state of that girl. When she was taken to the hospital, we wondered who had placed a lump of coal on a precious hospital bed..."}}, {"title": "Arashium Surges", "text": "\"Unfortunately, we can't create a detailed rehab plan for Melissa. The fact that she survived two years ago was nothing short of a miracle. Our current approach is administering the Arashi inhibitor and monitoring the data, hoping for another miracle. This method has proven effective, so we'll keep at it. And as per your instructions, Lieutenant, none of this data will be submitted to the UNCS Academy of Science and Engineering, including her claims of possessing a unique ST synchronization ability...\" — Outpatient Note, March 31, XC 102", "comment": {"by": "Cicero", "text": "It's such a pity... no, it's tragic that such a precious sample has remained hidden for decades."}}, {"title": "Regular Follow-up", "text": "\"Mr. Hicks, your decision to personally bring your daughter in for regular check-ups each month is a wise one. While traveling back and forth from the southern Parill Desert to White Maple is no easy task, the treatment is essential for her health, and requires our joint efforts... By the way, we've noticed there have been an increasing number of delayed payments from you in the past two years. This isn't exactly appropriate now, wouldn't you agree?\" — Outpatient Recording, March 31, XC 115"}, {"title": "No News at All", "text": "\"Are you kidding me? Hicks is dead?! Send Melissa's file to Winston immediately, he's the new project leader... No, wait... Those files need to be destroyed, otherwise we'll have no way of explaining ourselves out of this to Blair and the others. The data we've been hiding for years is enough to put us on the list... Damn it, Hicks...\" — Outpatient Recording, March 31, XC 118", "comment": {"by": "Alyson", "text": "Only the living get caught in their own flaws. So, who really trapped who, me or Hicks?"}}]}, "10103106": {"profile": [{"label": "Affiliation", "value": "UNCS General Security Administration"}, {"label": "Blood Type", "value": "AB"}, {"label": "Height", "value": "158cm"}, {"label": "Skynet Permissions", "value": "High"}, {"label": "Specialty", "value": "Hacker technology, Electronic games"}, {"label": "▇▇", "value": "Don't expect to know more from here!"}], "introduction": "Ex-Ether Rats ace hacker. Competitive rebel who cracked codes to expose truth. Got tangled in Obsidian/UNCS plots while running Skynet intel. Natalia helped her escape to GSA.\nDon't let the punk student look fool you—she's a digital wizard no one dares ignore.", "stories": [{"title": "Beginning", "text": "Since my father's passing, my mother has done everything she can to keep me out of his study, as if it wasn't the gunfire but the research papers scattered across his desk that led to his death. One day, I couldn't resist—I picked the lock and rummaged through his things, searching for anything related to him, but all I found were piles of incomprehensible reports. As I was about to leave, something caught my eye—a black box buried beneath the mountain of books. It was just another terminal, nothing rare for researchers back then, but it changed everything. That device had the authority to connect to Skynet."}, {"title": "Student Hacker", "text": "Maintaining the minimum attendance and achieving average grades, my campus life remained dull and uneventful even after entering high school. That was because I already knew that everything before my eyes was just the surface layer of this world. The truth—hidden deep beneath, in the sea of intelligence known as \"Skynet\"—was where I truly belonged.\nBut learning alone has its limits, and soon, a special security system stood in my way. \"Can you break through our defenses?\" This challenge letter suddenly appeared in my mailbox and brought me into contact with the \"Ether Rats\" hacker group.", "comment": {"by": "Grant", "text": "What? This girl's amazing hacking skills were actually self-taught?!"}}, {"title": "Panic", "text": "We're the top hacker group in all of Milkhama. Three years ago, I joined the Ether Rats, and since then, we've uncovered all sorts of truths through our hacks. I couldn't help but think, no matter our ages or backgrounds, we all shared the belief that if we kept pushing, we'd break down all information barriers and expose the truth to the world, bringing justice with it. But that very confidence is what led us straight into the trap set by the NDF and Obsidian.", "comment": {"by": "Anonymous Hacker", "text": "I remember the day a bounty for the Ether Rats suddenly appeared on Skynet, and then they disappeared without a trace... It's their own fault for being so stubborn and getting involved with Obsidian."}}, {"title": "The Path of Espionage", "text": "The regulations of the General Security Administration are beyond anything I had imagined. I decided to use my position as an agent to get to the bottom of the NDF and Obsidian conspiracy, but instead, I found myself shackled by even more restrictions... Luckily, the GKD Squad's hijinks have shifted things a bit. Natalia granted me special operations clearance, allowing me to make contact and even provide direct support. No doubt, they've uncovered something crucial. If their goal is to expose the dark secrets hidden deep in Milkhama, helping them achieve that is exactly what I want... But as for whether that's what Natalia really wants, I'm not so sure anymore."}]}, "10103105": {"profile": [{"label": "Affiliation", "value": "UNCS General Security Administration"}, {"label": "Blood Type", "value": "B"}, {"label": "Height", "value": "173cm"}, {"label": "Specialty", "value": "Accordion Performance"}], "introduction": "A woman of mystery, her identity is difficult to pin down. Operates on Skynet under the pseudonym \"Accordion,\" but in truth she serves as an agent of the General Security Administration, working with her partner, Naomi. Both Obsidian and the NDF regard her caution.Her true motives are shrouded in secrecy, while her remarkable beauty and perfect figure bring men to their knees. Shrewd in speech, she carefully controls the flow of information, never allowing her interests to be compromised. A real femme fatale.", "stories": [{"title": "Closing Performance", "text": "If it weren't for the sudden incident, Natalia might have lived a carefree life as a prominent noble. She would've only had to worry about whether her food tasted right, if the fire was warm enough, and whether her potential suitor measured up to her expectations—living the life of a noblewoman, from one privilege to the next.\nHowever, on that day in XC 101, a group of Principality guards stormed the Ovett performance hall. Sir Coronado, sitting in the audience, left Natalia, who was playing the accordion on stage, to face the panic that swept through the crowd."}, {"title": "[Espionage Offenses]", "text": "When Principality authorities told Natalia she'd been arrested for \"espionage offenses,\" she had no idea what the term even meant. It wasn't until then that the truth hit her—her father, so proud of his duchy bloodline, had been working for the UNCS all along. The family's fall from grace was swift—confiscations, arrests, her mother and brother locked away. Just a day before the arrest warrant for her was issued, an old colleague of her father's from the General Security Administration of the UNCS, Sir Coronado, showed up at her door.", "comment": {"by": "Naomi", "text": "This person was supposed to be my immediate superior. Just a month before I joined the intelligence agency, he was suddenly killed at an Ovett base... *sigh* I guess being a spy really is a dangerous profession."}}, {"title": "Accordion", "text": "With the help of her father's former colleagues, Natalia received the protection of the General Security Administration and escaped from the center of the vortex, the Ovett Principality. Determined to rescue her parents, Natalia, nicknamed \"Accordion,\" became a special agent of the GSA. Armed with diligence and talent, she quickly became a key investigator, and through her relentless efforts, the truth about her father's past began to unravel."}, {"title": "▇▇▇▇", "text": "In the year XC 113, Natalia found the name of her father, Sir Coronado, on a contact list intercepted from Obsidian. The secrets of Arashium alloy, Milkhama, the UNCS, and ▇▇▇▇▇▇▇ of Ovett Principality were revealed one by one before Natalia's eyes. After realizing she finally had a chance to rescue her imprisoned father, Natalia set her sights on that embattled island, cut off by boundless ocean.", "comment": {"by": "Naomi", "text": "Strange... How exactly is this file encrypted? What's inside it?"}}]}, "10103175": {"profile": [{"label": "Affiliation", "value": "Obsidian Group"}, {"label": "Blood Type", "value": "A"}, {"label": "Height", "value": "140cm"}, {"label": "Education", "value": "本科辍学"}], "introduction": "「尼尔·昆施泰特这个名字，最初在学界崭露头角时，并非荣耀，而是一根刺。\n在当时所有学者眼中，她都是那个不合时宜的异端。她毫不留情地抨击前人的成果，否定那些被奉为圭臬的理论，也从不因对方的身份、资历或声望而收敛半分。仍是学生的她，曾不止一次在学术会议上夺过主持人的话筒，当众宣称台上众人所交流的理论，不过是科学代谢后残留下来的废物。\n多个机构联合封杀了她，大学也在压力之下将她强制退学。那时的尼尔甚至尚未完成自己的本科学业，便已被整个学界从名册中抹去。\n然而，一切都在她第一次于期刊上发表文章后发生了改变。\n那些曾被她否定的学者与机构，终于不得不重新审视这位被他们驱逐的天才。随着更多前所未闻的学说被提出，随着她的理论一次又一次撕开旧时代的边界，过去所有针对她的封杀，都逐渐显得像是一场迟钝而可笑的误判。到后来，甚至连她的否认本身，都成为了一种荣誉。\n若她生于中世纪，那么她大概会在出生的第一天便被冠以女巫之名，送上火刑架。\n但她生在了一个仍愿意相信科学的时代，便成为了女神。\n她生在了『正确』的时代，也渐渐成为了这个时代所承认、所追随、所代表的『正确』。」——米赫玛自然杂志", "stories": [{"title": "危险", "text": "「尼尔·昆施泰特……她对学术的理解，以及她在科研领域展现出的造诣，或许确实已经走在了这个时代的最前沿。\n这一点，我从不否认。\n但我始终认为，她所主张的科研方式，不应被推崇，更不应被奉为未来的方向。\n如今，越来越多的科研者开始认可她，追随她，甚至模仿她那种不计代价、不问后果，只一味向前推进的研究方式。我对此感到担忧，非常担忧。\n我希望他们能记住一件事。\n在成为科研者之前，我们首先是人。\n我们是某些人的子女，也可能是某些人的父母。我们拥有被牵挂的生命，也牵挂着他人的生命。因此，当我们创造某种事物时，所要思考的不该只是它能否实现，不该只是它是否足够伟大、足够突破、足够改写历史。\n我们更应该思考的是——它会把这个世界带向何处。\n科学不该只是向前。至少，不该是闭着眼睛向前。\n如果每个人都像尼尔·昆施泰特那样，把一切代价都视为可以支付的成本，把一切后果都留给时代自行承担，那么最后，人类或许真的会抵达某个前所未有的地方。\n只是到了那时，我们恐怕再也无法回头。」——沃尔特·纽曼访谈"}, {"title": "始终如一者", "text": "「同盟里有些人称我是天才，但在看过尼尔·昆施泰特的资料之后，我才明白，早在二十余年前，尼尔就已经是那样的天才了。\n而且，与我不同的是，她从未动摇过。\n身为天才的她，从一开始便始终如一。她没有偏离，没有妥协，也没有停下脚步，就这样一路走到了现在。\n我并不是在认可她的科研方式。只是，无论是哪一位科研者，只要真正读过她给出的那些答案，就都很难对尼尔做出彻底的否定。她所抵达的高度，她所撕开的边界，她所证明的一切……都不是一句『错误』或『危险』就能轻易抹去的。\n或许，我们不该再用看待普通人类的方式去看待她。\n嗯……如果这句话听起来像是否认她身为人的部分，那我必须先道歉。这并非我的本意。\n我只是觉得，尼尔更像是一台永不停歇的探究机器。她不因赞美而加速，也不因谴责而停下。她只是持续向前，拆解问题，追索答案，直到抵达某个我们尚无法理解的终点。\n因此，对她的行为轻易做出道德评判，或许并不是明智的决定。\n我们能做的，只有期望，或者说，相信……她最终不会驶向毁灭的方向。」——对黑曜石会议海莉丝发言记录"}, {"title": "滞后的选择", "text": "「尼尔吗……有时候，我会在无人知晓的时候后悔。后悔自己曾将那个问题留给她。\n对于未曾踏足奥维特的人而言，那或许本该是一个无解的难题。一个只能被封存、被回避、被永远搁置在沉默之中的问题。\n可对于尼尔·昆施泰特而言，并不是这样。\n越是了解她，我便越清楚一件事——这个世界上或许存在她尚未解开的谜题，却不存在她无法解开的谜题。\n只要给予她足够的时间，她终究会抵达答案。她会理解它，拆解它，证明它，然后以她一贯的方式，将其公之于世。\n而到了那时，人们或许会将一切归因于她的天才，归因于她不可阻挡的求知欲，归因于她从不回头的脚步。\n但我知道，事情并非如此简单……因为最初，是我将那个问题交到了她手中。是我把钥匙递给了她。\n也是我，亲手为这个世界做出了选择。\n时至今日，我依旧无法确定，那个选择究竟意味着正确，还是只是另一种更漫长的错误。」——弗朗西斯·希迪恩录音记录"}, {"title": "答案", "text": "「喂……喂喂，听得到吗？我是尼尔·昆施泰特。在我所处的这个年代，我大概是唯一一个仍然在乎科学，并愿意为此付出一切努力的家伙。\n至于正在听这段信息的你……我不知道，在你的时代，是否还存在与我相似的人。我的同类，或者说，那个人就是你？很遗憾，我无法给出确切的判断。毕竟，当你听到这些话时，现在的我，应该早已不在人世了。\n我曾否认过我所在世界的一切。它的秩序、权威、自以为正确的常识与结论，我几乎全都否认过。可有趣的是，那些同样否认着我的人，却在某些时刻选择了相信我。\n正因如此，我才留下了这些资料。他们让我明白了一件事——或许，我并不一定要先认可某个人，才有资格选择相信他。这是一个非常暧昧的答案，坦白说，我并不喜欢。\n但如果我想更好地成为我自己，如果我想让这些答案在我死后仍能继续抵达某个地方，那么我就必须承认，这种暧昧也有其存在的价值。所以，听好了。\n我并不要求你认可我，但你必须要做的是——相信我留下的答案。」——尼尔·昆施泰特录音记录"}], "cn": true}, "10103134": {"profile": [{"label": "Affiliation", "value": "Union of Northern Continental States"}, {"label": "Blood Type", "value": "O"}, {"label": "Height", "value": "167cm"}, {"label": "Mercenary ID", "value": "Phantom Pain"}, {"label": "Sync Ratio", "value": "92%"}, {"label": "Subject ID", "value": "Σ-04"}], "introduction": "Individual identification code \"Phantom Pain,\" a mysterious mercenary who suddenly appeared after the Blair Rebellion. Her true identity is Aynis Newman, the daughter of Dr. Newman, who was declared deceased many years ago. Under the arrangement of UNCS GSA Director Rosemary Jean, she returned to Milkhama under the name of her late mother, \"Ophelia.\" A new generation Hyper-Aptamer with an excellent Sync Ratio, she is willful, arrogant, and rebellious, seemingly holding many secrets. Her actions and objectives are entirely unknown, but the only certainty is her intense hostility toward Kaidan Newman.", "stories": [{"title": "Aynis Newman", "text": "\"Today, Aynis snuck into the Research Institute again, hiding in the food delivery cart to evade the guards... With such strong curiosity and initiative, I really don't know which side this child takes after more. Fortunately, Goman discovered her quickly and prevented her from seeing those horrifying experiments. I'm not yet prepared to explain all of this to her. Although Aynis tearfully explained that she just wanted to help me, Ophelia uncharacteristically became very angry. She never inquires about my research, but she absolutely does not want her daughter involved in it... In this regard, I share the same sentiment.\" —Walter Newman Related Recovery Data Entry 13255"}, {"title": "Another \"Prototype\"", "text": "\"Aynis and Kaidan have made contact. Although neither of them confirmed each other's identity, this brief exchange has already gone against my initial expectations. I had planned to arrange a proper meeting for them to officially become family once everything settled down, but this sudden incident disrupted my plans... Even worse, the activated Nova-Frame reacted to Aynis, with sensors capturing unprecedented high values. This means that not only Kaidan, but even Aynis has the potential to become a 'Prototype'... It is the worst possibility—one I should have foreseen, yet never wished to face.\" —Walter Newman Related Recovery Data Entry 34711", "comment": {"by": "Kaidan", "text": "So the girl from that time was her... That was the only time we met. Looking back, it must have been my father's deliberate attempt to prevent further contact between us. It was to protect the secret of the Hyper-Aptamer and to protect all of us."}}, {"title": "Hostage", "text": "\"I failed. Blair somehow obtained the data that was supposed to be deleted, and discovered Aynis's potential as a Hyper-Aptamer. He also uncovered my secret plan for escape. The forced transfer of Ophelia and Aynis under the guise of a 'safety drill' was his last warning to me. Perhaps I should give up here... However, the fate of Kaidan and the Diaz sisters also depends on my choice. Hmm...? Who could it be at this hour? Aynis? What are you doing here? What? My birthday? Just for that? ...\nNo, thank you, good girl. Don't cry. It will be all right. Daddy promises... I will protect all of you, no matter what...\" —Walter Newman Related Recovered Data Entry 83906", "comment": {"by": "Anonymous User", "text": "Filthy liar."}}, {"title": "∑-04", "text": "\"Test concluded, ∑-04 emerged the victor, ∑-07's cockpit completely shattered. Logistics team, remember to clean up thoroughly... I never expected such an outcome. It took over six years to complete the entire Hyper-Aptamer Renovation, and we had no expectations for ∑-04. However, during the field test, her Sync Ratio reached an astonishing 92%. I've never seen such a high value in anyone outside Valkyrie. Is this due to the individual's innate potential, or have we inadvertently grasped the key to technical iteration? Either way, it means we still have hope for a reversal. According to the latest intelligence from Milkhama, Governor Blair probably won't hold out much longer. I must produce results quickly... If what that agent said is true, the General Security Administration should be willing to protect us. Before that, I must find a way to address ∑-04's rebellious and disobedient nature. Hopefully, increasing 'authority' can eliminate her instability as a weapon.\" —Hyper-Aptamer 9th Research Institute Experiment Record", "comment": {"by": "GSA Operative", "text": "Test Subject ∑-04 has been confirmed for retrieval and is expected to be deployed directly to Milkhama after adjustments are completed. Additionally, based on personal preference, the operational codename has been designated as \"Ophelia.\""}}]}, "10103153": {"profile": [{"label": "Affiliation", "value": "Dawnstar League"}, {"label": "Blood Type", "value": "B"}, {"label": "Height", "value": "162cm"}, {"label": "Research Results", "value": "An implantable pseudo-neural interface based on nano-scale Arashium Alloy."}, {"label": "Prosthetic Augmentation Progress", "value": "Right Eye (Self-modified)"}, {"label": "Warning", "value": "Do not accept any form of experimental invitation from this individual!"}], "introduction": "\"'Paloma, a genius scientist specializing in the fusion of mechanical and neural medicine, transferred to the Reversion Squad due to a few minor misunderstandings. She is now an indispensable sniper meister, a well-behaved research elite, and Captain Ada's trusted support...'\nThe above description is a self-report provided by the surveillance target and is of limited reference value. The following supplemental notes are provided accordingly:\n1. The target was transferred to the Reversion Squad due to the unauthorized use of Obsidian technology for human modification. To date, she continues to develop portions of the related theoretical technologies.\n2. The target demonstrates excellent task completion capability, but frequently acts without authorization, resulting in unnecessary collateral damage.\n3. The target has repeatedly accessed critical databases without permission and altered stored data. While the outcomes are often optimized, the scale of these modifications has significantly disrupted subsequent research processes.\nAdditional note: Statistical analysis indicates that when operating alongside Lieutenant Sapientia, the frequency of the above issues is markedly reduced.\"—Routine Oversight Committee Report on the Reversion Squad", "stories": [{"title": "Origin", "text": "\"Paloma? Of course I remember her. Five years isn't nearly long enough to forget such a peculiar child. When we first met, she was a destitute young girl with no one to rely on, scraping by on government subsidies and a patchwork of part-time jobs just to keep studying. Thankfully, she truly did possess the talent—and the luck—to change her circumstances. Her academic performance and research results stood out sharply among her peers, earning her the attention of the Cognitionis family... yes, that renowned academic family. It sounds enviable, doesn't it? But as I said, Paloma was always an unusual child. She repeatedly refused the Cognitionis family's support and even mocked them to their faces, accusing them of monopolizing research resources and appropriating others' scientific achievements. I remember breaking out in a cold sweat at the time. I was certain her academic career had ended then and there.\nYet her classmate—Sapientia, the eldest daughter of the Cognitionis family—stepped in. She calmed the family's anger and held a long, private conversation with Paloma. I don't know what was said between them. I only know that afterward, Paloma became part of the Cognitionis family, and the two of them gradually grew as close as sisters.\nUnfortunately, I retired before they graduated. I only heard that they went through many hardships before eventually heading to Milkhama Island. For researchers, it's a place where risk and opportunity walk hand in hand. I can only hope they're doing well.\" —Interview with Renowned Neurologist Clay Stig"}, {"title": "Different Path", "text": "\"Boss, it's done! Those morons at Cognitionis never realized we replaced the core power unit. Their grand public experiment collapsed in disgrace—and Sapientia was caught in the blast—she even lost her arm. The police? Completely fooled. Took the bait and ran off in the wrong direction. Now all we have to do is— ...Wait. What was that sound? Wh-What are you doing here?! Paloma—how did you fin—ngh!? Aaaah—AAAAAAH!!!\n...\n...\nHeh. The machine's still running. So you can hear me, can't you?\nI don't care what your grudge against the Cognitionis family is. I just don't understand this one thing. Why her? Why did it have to be Sapientia? The day before the experiment, she was so excited. She said she finally had the chance to use technology to make this miserable world a little less awful... Of course. Creatures like you would never understand that. So here's the bad news. Thanks to the Obsidian Group's newest breakthroughs, I've already found a way to save her. The technique still needs refinement, though. Which means I need some hardy, long-lasting little lab rats.\nYou're not trying to run, are you? A rat that escapes the lab isn't a test subject anymore—it's vermin. And vermin get put down.\"\n— Connor & Co. Safehouse No. 3 Communications Log", "comment": {"by": "Sapientia", "text": "\"Obsidian does indeed command technologies that are advanced—and profoundly unsettling—but none of them come without a price... Paloma, even for my sake, you should never have struck a bargain with such demons.\""}}, {"title": "Reverse Recruit", "text": "\"Subject No. 49, Paloma, was arrested and tried a year ago for illegal experiments and intentional harm. Logically, she should have been sentenced to several years in prison, but instead, she was transferred to the Reversion Squad to atone for her crimes. It seems that some influential figures, beyond my reach, have taken a liking to her talents. Coincidentally, the previous squad member who died in action also had the codename 'Paloma'... If this is a joke of fate, it is indeed a dark one.\nHowever, the subsequent period of observation yielded unexpected results. Her actual situation was much better than I initially anticipated. Perhaps it is due to her exceptional ST piloting skills, or maybe it is thanks to the Shelter provided by the current captain, Ada Diaz. She has even become more free and more dangerous... The special forces' authority has given her more opportunities to experiment with those mysterious studies involving arashi material and human integration. Fortunately, this all changed with the recovery and joining of Sapientia Cognitionis—the regular technical exchanges with Obsidian have ceased, and her destructive behavior during missions has been curbed.\nYet, there remains an indelible unease in my heart... In the past, she was willing to use her own right eye as renovation material for experiments. Will she truly give up her research and reform? Perhaps more observation is needed to truly understand this volatile and dangerous genius.\" —Log of a Senior Agent of the Oversight Committee"}, {"title": "Pure", "text": "\"This morning, I received a complaint from the Research Bureau—the third this month... same story as always. Paloma again. This time, she breached the system of the DLAF's 44th Research Institute's system and forcibly initiated an unauthorized live-fire exercise, pitting herself against a swarm of PAMS-equipped test units. The result: more than half of the machines rendered inoperable, and Paloma herself sustaining minor injuries. Fortunately, the combat data proved highly valuable, and Paloma later submitted several concrete and viable proposals for ST improvements. On that basis, the incident was ultimately resolved with nothing more than a formal complaint.\nEven after reviewing her past through official records, I still cannot fully understand why she insists on expressing her curiosity toward people—or technology—through such overtly aggressive means... Perhaps that is precisely why she is the most unadulterated among us, and the one best suited to the Reversion Squad.\" —Excerpt from a report by Leopold Ashford, Vice Captain of the Reversion Squad"}]}, "10103150": {"profile": [{"label": "Affiliation", "value": "NERV"}, {"label": "Blood Type", "value": "Unknown"}, {"label": "Height", "value": "Unknown"}, {"label": "Likes", "value": "Reading"}], "introduction": "Rei Ayanami, the Evangelion Unit-00 pilot from another world, and the First Child of Evangelion. She is quiet and reserved, rarely speaking, but always steps up in battle to protect her allies. During the Leviathan invasion on Milkhama Island, Rei Ayanami performed a crucial role, learning to pilot Arashium STs and, under extreme circumstances, protecting her teammates.", "stories": [{"title": "A Calm Girl", "text": "\"It's hard to imagine how a girl her age managed to master so many abilities and tactical skills for piloting STs... When she appeared on the battlefield, we thought we were going to rescue her, but in the end, she was the one who protected us... Although I know that piloting STs has become an instinct deeply ingrained in the blood of the Milkhaman people, a gifted girl like her really is rare... Could she be the rumored special experimental subject that escaped from the laboratory in West Milkhama?\" — Account of a DLAF soldier"}, {"title": "Otherworldly Visitor", "text": "\"Officer Matilda says she and her companions come from a completely different alternate world... Is this official statement for real? That said, judging by how they fight, the official explanation somehow seems credible. I wonder what a state their world must be in for such young children to be piloting STs. Not that the situation here is much better... I hope we see peace again soon. Then maybe they can get back the childhood that was stolen from them.\" — Account of a DLAF soldier"}, {"title": "Dogged Stand", "text": "\"I've read Lieutenant Hardaway's combat report. In the battle against that Leviathan, she managed to stand her ground for so long, solo! It's unbelievable. Even seasoned pilots wouldn't remain so calm in such an environment, right? Was it her determination to protect her comrades that kept her going? I'm curious to know if they faced battles every day in their original world, just like in Milkhama, and what kind of enemies they encountered... The latest news says Commander Matilda disobeyed orders and went to rescue them. I hope they can defeat the enemy and return safely.\" — Account of a DLAF soldier"}, {"title": "At All Costs", "text": "\"I heard that the Logistics Equipment Department and Obsidian have created a special ST for this child so she can participate in the decisive battle at Milthus Port... I'm not sure whether to envy or to pity her. I heard that in her original world, she piloted something much larger than ours, an Evangelion unit or something... Imagine if we brought one of those over here... But in any case, going to the battlefield is a dangerous thing. We can't afford to slack off. We have to give it our all to defeat Leviathan!\" — Account of a DLAF soldier"}]}, "10103107": {"profile": [{"label": "Affiliation", "value": "Union of Northern Continental States"}, {"label": "Blood Type", "value": "AB"}, {"label": "Height", "value": "166cm"}, {"label": "Physical Status", "value": "Healthy"}, {"label": "Current Military Rank", "value": "Major"}, {"label": "Nickname", "value": "Valkyrie"}], "introduction": "\"Rosa Diaz, UNCS's Valkyrie ace! Beauty and skill made her a military idol. But beyond the promos and press? Pure mystery. What's her real story? More to come...\" —Milkhama Entertainment Weekly", "stories": [{"title": "Various Labels", "text": "If there is one name that epitomizes the apex of ST mastery, it has to be \"Rosa Diaz.\" As the highly lauded \"Valkyrie\" of the NDF, Rosa has become a living symbol for the organization. With an impeccable record, sharp skills, and a poised elegance, she's gained a loyal following both within the NDF and even among their enemies. However, no matter how many halos the outside world puts on Rosa, her response is always one of hostility and indifference... \"I would rather not have been given such power from the beginning...\" With that, she vanished, her secrets buried under the weight of public speculation."}, {"title": "Fate Descends", "text": "Rosa knows all too well the cost of the praise she receives. She can control STs perfectly, being a Hyper-Aptamer who can directly resonate with Arashium alloy using her brainwaves. Still, this has also made her a natural-born test subject... However, the cruel cost of being a test subject is not entirely borne by Rosa but also by her sister, Ada Diaz, and the other girls brought in based on Diaz's blueprint... Needles, electrodes, prosthetics, and various experimental drugs... Rosa lay there in her glass cage, witnessing time and time again everything the UNCS did to those girls, knowing there was nothing she could do but climb into an ST and crush the coalition forces one enemy at a time, driven by that elusive promise.", "comment": {"by": "Naomi", "text": "Not long after the Hyper-Aptamer project was proposed, Dr. Newman plotted to falsify data and terminate the project. However, with the discovery of the Diaz sisters, this attempt was ultimately thwarted under military pressure."}}, {"title": "Unending Nightmare", "text": "\"As long as the enemies of the NDF disappear from this island, both STs and pilots will lose their basic foundation, and Hyper-Aptamer research will naturally come to a halt.\" To uphold this unrealistic lie, Rosa became the Valkyrie. However, the stronger she became, the more necessary the research became. Behind the countless lines of incredible battle data was the deception and cruelty of the NDF, as well as the withering and despair of those girls... until her unexpected breakthrough—Cicero's escape, Dr. Newman's death, and the disappearance of her sister, finally caused Rosa to awaken."}, {"title": "In the Face of Death", "text": "The enemies of the NDF are endless, and she is no exception. She could have been a savior to those girls, but in the end, she indirectly advanced the plan... Three days after Ada's disappearance, Rosa returned from the border. Blair used his authority to pardon her for her unauthorized action. However, Rosa will no longer be blinded by such \"grace\"...\nNow, only those girls remain, and Rosa has made her decision—even if the final cost is death, she will redeem their shattered fate... Even if it means nothing more than a fleeting moment, like a blooming flower that fades in an instant.", "comment": {"by": "Sylvie", "text": "Rosa did nothing wrong. She was our savior, our hope... Even though she's passed away, every girl she saved will remember the way she bloomed in the end, just like the Epiphyllum."}}]}, "10103154": {"profile": [{"label": "Affiliation", "value": "The Epiphyllum"}, {"label": "Blood Type", "value": "AB"}, {"label": "Height", "value": "167cm"}, {"label": "Sync Ratio", "value": "99%"}], "introduction": "After the Blair Rebellion, Rosa Díaz reawakened in the Laboratory of the Reversion Squad. Due to radical Experiment plans and intentional external Interference, she experiences some upgrades in memory and self-awareness obstacles. However, she has gained a stronger Arashi Matter resonance ability than before... Although her appearance and demeanor remain unchanged from the past, her way of viewing her companions and her mindset in facing her tumultuous past have quietly changed through interactions with new companions. Now, the only thing Rosa Díaz looks forward to is reclaiming her sister and a reunion and parting with Epiphyllum and that reckless mercenary.", "stories": [{"title": "Blueprint", "text": "\"Rosa Diaz—the Valkyrie of the UNCS, the blueprint of the Hyper-Aptamer Project, a legend among legends... and yet, in the end, she became someone who sought to shoulder everything, only to be betrayed by everything in return. For her, perhaps death would have been the easier conclusion. Tragically, she was denied even that—true death itself remains beyond her reach. I believe the UNCS—more precisely, the Blair administration—made a grave error in its handling of Rosa Diaz. They were far too eager to convert this heaven-sent creation into immediate combat power, and in doing so, brought about their own backlash... like someone grasping for a blade in haste, only to slice open their own hand. Such incidents are, regrettably, not uncommon within certain internal departments of our own organization. Even so, Rosa's fate should stand as a warning to those who would repeat the same mistake. Therefore, I propose that I personally step forward to establish contact with the other groups currently searching for Rosa Diaz—extending favor where necessary, while securing our objectives in the process.\" —Excerpt from a meeting recording at Obsidian Headquarters"}, {"title": "Surpass", "text": "\"I believe our experiment has reached the edge of ethical taboo, as we are creating a new life form that surpasses the realm of humanity. However, the Valkyrie, as a weapon, will still carry human emotions, making her more uncontrollable than any conventional weapon. Therefore, in the subsequent plan advancement, erasing her memory and consciousness should be prioritized. Although we still do not fully understand how human consciousness and memory systems operate, we should at least retain the means to counteract her being out of control... Piloting STs... Since the Valkyrie was born for this, let the ST be her cage.\" —Internal document from the UNCS Laboratory"}, {"title": "Determination", "text": "\"After a long and exhausting pursuit, we have finally uncovered new leads—regarding Rosa's whereabouts, and the truth behind the experiment all those years ago... It is now painfully clear that the Dawnstar League is engaged in the very same practices as the UNCS. Once again, we may find ourselves standing against superpowers that control half the world... And if Ada Diaz also chooses to oppose us, then this mission will become even more arduous. I do not expect everyone to involve themselves in a rescue effort with so little hope of success. All of this began because of me and my father; it is a burden that should rightfully be borne by me alone. Therefore, if any of you choose to withdraw at this point, I will hold no one at fault.\" —Meeting record from GKD Parcel Service", "comment": {"by": "Rosa: Judgment", "text": "\"You barely escaped that catastrophe alive, and yet you still insist on throwing yourself back into this disaster... You really do enjoy making trouble for yourself—just like that foolish girl, Sylvie...\""}}, {"title": "Stranger", "text": "\"When she wakes and is forced to face that past, it will be unbearably difficult... facing my existence as well. Watching the person she once tried so desperately to protect become what I am now—will she feel disappointment, regret... or will she do what she always did, blaming everything on herself and bearing fate's imposed burden alone? Heh. I think I finally understand how she felt back then. And yet, even knowing that what I'm about to do runs counter to her wishes, I cannot stand by and watch her continue to wither away. Besides, I am no longer the child who could only hide beneath her protection. I will bring something of sufficient weight to the table—enough to purchase a way to save her—even if that places me on the opposite side of her path... I hope my sister can forgive my stubbornness...\" —Communication log from a Dawnstar League laboratory", "comment": {"by": "Rosa: Judgment", "text": "\"...Wait for me, Ada. I will get you out of here—no matter what it takes. We'll go home together.\""}}]}, "10103133": {"profile": [{"label": "Affiliation", "value": "Union of Northern Continental States"}, {"label": "Blood Type", "value": "AB"}, {"label": "Height", "value": "170cm"}, {"label": "Codename", "value": "\"M\""}], "introduction": "Rosemary Jean, code-named \"M,\" also known as \"Madam.\" She is one of the most legendary agents in UNCS history and a seasoned bureaucrat holding multiple powerful positions, including GSA Director and Acting Viceroy of Milkhama. With the prestige she built in domestic affairs and intel warfare, Rosemary and her bureaucratic faction rapidly ascended in the post-war decade, gradually breaking the monopoly of political resources held by military oligarchs and traditional political families, and fostering the rise of a new wave of rising political stars.", "stories": [{"title": "Fresh Wave", "text": "\"Sharp vision, a solid record, decisive methods, and refined leadership... It comes as no surprise that she will become the new helmsman of West Milkhama. Her judgment in personnel matters is particularly astonishing. Unproven island hackers. Foreign prisoners of complex background. Individuals with questionable records and diagnosed personality disorders. Alongside them, the mercenary outfits and entrenched local families of Milkhama Island... Due to classification restrictions, the author cannot yet present the full account of how this legendary director swept through the political arena, but judging from her personnel philosophy and political tactics alone, it is precisely her willingness to cut across convention—to operate at oblique angles—that allows her to outmaneuver traditional politicians. In doing so, she has injected rare new momentum into the UNCS political sphere, long monopolized by the military and aristocracy.\" —Rosemary's Legend", "comment": {"by": "Naomi", "text": "An untested remote island hacker? Heh-heh... Noted. Wait for the UNCS investigator to come knocking at your door. Good luck!"}}, {"title": "Wrist", "text": "\"The current situation surprises me not in the slightest—it's all because my dear committee members somehow believed that a handful of military restriction clauses could stop Rosemary. We've struggled against this old woman for years—do we really still fail to understand her resolve and methods? Look at the NDF forces stationed on the island. They're a farce. They think that refusing cooperation somehow restrains her. In reality, all they've done is handcuff themselves. Even the Electric Eels, the Luno Family, and the nobodies from the GKD Parcel Service are speaking up on the NDF's behalf—and their appearances are more effective than official deployments. At this rate, one day the island's bandits, mercenaries, and even armored units will become Rosemary's private guard, while the military department congratulates itself on a job well done.\" —UNCS Internal Meeting Record", "comment": {"by": "UNCS Colonel", "text": "Political factions and war maniacs come and go, but in the end, they paved the way for someone like Rosemary, who comes from a purely bureaucratic system... The political climate of the UNCS is about to change!"}}, {"title": "Vengeance", "text": "The conflict between Rosemary and the military predates Milkhama by many years. Rumors persist that during the Battle of Milthus—the engagement that reshaped Milkhama Island's future—the GSA, with Rosemary serving as wartime intelligence officer, had already decrypted information confirming Obsidian and DL troop concentrations in Milthus. For reasons still unknown, this intelligence was never delivered to the landing force. The result was a catastrophic NDF failure—one that altered not only Milkhama's history, but arguably world history itself. This unresolved grievance ignited a prolonged internal struggle between the UNCS General Security Administration and the NDF. When Blair returned to power, his first directive was the systematic purge of all GSA forces on Milkhama. Rosemary exploited the escalating three-way confrontation, gradually extending her reach beyond the GSA—until she finally settled accounts with Blair on Milkhama, completing a vendetta nearly twenty years in the making. —Special Segment, Inside the NDF", "comment": {"by": "Naomi", "text": "These ridiculous conspiracy theories need to stop! The truth is that Blair, the commander of the landing forces, acted on his own, imprisoned and plotted against the agent transmitting intelligence to the front lines, launched an unauthorized assault on Milthus, and was wiped out by the enemy. On the day of Blair's death, the GSA transmitted the council's order to \"bring back Blair Bluecher.\" His death resulted from Arnold's directive to encircle and intercept, combined with Raven Bluecher's refusal to comply. This was a strictly personal incident—nothing more!"}}, {"title": "Friend or Foe", "text": "\"What makes her truly terrifying is that we can't see her desires. We don't know what she wants—nor what she intends to do. Her record only tells you this: a civilian born during the baby boom. After her father, a newspaper editor, died, she inherited his work. To support a sick mother and a young brother, she became an investigative journalist for better pay. A few minor but influential cases led her into intelligence work, after which she was thrown into the economic investigation division like expendable fodder. By the time she resurfaced, she had become the old director's 'black goat.' No one remembers how she climbed that far. And when everyone finally realized what was happening, even the old director had been personally dealt with—yet no one inside the agency believed she had betrayed him. The evidence was clear. The methods, precise. The motive remains a mystery. She can be an enemy. She can be a friend. But she must be neither. That is what makes her truly dangerous.\" —Interview with a Retired GSA Agent"}]}, "10103157": {"profile": [{"label": "Affiliation", "value": "Dawnstar League"}, {"label": "Blood Type", "value": "A"}, {"label": "Height", "value": "166cm"}, {"label": "Research Results", "value": "Arashi Neural Intelligence and Its Differential Evolution Algorithm"}, {"label": "Registered Pet", "value": "Autonomous Support Terminal \"Guggle\""}], "introduction": "The eldest daughter of the renowned Cognitionis academic family, the youngest expert in arashium neural intelligence systems, once regarded by the academic community of the DL as the next rising star after Elise—one who could revolutionize bionic intelligence framework theory. However, due to certain private reasons, she actively joined the Reversion Squad, working as an ST technician on Milkhama Island.\nIntelligent and sincere, diligent yet reserved—an unassuming academic type. This is the consensus among her colleagues. But those who know her well dismiss that outright—\"Sapi sometimes comes up with ideas even I wouldn't think of, then quietly puts them into action... If you think she's just a well-behaved top student, you'd better be ready for a surprise!\"", "stories": [{"title": "Family", "text": "In the DL scientific community, the Cognitionis Family's reputation precedes them. As a historical and influential scholarly family, they possess a vast array of academic, political, and economic resources, which helps them to maintain a long-standing symbiotic relationship with the military-industrial complex. Their position seemed unshakable for years, but all of this changed completely with the development of arashi matter technology. Amidst the intense competition in this emerging field, they lost the upper hand. Now the family needs decisive talent and technology to reestablish authority, and Sapientia, who has shown exceptional talent since childhood, is highly anticipated.\nSince she became aware, Sapientia's life has been almost entirely spent in learning. Inundated with study and research, and with all social interactions subject to strict screening by her family, her childhood environment was oppressive and suffocating. To give her some relief, she mustered the courage to tell her first lie. Under the guise of researching Bionic Intelligence Frame technology, she created her own intelligent mechanical friend, Guggle.\nAs luck would have it, this small act of rebellion brought unexpectedly fruitful results. In the process of continuously modifying and improving Guggle, Sapientia developed a real passion for research, leading her eventually to some remarkable scientific achievements. She soon became a rising star of the DL academic community and even won a place on the most advanced AI Bionics research team at the prestigious Leibniz University. Her life is about to enter a new chapter—away from the family, she can finally break free from long-standing constraints—and will soon meet what turns out to be a lifelong friend."}, {"title": "Upheaval", "text": "Ever since they first met, Sapientia and Paloma were rivals when it came to tech—a dynamic that did not change even after the two became close friends. This healthy competition only served to amplify her passion and natural talent. Inspired by Paloma's pseudo-neural components, Sapientia successfully developed a brand-new differential evolution Bionic AI modeled after Guggle. The Cognitionis family were ecstatic, but from others it attracted animosity.\nIn September, XC 116, a severe accident of unknown origin occurred during a public experiment at Leibniz University, resulting in the loss of Sapientia's left arm. For her protection and to facilitate an investigation, the family chose to isolate her, cutting off contact with the outside world. Aside from her family and designated medical staff, Guggle was once again her only companion.\nHowever, this closed treatment did not yield the expected results—due to arashi particle contamination from the accident, the muscles on Sapientia's left side suffered a degree of atrophy, and her recovery was painfully slow. The residual arashi particles obstructed neural signals, rendering existing prosthetic limbs ineffective. \nAs a month passed, Sapientia's spirits continued to sink... It was then that a special envoy from Obsidian suddenly appeared in the ward, bringing advanced prosthetic technology and new medical treatments—along with the news that Paloma had been arrested and imprisoned for illegal experimentation and intentional injury."}, {"title": "Abyss", "text": "Having just adapted to her new prosthetics, Sapientia applied to join the Reversion Squad—a move the Cognitionis family naturally opposed. Sapientia, however, had already prepared a convincing excuse—Milkhama Island is the source of arashi matter and the cutting-edge testing ground for the Bionic Intelligence Frame. Only there can she truly perfect her technology and maintain the family's academic prestige.\nIt didn't take long for Sapientia to first set foot on Milkhama with Guggle in tow. But when she disembarked, what awaited her was not her long-missed friend, but the contact from Obsidian headquarters. As the price for stopping the ongoing collaboration between Paloma and Obsidian, Sapientia was forced to become an informant within the Reversion Squad, tasked with providing regular test data on Ada.\nShe resisted, almost subduing the Obsidian contact, but her prosthetic suddenly went out of control due to a backdoor command left by the contact. Only then did she realize this had all been a trap from the start. Now, struggling to maintain a facade of calm while desperately searching for a way out, Sapientia anxiously awaited a new opportunity.\nWhether by luck or misfortune, this opportunity soon materialized: the Reversion Squad took on Rosa Diaz—someone whose value to Obsidian far outweighed that of both Sapientia and Paloma combined.", "comment": {"by": "Paloma", "text": "Sapi, you idiot!!! Why didn't you explain it to me earlier!!"}}, {"title": "Daybreak", "text": "Through the concerted efforts of many, the Reversion Paradox centered around Rosa Díaz ultimately avoided its worst-case scenario. However, the Oceanic Conclave was never going to remain indifferent. A joint investigation task force, formed by the Oversight Committee and the Defense Force Headquarters, intervened and ordered Veronica to escort Sapientia—the direct instigator of the incident—to their base for interrogation.\nDespite this, Sapientia felt a sense of clarity she hadn't known for a long time. The nanobots implanted in her prosthetics had been destroyed by the power of the Hyper-Aptamer, and Obsidian had lost its leverage over her and Paloma. Following the upheaval, the members of the Reversion Squad finally opened up to one another, and the six, each of whom had started with their own hidden agendas, were now gradually moving toward the same destination, together... Sapientia no longer needed to force herself to make impossible sacrifices; her only focus now was protecting this hard-won home and helping Ada and Rosa break free from the shackles fate had imposed upon on them. \nThis is her atonement for the past—and her hope for the future.", "comment": {"by": "Veronica", "text": "Though she's weak, lying on the hospital bed, she still seems much more at ease... Perhaps for her, life is only just now beginning."}}]}, "10103120": {"profile": [{"label": "Affiliation", "value": "Lollipop Machine Shop"}, {"label": "Blood Type", "value": "O"}, {"label": "Height", "value": "156cm"}, {"label": "Preference", "value": "Mechanical Modification, Candy Collection"}, {"label": "Masterpiece", "value": "Mechanical Assistant \"Pochy\""}], "introduction": "Young mechanic chasing Milkhama dreams. Prefers mods to repairs and is fascinated by Arashium. Runs Lollipop Machine Shop with one rule: top service means she mods your ST her way.", "stories": [{"title": "Wrench", "text": "Ever since I was little, I just loved hanging around my dad. He was always tinkering with all kinds of machines, stuff that most people would never find interesting. But somehow, he could make it all come to life. I remember one time, I couldn't resist anymore and decided to try fixing a clock and a microwave at home just like he did. Except, I had no idea how to put them back together. So, there I was, surrounded by pieces, and Mom was about to lose it. But Dad, with his big grin, just grabbed his wrench and took care of it like it was nothing. That's when I found out he used to be a machinist on Milkhama Island."}, {"title": "Gummies", "text": "Whenever I asked my dad about his days as a machinist on Milkhama, he'd just shake his head, that tired, knowing look in his eyes, before telling me not to waste my time thinking about that place. \"The world's best, most cutting-edge STs are manufactured and invented there, but it's also where the most brutal, most horrifying ST battles take place.\" I remember his serious expression as he spoke, \"It's a paradise for machinists, but a hell for ordinary people.\"", "comment": {"by": "Naomi", "text": "Since the technological innovation of Arashium, Milkhama has become the preferred location for ST manufacturing and ST technology research due to its proximity to raw material sources. Calling this place a machinists' paradise is no exaggeration."}}, {"title": "Bolt", "text": "I still can't figure out what makes Milkhama so special—why my dad both fears it and can't seem to stay away. But ever since then, it's felt like my fate's been tied to that damn island. Before long, I was shadowing him at the shop, running errands, learning the ropes. By sixteen, I had my own machinist's license. When I told him I wanted to head to Milkhama to see the latest STs for myself, he didn't say a word. But the next morning, I found an old bolt from Milkhama, the kind he'd brought back years ago, slipped in with my stuff. No words, just that bolt. I guess he knew I'd made up my mind to go.", "comment": {"by": "Grant", "text": "Tsk, that girl keeps that bolt right on the counter in her shop... Doesn't she know how tough it is to get your hands on something made of Arashium alloy? What the hell was her old man even doing back then?!"}}, {"title": "Lollipop", "text": "Dad wasn't wrong—Milkhama Island really is a paradise for machinists. With the money I earned from doing side gigs, I saved up enough to open my own repair shop on this island! I'm seriously pumped to check out this new material they call \"Arashium.\" I swear, once I get my hands on it, I'll make some insane upgrades! And now that I've got a new direction to expand my business, my shop's gonna be one-of-a-kind. Dad always said a good name is half the battle, so... I'm calling it the Lollipop Machine Shop!"}]}, "10102102": {"profile": [{"label": "Affiliation", "value": "Dawnstar League"}, {"label": "Blood Type", "value": "A"}, {"label": "Height", "value": "165cm"}], "introduction": "\"Shawnee Russell, East Milkhama security chief, DLAF rising star. People see law and order. Don't see the iron fist. Opponents quit races early. Watch that sweet smile. It hides teeth.\" —Naomi's Brief to Arnold", "stories": [{"title": "Evening Broadcast", "text": "\"Good evening, ladies and gentlemen. Tonight, we introduce Miss Shawnee Russell, the newly appointed security chief of East Milkhama. Since stepping into the political arena last year, Miss Russell has attracted significant attention. Her youth and striking appearance have earned her considerable support, but there are whispers questioning her competence and the potential connections behind her rise. In tonight's program, we'll hear from those closest to her, giving you a closer look at this rising star in Milkhama's political landscape.\" — DL TV Program \"Milkhama News\""}, {"title": "Teaching Evaluation", "text": "\"Ah... Shawnee has been my student for a long time. As a teacher, my expectations are very high... but Shawnee is a rare kind of polymath... no, more like a genius par excellence. Of course, her family background plays a heavy part in this. After all, her father is also quite a figure within the DL. But don't get me wrong, she's not the kind of spoiled princess who simply rides on her family's coattails. She has a talent that has been carefully nurtured and the awareness to use wisely.\" — Evaluation of Shawnee by a Well-Known Professor", "comment": {"by": "Naomi", "text": "I knew it... Shawnee's hiding something. I'm digging up all her dirt from Skynet before any kind of deal goes down."}}, {"title": "Peacekeeper", "text": "\"Shawnee... that girl's a freak, the kind that's completely off the rails... Hmph, if you ask me, with that face and figure, she should've gone into modeling, or found some rich playboy to latch onto... Coming to a place like this is a total waste. Of course, her shooting skills, and her nose for solving cases, are flawless... So, I wasn't surprised when she became the head of the Guard Bureau... I just don't get why she's in this line of work.\" — A Senior Detective from the DL Commenting on Shawnee"}, {"title": "Future of the League", "text": "\"The pursuit of peace has always been my goal... This has never changed, and of course, I understand that these two words are a luxury on Milkhama. However, the key to the Dawnstar League's ability to take the initiative and achieve a situation of co-governance with the UNCS lies in our expectations for the future and the prudent exercise of our advanced power... Milkhama is shrouded in the fog of war, and there are also voices of agreement within the League... In this regard, I urge you all to reconsider, and I will also represent the position of the security department and take whatever action is necessary.\" — League Meeting Minutes", "comment": {"by": "Arnold", "text": "Well, it's just as I expected. The Dawnstar League isn't the monolithic entity some make it out to be. Miss Russell clearly needs allies who share her interests right now, but how long will this facade of peace conceal her true ambitions?"}}]}, "10103151": {"profile": [{"label": "Affiliation", "value": "NERV"}, {"label": "Blood Type", "value": "Unknown"}, {"label": "Height", "value": "Unknown"}, {"label": "Likes", "value": "Listening to his cassette player"}], "introduction": "Shinji Ikari, the Evangelion Unit-01 pilot from another world, and the Third Child of Evangelion. A boy who seeks recognition as he fights endlessly against creatures known as Angels. After arriving in Milkhama, Shinji Ikari escaped the Leviathan crisis under Dean Knight's protection. After a series of wild adventures, he and his companions defeated the invading Leviathan.", "stories": [{"title": "Timid Youth", "text": "\"When I found Shinji, he was curled up with his legs trapped under rubble, neither calling for help nor attempting to escape, even though the enemy was closing in. Honestly, I'd never met a boy who reacted like that to such imminent danger. But in that split-second, I didn't have time to think. All I could do was rush to his side and take the brunt of the enemy fire. Then, during a lull in Leviathan's assault, I opened the cockpit to let him in... Luckily, I had fine-tuned this prototype before the battle. Otherwise that ambush would've been the end of us both...\" —Excerpt from Dean Knight's interview record"}, {"title": "Ideal Life", "text": "\"After coming back, that kid told me he was actually a pilot for something called an Evangelion unit, and his duty was to fight invaders known as Angels to protect humanity... When he first said it, I thought the terror of battle must made him lose it. But as his description became more detailed, I began to think... is this true? I have to say, as a warrior, I was green with envy! Piloting a giant humanoid machine, defeating invaders to safeguard humanity—that's the life I've always dreamed of! Yet, when he talked about it, he did not do so with enthusiasm or passion. Makes me think that behind those experiences there's a dark burden that I can't even imagine..\" —Excerpt from Dean Knight's Interview Record"}, {"title": "Never Alone", "text": "\"What lay ahead surpassed anything I could've imagined; I never could've guessed there was such a vast expanse within Leviathan... After fighting together, Shinji started to talk a bit more, but the dangers surrounding us only grew... I also began to understand the heavy burden he carried... Forced to pilot the ST to fulfull the demands of others, he had no way to connect to the world except through the machine... I must admit, I had never even considered what a world without STs might be like. But I told Shinji that in Milkhama, in this world where everyone has to pilot STs to fight, he will never be alone. We're all comrades, and we'll always stand by him!\" —Excerpt from Dean Knight's Interview Record"}, {"title": "Final Battle", "text": "\"The battle plan for the showdown with Leviathan had been set. I honestly thought Shinji wouldn't wake up in time for the final battle, but to my surprise, when I rushed to the hangar, he was already there! The kid really keeps you on your toes... I must say, Major Matilda is really playing favorites—she actually made custom STs for this guy and his two companions. Even the paintwork is cool! You know, I had to pester the old guys in the tech department for months just to get approved to pilot that Steel Puppet Test Type! But... well, this battle is a matter of life and death, and if your gear isn't just right, then forget about winning. Now all that's left is to pray for a bit of luck!\" —Excerpt from Dean Knight's Interview Record"}]}, "10103181": {"profile": [{"label": "Affiliation", "value": "The Principality of Ovett"}, {"label": "Blood Type", "value": "AB"}, {"label": "Height", "value": "168cm"}, {"label": "义体改造", "value": "左眼"}, {"label": "最喜爱书籍", "value": "《艾希的黎明》"}], "introduction": "索妮娅·沃洛科娃，隶属奥维特公国禁军特种侦察营，奉命渗透米赫玛岛，为禁军先遣部队指挥官阿列克谢·别拉诺夫提供情报支持。\n她出身于沃洛科夫家族，是家族领袖的私生女，自小远离亲族，在冷漠与孤独中长大。为了生存，幼时的她就已学会察言观色，懂得通过洞悉他人的弱点进而操纵对方为自己所用。后在机缘巧合之下成为了摩根娜的学生，受到其悉心教导保护，逐渐从家族的阴影中走出，并认定老师便是她在这个世界的救赎。但也正因此，当摩根娜不告而别后，索妮娅一度陷入了阴郁的偏执之中。为了寻回老师，也为了知晓自己被舍弃的理由，她费尽心力加入公国禁军，通过严酷训练成为了一名强大的战士。", "stories": [{"title": "新历109年12月28日 雪", "text": "今天是新雪节后的第三个休息日，母亲早早起了床，先是打扫了卫生，把壁炉的火烧旺，又急着走进厨房开始做饭。就在墙上时钟刚刚转过12点时，父亲照例来了。他进门的时候，母亲的眼睛亮得就像昨晚天上的月亮。\n吃饭的时候父亲很安静，偶尔摸摸我的头，那动作轻得像在拍一件旧家具上的灰。母亲一直笑，不停给他添菜，说镇上今年雪大、说邻居家的狗下了崽——他听着，偶尔点头，眼神却从未落在母亲身上。我放下勺子，问他：「你为什么不把妈妈接回去？为什么我们只能住在这里？」他的脸一下就沉了，摔了手里的杯子，说我不懂大人的事，说我被惯坏了。我看着他大发雷霆的样子，心里有一种说不出的畅快——原来母亲偷偷念叨了许久的这句话能戳到他心底。母亲着急地把我拉回房间，说我不该顶撞他，说他为了维系沃洛科夫家族有多不容易，说他为了获得「亲王」的信任付出了多少努力。她说着说着眼眶就红了，可很快又整理出一张笑脸回到父亲身边，陪着他吃完了午饭，然后目送着他坐上返回首都的豪华轿车……我们的生活又变回了昨天的模样。我还是改变不了父亲，改变不了母亲，改变不了这间被雪围住的小屋，改变不了沃洛科夫家族。\n……如果长大了，我就能做到吗？"}, {"title": "新历112年1月2日 晴", "text": "镇上前段时间来了个叫「摩根娜」的旅行者，借着旅店闲置的房间开了个学堂。据说她是看镇上孩子没处念书，愿意留下来教几个月，顺便赚点旅费。镇上很少会来外乡人，我对她和她的学堂都很好奇。尽管母亲对我跟平民接触颇有微词，但我还是会偷偷去旁听她的课。\n或许是我的举动太明显，摩根娜一下子就发现了我在观察她。她没生气，反而笑着说：「你比这镇上的人都聪明。」\n她没有教我认那些我早已认识的字，而是拿出一叠照片，和我讲起了小镇之外的世界；她还会教我算账，教我怎么从一个人的言行举止里读出真正的意思——这个我学得很快，因为这本来就是我在这个镇子上活下来的本事；在没有其他人的时候，她还会偷偷教我几招打架的技巧，让我能在被镇上的其他人欺负时狠狠反击。她从不过问我家里的事，即使看到了父亲来了又走、母亲泪眼婆娑，她也什么都不问，只是照常教我功课、给我带零食，把自己的围巾裹在我的身上。\n……我到现在都不知道她到底是怎样的人，不过应该，不是个讨厌的家伙。"}, {"title": "新历114年2月18日 雨", "text": "她已经离开五天了。五天前她还说，等贝列诺的蔷薇花开之后我们就离开这——去周游世界，过平静的日子，最好再养一条不会乱叫的狗。我把这些话都记在心里，就等着将来能和她逐个实现。\n可她却突然走了，连一句道别都没有。我把镇子翻了个遍。她住过的那间屋子收拾得干干净净，像从没有人住过。我问遍了所有见过她的人，都说她急匆匆地走了，不知道去了哪。我蹲在旅店门口，蹲到腿麻，天黑了又亮，直到母亲将我带回了家。母亲用一副理所当然到有些刻薄的语气，说人家本来就是旅行者，随时都可能离开，但我知道这绝没有那么简单——我曾无意中撞见过她和一些军人模样的家伙在暗巷里交谈，她当时的表情非常吓人。后来我几次尝试问起这件事，都被她用滴水不漏的回答挡了回来……她的离开很可能就与这件事有着什么关联。\n我尝试寻求父亲的帮助，毫不意外地被他拒绝了。他或许以为我会就此放弃，但他错了，我知道还有一个人可能帮我找到老师——那是父亲口中一位非常了不起的大人物，甚至与传闻中的禁军有着很深的联系，我不知道他的名字，甚至不知道他是男是女、多大年龄，只知道他被称作「亲王」。\n她教过我，想要的东西，要自己想办法拿到。既然如此，那我就想办法。"}, {"title": "新历119年3月13日 阴", "text": "今天我回到了小镇。自从和母亲搬走之后，这是我第一次回到这里。\n镇上的人或是认不出我，或是不敢认我，偶尔有人在远处悄悄议论，却没有一人主动与我交谈。这不奇怪，和离开时相比，我长大了许多，还换上了制服，就连左眼也换成了电子战专用的新型义眼——五年训练与改造，早已将我从当年那个在旅店门口蹲到腿麻的小丫头，转变为了禁军的战士。\n到了明天，我就会前往不远处的港口，以一名游人的身份前往千里之外的米赫玛岛，独自进行渗透侦察，为阿列克谢长官的特别行动收集情报。我必须感谢「亲王」，如果没有这个任务，我不会这么轻易去往那座不受奥维特控制的岛屿，也不会知道那个人这五年来一直躲在那里。\n我还没想好见面时先问哪一句，是「为什么走」，还是「这些年过得如何」。其实答案我早就有了大半，我只是想亲耳确认。如果她不肯跟我走，甚至不肯回答……我带来了一整套能让人屈服的办法，也做好了用上的准备。\n「想要的东西，要自己想办法拿到」——老师教的东西，我一直没忘。"}], "cn": true}, "10103183": {"profile": [{"label": "Affiliation", "value": "特务部队"}, {"label": "Blood Type", "value": "Unknown"}, {"label": "Height", "value": "160cm"}, {"label": "起源", "value": "蛇夫座项目"}], "introduction": "塞拉·瓦伦蒂亚，来自异世界的机兵驾驶员。她是暗杀部队的顶尖精英，即便在高手辈出的企业佣兵圈，也是令人闻风丧胆的存在。她「屠杀者」的名号，源于一场针对联合飞地的特种作战——在对所有后果心知肚明的情况下，她亲手投放了一枚战术核武器，直接造成整座小镇的彻底覆灭。尽管企业联合研发的 「清洁核武器」并未给当地留下次生灾害，而且行动的根本目的是消除未来人入侵造成的影响，但塞拉面无表情投下核弹的举动仍让她背负了这一恶名。本就性格冷淡的塞拉，也因此愈发被旁人敬而远之，不过向来独来独往的她对此毫不在意。坊间一直有传言，她其实是某项强化人计划的实验产物。\n她最初隶属于金恩势力，后转投泰坦工业麾下。而她如今的所有行径，皆指向同一个目的——赎回被泰坦工业囚禁的兄长。为此，她可以不择手段，也无需任何人理解。", "stories": [{"title": "特殊个体", "text": "「编号X-101，临时实验体，女性，银发红瞳。身高约160CM，体重约65KG。生理检测结果显示，该实验体的各项指标均远超常人上限：即便是在昏迷状态下，心率仍保持完美平稳，肌肉密度是普通人的1.7倍，神经传导速度还能达到理论极限的93%，就连黑障中队都没有这么夸张……而且我们在她那些疑似血液的循环液中检测出了大量未知的纳米级物质，还在脑部位置检测到疑似某种电子辅助模块发出的高密度电磁信号。\n尽管这只是初步扫描的结果，尚未经过实际的解剖验证，但如果推测正确，她绝不是什么普通的人类，而是某种……披着人皮的机械，或者说人造人？据我所知，即便是社长牵头的那什么『更生计划』都还没能完全达到这一步……这个实验体，到底是什么来头？」——黑曜石第二十九研究所的初步研究报告"}, {"title": "利刃之外", "text": "「说实话，第一次见到塞拉的时候，我有点被吓到了……她看人的眼神就像在评估猎物，冷漠得让人后背发凉。后来的战斗里，她的表现也确实配得上那副眼神——精准、凌厉、毫不犹豫，那部被称作『美杜莎MK2』的机兵在她手中，简直灵活得像是她身体的一部分。我也能理解艾达队长为什么会对一个只有一面之缘的人做出那么高的评价了。\n不过比起这些，其实最让我意外的是她竟然主动保护了我。在法兰河边的遭遇战里，虽然她嘴上什么都没说，但在对付黑曜石的大型兵器之余，还会分心帮我脱离敌机的包围。虽然我至今都不知道她到底是什么人，但很显然，一定不会是坏人。」——萨普里娅·柯格尼托尼斯的通讯记录"}, {"title": "蛇与笼", "text": "「没想到还会有其他人在这个时候来到米赫玛岛。根据公爵提供的资料来看，塞拉·瓦伦蒂亚是隶属于泰坦工业特务部队的顶尖精英，为了赎回自己的兄长而在暗中执行着各种高危任务，有着『屠杀者』的称号……这身份确实有趣，但最重要的是她似乎与赐克·斯缇有着颇为密切的合作关系，那台机体美杜莎也是源自赐克的技术。这意味着，她和她的机体或许就是我们寻求的线索，甚至可能是关键的钥匙。为了正确评估这份可能，必须与她进行足够的接触，哪怕这会大幅增加计划提前暴露的风险。\n我想想……就让那些完成训练的寄生体部队去试探她吧。只要能确定ND引擎的特殊性，就算折损一整队也不算什么代价。」——德里克·默瑟的语音日志"}, {"title": "棋局未终", "text": "「塞拉·瓦伦蒂亚——蛇夫座项目的漏网之鱼。哼，那些家伙自以为打造了一件玩具，却不会料到玩具也能长出自己的意志。有趣的是，她本人大概至今都不清楚项目的全貌，也不明白ND技术的真正意义——但这无所谓。我至今还在关注她，已不是为了她本身……真正值得观测的是那部美杜莎MK2。\n赐克·斯缇的ND技术远比这座岛上任何人想象的都要精妙。美杜莎的ND引擎在贝洛伦展现出了远超预期的潜能，甚至可以主动干扰ND变换，而这种潜能兑现得越多，就越能帮我看清ND技术的本质。至于塞拉会作何选择，那不过是观测过程中的变量之一……她越活跃，暴露的细节就越多。\n从这个层面来讲，德里克，你的失败也不是完全没有意义。」——噬骨魔鸟残留通讯记录"}], "cn": true}, "10103119": {"profile": [{"label": "Affiliation", "value": "The Epiphyllum"}, {"label": "Blood Type", "value": "O"}, {"label": "Height", "value": "170cm"}, {"label": "Physical Status", "value": "Healthy"}], "introduction": "In the days of the Hyper-Aptamer experiments, Sylvie and Rosa formed an unbreakable bond. She became the Valkyrie's most loyal shadow—and her hate for the labs spread across Milkhama runs bone-deep. With Rosa gone, Sylvie leads a crew of girls scarred by the same nightmares, driving them into a bloody revolt with no way back. She's got the mind of a leader and the will to match, but where her shaky fate goes from here... no one can say.", "stories": [{"title": "February, XC 107, Sunny", "text": "Today marks my second week here since being brought in, but Dad still hasn't come to pick me up like he promised... That white-haired girl appeared at the door of my room again. She told me that she and the people in white coats were not working together. She urged me to give up waiting and said she'd seen Dad discussing something with those grown-ups... I don't believe he could've brought me here... Why would he do that? After Mom left, Dad didn't smile again... I wish Mom were still here...", "comment": {"by": "Dana", "text": "Sylvie... was actually sent by her father to this UNCS research facility!? That guy... There are no words to describe how despicable he is, willing to sacrifice his own daughter for the sake of his so-called research."}}, {"title": "April, XC 108, Cloudy", "text": "This is my third diary since they confiscated the others from me... Thank god for Rosa. She used her access to grab it from the warden's quarters. Yep, Rosa's the only friend I've got now. Sure, she's a bit rough sometimes, and her situation's different from ours, but she's honestly pretty badass. She's even planning an escape for us, though... can we really pull it off? I'm not sure. But if she's in charge, I think we've got a shot!", "comment": {"by": "Kaidan", "text": "Is this a diary? Is this page about her and Rosa's past...? Wait, do I really want to risk getting beaten up and keep reading it?"}}, {"title": "April, XC 113, Overcast", "text": "In today's \"training,\" the current was way stronger than usual. I lost track of how many times I blacked out. Rosa came to visit me, like she always does... She says it's punishment for all our failed escape attempts... I don't get it! Why do we have to go through this? I screamed and tore at my uniform until Rosa held me tight... She keeps telling me that one day we'll get out, just like she did with her \"sister\"... But I'm too sick and tired to believe in any of it anymore. My father betrayed me... Will Rosa do the same?"}, {"title": "July, XC 116, Rain", "text": "I escaped, but Rosa didn't. ▇▇▇▇▇▇, the only thing that keeps me going is knowing that Hong and Emily are doing well. We were all saved by Rosa, but then the UNCS took her away. I can't let that slide. Even if they took her physical body, they can't stop us from continuing to fight for her beliefs... The pain this island has given us, we will return it tenfold in Rosa's name... ▇▇▇▇▇▇, in the name of the Epiphyllum."}]}, "10103166": {"profile": [{"label": "Affiliation", "value": "Harpy Commerce"}, {"label": "Blood Type", "value": "B"}, {"label": "Height", "value": "167cm"}, {"label": "Skynet Permissions", "value": "最高"}, {"label": "Likes", "value": "各式占卜"}], "introduction": "唐小葵，角雕佣兵业务负责人。年纪轻轻却手段了得，凭借自身的出众才智以及佣兵们的支持，成功跻身商会最核心管理层，帮助角雕周旋于米赫玛各大势力之间，也与多尔、卡塔纳乃至神州势力建立了合作关系。\n因为已逝双亲的遗志和自身从小到大的经历，她对「佣兵」这一旁人敬而远之的危险职业持独特看法——认为他们与劳苦大众并无不同，只是在米赫玛既有规则下讨着生活。他们无法触及真正的利益，也无法对抗剧变的局势。在战争不断激化的当下，她不惜亲身入局，希望利用角雕的力量维持米赫玛局势平衡，为这些佣兵提供尽可能多的生存与发展机会。", "stories": [{"title": "商人与佣兵", "text": "「我第一次见到小葵时，她还只是个襁褓中的婴儿。粉嘟嘟的脸、墨黑的头发，简直跟她那来自神州的商人老娘是一个模子刻出来的，不过碧绿的眼睛倒是随了她的佣兵老爹。因为这副模样在米赫玛实在少见，周围的弟兄都好奇地凑上来瞧，结果……那孩子不但没被这群五大三粗的佣兵吓哭，反而笑了出来，主动伸手触碰着大伙脸上的伤疤。从那天起，小葵就成了角雕商会里的名人，谁见了她都忍不住逗上一下。后来她学会了走路，更是闲不下来，今天跟着她娘，看她出席会议、处理商务；明天又跟着她爹，看他操练新兵、整备武器；两人都没空时，就在商会大楼里到处乱跑，或者和帮忙照顾她的人捉迷藏，好几次惹得一片鸡飞狗跳，我年轻时也没少被她折腾……那时的我只觉得头疼，不明白这种日子是多么宝贵。\n后来……这一切都变了。就和你了解的一样，新历97年后，北陆联合和晨星同盟相继下场——米赫玛战争来了。无论自愿与否，岛上所有人都被卷入其中，角雕也不例外。每分每秒都有新的战斗在某处爆发，抽签似的随机带走一批人的生命，就算是身经百战的传奇佣兵也可能死得不明不白。没有人再顾得上陪她玩耍，只剩下她的父母为了维系角雕四处奔波，在疲惫中保护着她逐渐长大。\n等她终于成长到能亲口念出大伙名字的时候，角雕已经不剩下多少熟悉的面孔了。」——角雕商会高级干部语音记录"}, {"title": "余烬摇篮", "text": "「米尔萨斯爆炸前十五分钟，我还在港口仓库里卸货，根本不知道接下来会发生什么。就在那时候，一男一女两位机师驾驶机兵闯了进来，告诉我们联合和同盟的军队已经在米尔萨斯展开交火，让大家立刻转移。把我们送到安全地带后，他们又准备折回去救助更多人，还打算在被战火波及前转移仓库里的岚矿……我那时已经被漫天炮火吓坏了，只能眼睁睁看着他们离开。\n后来，直到整个米赫玛战争结束后的第三年，我才从合作的商人口中了解到那两位救命恩人的情况——他们是角雕的干部，偶然得知了联合军奇袭黑曜石的计划，明白岚矿危险性的他们不顾自身安危赶往港口，结果功亏一篑，在近距离被卷入了爆炸……唉，这座岛上的好人，为什么总是不能有好报。\n那天我还见到了他们年幼的女儿唐小葵，看上去乖巧又聪明，实在是个非常可爱的孩子。她现在由角雕商会一部分商人和佣兵共同抚养，其中有些人是她父母的朋友，有些人曾受过两人的恩惠，也有一些人是单纯喜欢这个小丫头而主动帮忙，这让我安心了许多。米赫玛岛这地方虽然糟糕，但还不是无药可救。\n现在又过去了十多年，算起来那孩子也该有二十多岁了，希望她一切安好……」——已退休的米尔萨斯港口物流监管人口述"}, {"title": "后起之秀", "text": "「我们在角雕商会布置的眼线被拔掉了。\n那个叫唐小葵的女人，不知从哪里拿到了斯肯斯为我们输送实验者的证据，把他从佣兵业务负责人的位置上弹劾了下来。现在角雕内部有不少人打算让她接班，就连那几个老家伙也是……哼，表面上是照顾故人之女，可谁不知道他们是想把唐小葵当做傀儡，借着她父母在角雕内部的名望，进一步把控整个商会，逼我们掏出更多的筹码。\n不过，这一步棋恐怕要落空了。\n以我们最新掌握的情报来看，唐小葵在角雕外部早就有所布局——她通过自己的商人关系网，已经与创新动力、GeekX、多尔工业甚至神州的资本巨头达成了一些合作；又靠着对佣兵们的大力支援，在西北丛林、法兰河、珂尚罗地带都组织起了自己的部队。这女人年纪轻轻，手段可一点都不简单，角雕从此要变天了。\n对我们小组而言，当务之急就是与唐小葵建立稳定良好的私人关系。如有必要，我们甚至可以主动抛弃部分尚在潜伏的棋子，换取更有分量的合作。」——黑曜石机密调查日志"}, {"title": "守衡之志", "text": "「在我走投无路的时候，是唐小姐向我伸出了援手，她还清了我的债务，也买下了我的后半生。我对此充满感激，毕竟除了她，还有谁愿意雇佣一个双腿残废的失败佣兵，让他担任战术教官呢？而且据我所知，类似情况发生过不止一次……她掌握着米赫玛佣兵们的命脉，精明地为他们安排任务，也慷慨地给予他们生路。\n我曾问她这么做的理由，她只是笑着说自己『比起你死我活，更喜欢小打小闹』，当时的我没能理解其中的深意，甚至无法判断它是不是一句玩笑。后来我从档案里了解到她父母在米尔萨斯所做的努力，以及她是如何在商人和佣兵的共同抚养下长大，才算是明白了她的信念从何而来——或许商人和佣兵就是她的家人，他们会因适当的争斗而荣，也会因过量的争斗而死。\n哪怕成为了佣兵业务负责人，跻身角雕核心管理层，她也没有背离过这份信念。但也正因此，我才非常担心……如今米赫玛战火再起，谁也不知道平衡会在哪天崩溃，带来下一场绞肉机般的全面战争，而这肯定不是她愿意看到的。据说她最近亲自参与了几次佣兵行动，或许就是在想办法维系平衡，但这绝非易事。且不说参战势力的态度，光是角雕内部，希望凭借战争谋取利益的人就不在少数，他们都会是横在唐小姐面前的阻碍。\n如果真的到了不得不摊牌的那一天，希望我这个废人还能帮到她……哪怕要用上这条命。」——角雕某高级战术教官日记"}], "cn": true}, "10103131": {"profile": [{"label": "Affiliation", "value": "DLAF"}, {"label": "Blood Type", "value": "B"}, {"label": "Height", "value": "182cm"}, {"label": "Likes", "value": "Igidi Red Tea"}, {"label": "Habits", "value": "Enjoys field-stripping and reassembling heavy firearms to relax after work."}, {"label": "Nickname", "value": "Shepherd"}], "introduction": "\"During the war, I found myself trapped in a trench with two gunshot wounds in my left thigh, while Tiphys suffered a broken arm. We had to improvise medical care and managed to relay a critical intelligence message to prevent an NDF breach. He once shared a piece of timeless wisdom that has remained with me for decades: 'You cannot rest until the mission is accomplished.' Today, he is celebrated as a war hero of the DL, and the Milthus Battle he commanded is enshrined in the history books. Yet, he often reflects on the past, reminding us, 'What arrogance it is to praise honor built upon the lives of others.'\" — Memoirs of a Senior DLAF Officer", "stories": [{"title": "[Hazard]", "text": "\"Sorry, boss. Bastard slipped through our fingers... We worked him over for three days—nothing useful. But one of his boys cracked. Let a few things slip. Your gut was right—they're DLAF. The leader's Tiphys Mill, a lieutenant. They were posing as our contacts, trying to scam the goods for evidence—haul us in and dump us in a military tribunal! How did they get past all the checks when we've been working with 'them'? I've checked, and this Tiphys has no big name behind him. He was able to join this special establishment squad because of his outstanding combat performance and command ability, they say. Maybe he's the only one who overlooked our deal. Boss, we should just kill him. He's threatening our whole operation... Just now, he ran solo past the electric fence—straight into the damn minefield. Our guys are on him. If the bombs don't get him, I'm asking for clearance to finish the job myself.\" — [XXXX] Mercenary Group Communication Records", "comment": {"by": "DLAF Soldier", "text": "You know, when we found the lieutenant, he was oozing blood from wounds all over his body, but he insisted on taking us back to fight and avenge those comrades who'd been tortured to death. They say he lay in the hospital for over a month after this. He was fantastic!"}}, {"title": "[Build-up]", "text": "\"Once the big exercise kicked off, Lieutenant Colonel Mill became a regular in the command room. When duties weren't too demanding, he always came in low-key and sat in an inconspicuous corner to discuss the progress of the exercise with the others. He looked younger than the face I'd seen on the Wall of Honor—and far more serious. I was just a nobody, a service aide, but every time I brought him tea, my hands would tremble. He knew every officer by name, remembered their records by heart. He could watch the flow of the drills and predict each move like a chess master. By the end, it was the team he'd pegged from the start that took first place. I still remember the last time I cleared his cup. He suddenly said my name—my whole body locked up. Turns out, he just wanted to compliment my tea. Later, I heard most of the officers in that exercise ended up under his wing. Some people have all the luck.\" — Diary of a DLAF Orderly", "comment": {"by": "DLAF Orderly", "text": "Can you believe it? That's me, right there! Alright, let me sneak in one more thing... I later met Lt. Col. Mill once again—by then, he had become a rear admiral. Hah! Don't even get me started. I'm not bragging or anything! Just thought I'd toss that in."}}, {"title": "[Father]", "text": "\"After discussing Elise's advancement issue for an entire afternoon, we unanimously agreed that she is a highly talented child. Given her current knowledge reserves, we should really create more suitable learning conditions for her. After finalizing several suitable university options, Colonel Mill, who is usually expressionless, showed a few traces of worry. I fully understand this—after all, Elise is just a young girl who has recently entered high school. For parents, asking her to take such a leap so early is no easy emotional burden.\nAfter the conversation, three things happened that deeply touched me. First, Colonel Mill asked, 'Do these schools require a letter of recommendation from me?' Second, he requested, 'The final decision needs to be thoroughly discussed between Elise and I. Please hold off on the submission for now.' Lastly, he asked, 'If Elise ultimately chooses to study away from home, as a father, what can I do to help prepare her for her new life?' It is genuinely moving to see such a devoted father. Elise should be able to go far in the future with a father like him...\" — Work Record of a Well-Known Teacher in the DL", "comment": {"by": "Elise", "text": "Dad has always supported me, no matter what decisions I made. Maybe I could chase some far-off dream, but what I truly want is to give something back to him."}}, {"title": "[Ghost]", "text": "\"Captured at the moment the Milthus Battle officially ended, this rare photograph shows General Mill, covered in blood, breaking through the haze of the battlefield and charging at the camera. Photographer Harry Brown, upon hearing the detonation of a landmine, pressed the shutter one last time—this would be the final image of his life. Brown was the last casualty of the Milthus Battle, and as fate would have it, Mill's image was the last to emerge from Harry's film.\nAfter a fragile peace took hold, the crowds hailed their hero—Mill, the man who pulled the land from the jaws of hell. His name shone brighter than the sun, but he refused the glory, again and again. Perhaps in the hearts of many, the shadow of war had already dissipated along with the remains of those who were sacrificed, but a part of General Mill will forever be locked in the haze with that 'last photo.'\" - Excerpt from the Military Documentary, Burning Milthus"}]}, "10103172": {"profile": [{"label": "Affiliation", "value": "创界山"}, {"label": "Blood Type", "value": "O"}, {"label": "Height", "value": "132.5cm"}], "introduction": "虎王，来自异世界的少年，大魔王多恶达的儿子。酷爱玩乐的他通过梦境来到米赫玛岛，开启了全新的冒险之旅。", "stories": [{"title": "魔界皇子", "text": "虎王是被当成魔王继承者培养的魔界皇子，主要由魔王的亲信东哥罗代为教导，但调皮的虎王总是让东哥罗束手无策。"}, {"title": "兴趣", "text": "虎王个性贪玩，感到无聊时就会主动寻找乐趣。也因此，他偶然结识了小渡与火美子等人，并对他们产生了兴趣，时常关注他们的动向。"}, {"title": "熟悉", "text": "在一起经历了多次冒险后，虎王与小渡一行人也逐渐熟悉起来。"}, {"title": "新的冒险", "text": "经由梦境意外来到了陌生的米赫玛岛后，虎王决心开启属于自己的全新冒险之旅。"}], "cn": true}, "10103144": {"profile": [{"label": "Affiliation", "value": "Luno Family"}, {"label": "Blood Type", "value": "O"}, {"label": "Height", "value": "171cm"}, {"label": "Favorite Book", "value": "A Complete History of the UNCS"}, {"label": "Gossip", "value": "Rumored to have once won an underground tournament in Kadrey."}], "introduction": "\"I first laid eyes on Vincenza Luno at the DR. ROYAL in Kadrey. Doll was marking the opening of its 100th DR hotel, and the city's most powerful names had gathered for the celebration. The moment Vincenza stepped into the room, every eye turned toward her. People whispered, wondering why Doll's largest rival in Kadrey had shown up. Faced with hostile, heavily armed Doll security, she merely offered a faint smile and snapped her fingers. In the next instant, headlights flared and engines roared to life. Hundreds of biker enforcers stood ready outside. The guards could only watch as she mounted the back of a female rider's bike, then the convoy circled the hotel three times before thundering off into the night. That was the moment I knew—war had come.\" —Testimony of Undercover Kadrey Police Agent X.W.", "stories": [{"title": "Underworld Heiress", "text": "There is no doubt that when Vincenza was young, she was a naive, happy, adorable little girl. She excelled in school and would happily play with friends after class—everyone thought she was a good child. It was only when the news leaked our that her father had connections to the underworld that, gradually, her childhood friends began distancing themselves from her in fear, and the teachers at school began treating her with an obsequious level of respect and attention. Even during the youth baseball games, the umpires would constantly look to her for approval before making a call. No one dared touch her, but no one dared to approach her either. After a large-scale turf war on Flogg Street, her daily outings could only be conducted with the accompaniment of bodyguards— a complete departure from her old life as an ordinary girl."}, {"title": "The Game Board", "text": "Alone and without friends, Vincenza immersed herself in books and chess. Through the pages of old texts and game records, she felt as though she could converse with minds from the past, learning their thoughts and temperaments. A player's character always reveals itself on the board—bold and decisive, swift and fluid, cautious and defensive, timid and uncertain. Each move whispers something about the player's life, and perhaps their future. Vincenza's own style is a web of traps. When it seems she is quietly defending, a hidden strike force is already waiting in some forgotten corner of the board, ready to deliver the fatal blow."}, {"title": "Successor", "text": "\"Are we really going to go along with that old fox from the GSA and replace the leader with Vincenza?\"\n\"The boss has already decided. It's being announced at tomorrow's meeting. Or are you planning to vote against it?\"\n\"...This isn't just his family's business. I'm the youngest here, so I'll just say it—it's wrong!\"\n\"I know. The current territory and business were built by all the brothers together. If Boss Luno insists on this, I'll lead the brothers to start our own group.\"\n—Excerpt from GSA Surveillance Records", "comment": {"by": "GSA Operative", "text": "At the time, we received more than thirty recordings. From them, we obtained evidence of crimes committed by several key members of the Luno family, including murder, smuggling, tax evasion..."}}, {"title": "Vision", "text": "Genovese Luno failed after charging at the immovable windmill, but Vincenza is determined not to repeat her father's mistakes. Despite the Doll Group's constraints and the GSA's oversight, even if the path is thorny, she is resolute in securing a place for the Luno Family in the turbulent future. \nShe voluntarily stepped away from the lights of Kadrey, to listen to the wails echoing from the shadows... the lonely elderly in community hospitals, the homeless children in old industrial areas, the workers selling their strength at the old docks, and even the outlaws who cannot survive in the light. While they seek sustenance, they continuously provide energy to the Luno Family. Vincenza understands that to realize her vision, she must recruit and utilize every possible ally..."}]}, "10103155": {"profile": [{"label": "Affiliation", "value": "Dawnstar League"}, {"label": "Blood Type", "value": "AB"}, {"label": "Height", "value": "176cm"}, {"label": "Oversight Committee Rank", "value": "Special Agent"}, {"label": "Trauma Level Assessment", "value": "Severe"}], "introduction": "\"The DL Oversight Committee was once the laughingstock of all Milkhama. During the war, the military would at times deliberately feed them false intel, knowing the Committee had been thoroughly infiltrated by the GSA. Even their office's weekly meal list became a source of amusement for the opposition.\nBut everything changed when a man named Colin took over... After a 'purge,' nearly all former members of the Committee vanished, replaced by an 'organization' that officially did not exist.\nMuch later, the Committee was reestablished. Veronica was the first agent reassigned to Milkhama—marking her as a representative of this new committee.\nDecisive, ruthless, and composed under any circumstance, she approaches every situation with unwavering professionalism. She is the model of what an agent should be. But more than that, the reason she was chosen to return to Milkhama Island lies in a recommendation letter from Colin—containing only a single sentence:\n'During the war, she found a reason she will never betray.'\"", "stories": [{"title": "Promotion", "text": "\"I recommend Veronica for promotion to Captain of the 3rd Mobile Unit. She acts decisively and takes care of her teammates... After observing her for the past two years, I believe she has the full capability to take on this position. Haha, she always thinks it's my planning and remote command that allow the team to escape danger time and again, but in reality, her on-the-spot performance is often the key to victory, though she is reluctant to admit it. This humility is also why I recommend her, and I believe her teammates think the same.\nThat said, there is one thing I am concerned about. Although she always makes firm decisions, if a moment truly comes that demands a heavy sacrifice, can she really make the right call...? Of course, I will do my utmost to prevent such situations from occurring. That is, after all, my duty.\""}, {"title": "Trauma Assessment", "text": "\"Miss Veronica, you have consistently stated your belief that it was your counterattack that led to the squad's annihilation—even though we all know it wasn't your fault.\nFor three years, you have repeatedly relived that moment, deliberately ignoring the headquarters' responsibility statement. After leaving the 3rd Mobile, you have refused all joint training exercises. You even insisted on single-handedly transporting the injured to the field hospital, even after your old wounds fared up. Avoiding teamwork like this is precisely what drove you to submit your discharge papers. Your psychological assessment shows that you anonymously remit 80% of your monthly allowance to the families of fallen comrades, yet exhibit pathological pleasure upon receiving returned remittance slips. This self-punishment mechanism is more destructive than any battlefield trauma.\""}, {"title": "Blessing", "text": "\"We all blame ourselves for everything that went wrong. My way was to seek atonement through sacrifice; hers was to shut herself off completely... Although Veronica says she's fine now and is learning to trust others and be trusted, honestly, I think she still hasn't moved on from that moment.\nShe has always longed for an answer, and all I can do is give her a speculation to help her not be so tense. But that answer, that... so-called truth, still needs to be discovered by herself.\""}, {"title": "Missions", "text": "\"The fact that she can bring Sapientia back proves she's more capable than we thought... Although I'm not very fond of surprises, what's done is done—we'd best try to make good use of her.\nBeing able to easily let go of the obsession that supports her for the rest of her life proves she's the best candidate for that mission—no matter what the final truth is, she will surely be able to accept it.\""}]}, "10103171": {"profile": [{"label": "Affiliation", "value": "创界山"}, {"label": "Blood Type", "value": "B"}, {"label": "Height", "value": "132cm"}], "introduction": "战部渡，来自异世界的四年级小学生，为了拯救创界山而勇敢行动的「救世主」，在冒险中经由梦境来到了米赫玛岛。", "stories": [{"title": "小学四年级学生", "text": "战部渡原本是住在龙神町的小学四年级学生，活泼开朗，富有正义感。某一天在龙神池邂逅了金色的龙，并被它带往了异世界的创界山。"}, {"title": "启程", "text": "因与传说中拯救创界山的救世主同名，人们对战部渡充满了期待。而天性正直的他决定担起责任，踏上了打倒魔王多恶达，拯救创界山的旅程。"}, {"title": "伙伴", "text": "战部渡的魔神「龙神丸」由他亲手制作的黏土人偶变化而来，并在旅程之中始终陪伴着他，帮助他战斗，两者的关系变得越来越紧密。另外，小渡还邂逅了忍部火美子、剑部武一郎等可靠的伙伴。"}, {"title": "冒险插曲", "text": "通过梦境意外来到米赫玛岛的小渡依然是那个富有正义感的正直之人，他在这陌生的世界一边冒险，一边如往常那样努力拯救着苦难中的人们。"}], "cn": true}, "10103115": {"profile": [{"label": "Affiliation", "value": "Union of Northern Continental States"}, {"label": "Blood Type", "value": "B"}, {"label": "Height", "value": "203cm"}, {"label": "AMC Degree", "value": "Medium"}, {"label": "Current Military Rank", "value": "Major"}, {"label": "Special Honor", "value": "Silver Moon"}], "introduction": "An NDF major and 20-year vet, fighting on the frontlines since the Milkhama Landing—a Blair loyalist, crushing rebels and lending his firepower to any operation that needs a rough edge. Past defeats left him with a heart of hatred and a savage style that terrifies allies and enemies alike.", "stories": [{"title": "[Hero]", "text": "William, who had just joined the army, instantly became a celebrity in the military. The reason for this is not his muscular, beast-like body or his excellent training data, but rather during a drill, he led the rookies in a charge against the officer's line, and ended up beating one of them to a pulp. Surprisingly, this heinous event was eventually settled, and both sides were punished. But every now and then, you'd catch a soldier grinning when the story came up—\"That scumbag was always bullying rookies and stealing their stuff. William simply gave him what he had coming to him. He's a damn hero to us!\"", "comment": {"by": "Kaidan", "text": "Passion, righteousness... This is a far cry from the William of today. What happened to him?"}}, {"title": "[Warrior]", "text": "As the captain of the UNCS's elite troops, William was selected to join the peacekeeping forces of the UNCS in assisting their cooperation with Obsidian, and landed with his unit on Milkhama Island to participate in the operation against the rebels. This was his first time piloting a fully armed ST in actual combat, and the results far exceeded expectations. Under the leadership of former frontline commander Blair, the troops he commanded repeatedly annihilated enemy forces. Even the DL's intervention couldn't halt their advance... But then, a sudden explosion in the Milthus region shattered their momentum, changing William, Blair, and the fate of Milkhama Island forever.", "comment": {"by": "Dana", "text": "The Milthus Explosion... I learned about it in history class. Was William actually a part of it?"}}, {"title": "[Prisoner]", "text": "It has been nearly ten years since the ceasefire, and William has become a major in the Armored Corps. He still maintains high-intensity training difficult for most ordinary people to bear, regardless of his war-torn body and the fact that he is approaching retirement age. The war still imprisons him to some extent, and he cannot forget the unwillingness of his companions' sacrifice, nor can he forget his anger when ordered to retreat. He still has debts to settle with the culprit who caused all this.\nThe long wait finally led to a turning point—his former senior officer Blair approached him again and revealed to him a grand plan he had been brewing for years. William saw hope in it—a great hope worth any cost."}, {"title": "[Devil]", "text": "The Ashes are rapidly rising, and the whereabouts of the traitors are unknown. The \"GKD\" that seeks to dig up insider information is becoming more active. The General Security Administration has also turned its attention to Milkhama. Even the Dawnstar League and Obsidian have increased their efforts to interfere. Blair and William's plan is facing unprecedented internal and external pressures.\nHowever, this has made William's almost crazed belief even firmer. If he chooses a path of no return, he will drag the whole world into it."}]}, "10103158": {"profile": [{"label": "Affiliation", "value": "Union of Northern Continental States"}, {"label": "Blood Type", "value": "O"}, {"label": "Height", "value": "185cm"}, {"label": "Original Unit", "value": "Landing Force Assault Special Operations Team (Disbanded)"}, {"label": "Mercenary ID", "value": "\"Cowboy\""}], "introduction": "\"Wyatt Morgan? Of course I know him, 'Ace of the Joint Mobile Battalion,' 'Hero of the Milkhama War'... His titles before retirement were more impressive one after another, but people in our line of work prefer to call him 'Cowboy.' You might have heard the saying—strong, smart, cautious, lucky... At least possessing one of these traits can help you survive longer on the battlefield. And him? He is a lone wolf, yet he survives better than most, returning intact from any kind of hell. Although I don't know why such a talented person would give up a promising future to become a mercenary, the fact proves he is indeed cut out for it, and given time, he will surely become a new legend in the mercenary world. It's a pity, though, that I heard he was recently recalled by the NDF to Milkhama Island, and that's not good news. Those in the know understand that place seems peaceful on the surface, but in reality, it's a slaughterhouse where big shots incubate wars and reap the profits. I don't know what considerations led him to accept this task...\" —Interview with a Certain Mercenary Contactor", "stories": [{"title": "Youthful Bravado", "text": "Even before enlisting, Wyatt Morgan was already something of a local legend. All it took was a late-night dare: sneaking alone into the barracks command building and covering the walls with graffiti. Had he not run straight into the newly appointed commander, Blair Bluecher, on patrol, he might have walked away unscathed. Even so, headlines about a \"sixteen-year-old breaking into the barracks\" humiliated the NDF. Soon after, the rebellious boy vanished from the streets, and most assumed he had been severely punished—until months later, when he returned on leave wearing the uniform of Enfield Military Academy. Only then did people realize the outcome had been anything but dire. Blair had recognized his sharp mind and not only spared him punishment, but personally recommended him for academy admission.\nPerhaps it was fate. In Wyatt's first year, the armored training program underwent reform. The unprecedented new system—the ST—was introduced as a core discipline for all soldiers. Veterans and recruits alike started from zero, learning together. Wyatt's aptitude stood out almost immediately.\nThree years later, upon graduating with exceptional marks, Wyatt received an urgent transfer order. He was assigned to the Landing Force mobile battalion under Blair's command, bound for Milkhama Island to protect commercial partners and confront the DL."}, {"title": "Ace's Desolation", "text": "\"Ace Pilot.\" The title arrived after Wyatt completed his thirty-seventh sortie. Unlike William, who led the main force head-on, Wyatt's special operations unit specialized in maneuver warfare, striking key DL nodes from their weakest points. His successes made him a thorn in the DLAF's side. Repeated targeted encirclements failed to kill him—or even slow his momentum. Promotions followed in rapid succession: Second Lieutenant, Lieutenant, Captain. Many believed he would reach Major before William. All of that ended with the sudden conclusion of the war.\nThe surprise assault on Milthus—an operation intended by the NDF to pressure Obsidian—was vehemently opposed by Wyatt. He warned that such short-sighted action would drive the NDF into disaster. Blair ignored him, gambled everything, and inadvertently triggered the Milthus explosion that reshaped the conflict. From that point on, the rift between them could no longer be repaired. Years later, with military backing, Blair became Viceroy of West Milkhama and once again summoned his former subordinate. This time, Wyatt refused. He abandoned his honors, left the army, and became a free mercenary.", "comment": {"by": "Raven", "text": "I grew up watching Uncle Wyatt fight under my father's command. He took care of me more times than I can count. Back then, I never imagined the two of them would end up so divided. Now... I think I understand a little."}}, {"title": "Lone Cowboy", "text": "Wyatt's mercenary career unfolded more smoothly than he had imagined. Whether due to his combat experience, command instincts, or simply his calm, perceptive nature, he adapted effortlessly. For nearly a decade, he crossed battlefields and walked away alive, earning a reputation as a legend. People remembered not just his skill, but his solitary, easygoing nature. Gradually, his real name faded, replaced by a single moniker: \"Cowboy.\"\nThat freedom didn't last. In December of XC 118, an agent from the UNCS intelligence division found him and delivered news from Milkhama Island—Blair's downfall, the NDF's decline, the DLAF's rise. The military needed someone to replace Blair and William, to reorganize the West Milkhama NDF and keep its last embers alive. Wyatt gave no answer. He drank in silence until he passed out.\nNo one knows what he decided that night. Only that afterward, the mercenary Cowboy vanished—and the NDF regained its former ace."}, {"title": "Army's Hope", "text": "After returning to Milkhama, Wyatt delayed executing his orders. For nearly half a month, he moved in secret, assessing the island firsthand. Much had changed, but the growing stench of gunpowder between factions was familiar—a prelude to war. Worse still, the battered NDF was clearly unprepared for what was coming.\nAs tensions escalated in the Central Mining Area and GSA oversight faltered, Wyatt seized the moment. He led military agents to remove parliamentary officers obstructing NDF operations and quickly rallied veterans disillusioned with the current state of affairs. Acting as both a voice for the rank and file and a proxy for high command, the burden he carried far exceeded expectations.\n\"Being a mercenary was a hell of a lot freer than this damned Lieutenant Colonel gig.\" He muttered variations of that curse several times a day. Even so, he had no intention of walking away. Since he had chosen to return to this hell, he would see it through—to win the coming war, or at the very least, ensure that as many comrades as possible survived."}]}, "10103123": {"profile": [{"label": "Affiliation", "value": "The Ashes"}, {"label": "Blood Type", "value": "B"}, {"label": "Height", "value": "188cm"}, {"label": "Language Proficiency", "value": "Thirteen (Rumor)"}], "introduction": "Goman leads the Ashes—a ghost on Milkhama. Some say UNCS, some say DLAF, and some whisper Ovett. His moves and motives are shadows, but his people trust him blindly.", "stories": [{"title": "January 20, XC 101, Heavy Snow", "text": "\"Tomorrow is my day of departure. In the afternoon, I drove alone to the suburban cemetery. The cemetery was empty and blanketed in heavy snow. I strolled to that familiar location, bent down to brush off the snow on the gravestone, placed a bouquet of chamomile, and then stood up, bowing my head to gaze at the bouquet and the name buried under the swirling snowflakes. This may be the last time I visit them. I closed my eyes and listened to the long string of names exploding in my heart like sparks in a fireplace.\""}, {"title": "November 24, XC 104, Cloudy", "text": "\"Today, Dr. Newman invited me to have tea with him. During our chat, he showed me pictures of the foster son he keeps in the hidden compartment of his wallet. His face was beaming with a happiness that I had never seen before. It was surprising to see that this scientist, who usually appears so serious and studious, also has a warm and personable side.\"", "comment": {"by": "Kaidan", "text": "My father hardly ever mentioned his friends in the NDF to me. How many more secrets does he have that I don't know about...?"}}, {"title": "March 28, XC 112, Showers", "text": "Two hours ago, a warrior named Ronnie asked me about the meaning of \"The Ashes.\" Before I could even answer, he was gone, his grip still tight on my hand as they wheeled his lifeless body away. Truth is, I'd long since forgotten where I'd first seen this powerful name—perhaps it was in some poem honoring the fallen. Create faith, destroy faith; build trust, trample trust... Maybe it's fate's mercy that Ronnie never witnessed either of them crumble.", "comment": {"by": "Naomi", "text": "Huh? Faith? Trust? What is this guy trying to say...?"}}, {"title": "January 17, XC 117, Cloudy", "text": "Newman's adopted son is more resilient than I imagined. Although I never doubted that he could survive the pursuit of the NDF, I was still surprised when I received a message from the Northwest Jungle that day. He and his team will eventually turn this island upside down. It has been sixteen years... many things are overdue for resolution."}]}, "10103161": {"profile": [{"label": "Affiliation", "value": "Dawnstar League"}, {"label": "Blood Type", "value": "AB"}, {"label": "Height", "value": "168cm"}, {"label": "Mercenary ID", "value": "Fang (Deactivated)"}, {"label": "Likes", "value": "Weapon Maintenance"}], "introduction": "\"Zoey Steele, adjutant to Colin, Executor of the Oceanic Conclave, is responsible for assisting in the execution of classified operations. She is known for her volatile temperament and decisive actions, adhering firmly to a survival-of-the-fittest philosophy. She actively seeks out challenges against stronger or higher-ranking individuals in order to elevate her position within the 'food chain.' Despite her considerable strength, such traits make her ill-suited for the role of adjutant. As her personal file remains sealed, the exact circumstances of her association with the Oceanic Conclave cannot be confirmed. However, there are rumors that she once launched an armed assault on Dawnstar League officials and later engaged in direct combat with Colin's forces. If these claims are accurate, her relationship with Colin warrants reassessment to avoid potential misjudgment in future engagements.\" —Oversight Committee Internal Report", "stories": [{"title": "Raid", "text": "The 225th Special Operations Training Camp is a talent cultivation institution directly managed by the Operations Department under the Oceanic Conclave of the DL. It periodically recruits individuals with special talents from across the country, training them to become the sharpest blades of the Oceanic Conclave. In XC 112, Zoey Steele, only seventeen years old, became one of its students. No one knows how she got in, least of all her classmates or the Oversight Committee. \nThe only certainty is that this girl possesses astonishing talent. In her first melee training class, she nearly pierced a classmate's throat with a dagger, and in the subsequent simulated ST battles, she held her own against the instructor. She thus became a celebrity in the camp, gradually integrating into the environment. However, people never understood the source of the burning hatred in her eyes until the attack two years later—Colin Doyle, as a special envoy of the Oceanic Conclave, was on an inspection tour when he was targeted in his own room by a bomb attack and a knife-wielding assassin—and that assassin was none other than Zoey."}, {"title": "Objective", "text": "With Zoey's capture, some well-informed trainees finally learned about her past.\nShe was born into a southern mercenary group native to the DL, and once followed her father, the mercenary group leader, in an attack on high-ranking DL officials. However, due to Colin's timely support, the attempt failed, and her father died in the fierce battle that ensued. After the battle, Zoey, as the sole surviving member, was taken prisoner. Colin didn't mistreat her, but neither did he release her—instead, after a conversation, he suggested she join the 225th Special Operations Training Camp.\n\"I'll grow stronger. And once I do, I'm coming for you, Colin Doyle.\"\n\"If I had a dime for each time I've heard that... Yet here I am, alive and kicking. But if that's what you need to keep on keeping on, be my guest.\"\nYears later, the exchange was reprised, this time with smoke and steel.\nZoey, however, failed to achieve her goal. Colin, though his face was blackened from the smoke and soot, escaped unscathed, parrying all of Zoey's follow-up attacks until she was apprehended by guards. \nPerhaps due to Colin's moves behind the scenes, the serious charge of assassinating an officer was eventually lowered to the misuse of explosives and destruction of public property. After a month's confinement, Zoey returned to the training camp, catching up with her final test as a trainee."}, {"title": "Directive", "text": "Upon leaving the training camp, Zoey was immediately recruited by the operational department under the Oceanic Conclave and subsequently participated in over twenty special action missions. Although not all the missions ended smoothly, her well-honed combat skills were recognized, especially her ability to operate STs in solo combat, which rivals that of the military elite. If it weren't for her record of attacking a superior officer, she might have become an executor of the Oceanic Conclave.\nUntil XC 116, the situation on Milkhama Island accelerated into turmoil due to the White Maple incident, prompting the Oceanic Conclave to dispatch multiple teams of agents to gather intel in Milkhama, leaving some local positions vacant. This allowed the outstanding Colin to gain more authority. In this context, Zoey regained the Oceanic Conclave's attention, with Deputy Secretary McGonagall personally meeting her to convey a top-secret order—embed herself in Colin's team, watch him and keep him in check, all with authorization for independent action if necessary.\nZoey quickly understood the intention behind this; it was a clear warning from the Oceanic Conclave to Colin. Harnessing her grudge, she would be the Sword of Damocles held over Colin's head."}, {"title": "Chance", "text": "Colin seemed to have anticipated Zoey's arrival, even holding a makeshift welcome party. Naturally, Zoey returned his hospitality with an immediate attack. Colin again frustrated her attempt, blocking her just like last time. But Zoey restrained herself. She understood that she would have countless opportunities to achieve her goals, while Colin could not afford to slip up even once. Despite their twisted superior-subordinate relationship, their cooperation during missions was surprisingly good. Even though Zoey did not always obey Colin's orders, the results still perfectly realized his overall tactics, clearing countless obstacles from the frontlines.\nAfter the Milkhama Central Mines incident in March of XC 119, the Oceanic Conclave urgently needed a strong agent to go to Milkhama to maintain the situation and recover the key results of the Nova Project. Colin was the only man for the job. Whether through a direct clash with a Super Pilot or Colin finally showing a crack under high pressure, these were opportunities Zoey had been hoping for. Thus, she did not hesitate to follow him on the mission, setting foot on the land she had never known.\n\"This time, I'll prove I'm no pushover.\""}]}, "10102114": {"profile": [{"label": "Affiliation", "value": "Doll Offshore Group"}, {"label": "Blood Type", "value": "AB"}, {"label": "Height", "value": "161cm"}, {"label": "Current Assets", "value": "▇▇"}], "introduction": "The Young Doll heiress came to Milkhama seeking thrills. Sharp eyes under that rebel act.\nBlair's crew squeezed her family, so she's helping Arnold's faction and backing Kaidan's team.", "stories": [{"title": "Little Miss No-Life", "text": "Most people imagine Alyson Doll, daughter of the Doll Trading empire, leading a colorful and enviable life—endless money, servants at her command, beauty, impressive credentials, and a network of famous names all vying for a piece of the Doll Group. But for Alyson herself, there's nothing to celebrate except the constant buzz of boredom. She's seen it all, experienced every thrill the world has to offer, and now, the young heiress is craving something new—something she's never felt before."}, {"title": "When a Bipedal ST Appears Before You...", "text": "When Alyson first saw the bipedal mechs in the border war, she immediately realized that what she had been pursuing for so long had finally appeared before her eyes. These STs, agile in action and equipped with heavy firepower, perfectly matched the young lady's love for novelty. However, when Alyson instructed her butler to purchase one of these vehicles, the latter showed a hesitant expression for the first time ever.\n\"My lady, if you really want to get your hands on one of these dangerous toys... we'll have to go to Milkhama.\"", "comment": {"by": "Grant", "text": "In recent years, civilian STs have become popular. They can be purchased in many places, not just in Milkhama... Might the young lady be purely interested in military models?"}}, {"title": "Doll Family Territory", "text": "Upon learning about the origin of the STs, Alyson immediately decided to move the Doll family's business to Milkhama. The Doll family, which had always focused on local dealings, suddenly ventured into Milkhama's business, attracting the attention of other corporate giants. They speculated about the Doll family's sudden move and wondered what their motives were. Little did they know that it was all due to Alyson's parents' indulgence and their spoiled daughter's whims.", "comment": {"by": "Commercial Detective", "text": "Don't buy into the lies! The Doll Group is only deliberately laying out their arms business for the future war! Their second quarter financial report clearly exposes this fact!"}}, {"title": "Miss Doll Graces Milkhama", "text": "The Doll family has established numerous industries in Milkhama, including fiercely competitive businesses such as mining and crude oil processing. After the Doll family's high-profile involvement in Milkhama, Alyson has built her own \"amusement park\" on the island and hired many mercenaries specializing in piloting STs to serve as her entourage as she roams Milkhama... The mercenary leaders in the Northwest Jungle are becoming increasingly frustrated with this spoiled heiress."}]}, "10102107": {"profile": [{"label": "Affiliation", "value": "GKD"}, {"label": "Blood Type", "value": "A"}, {"label": "Height", "value": "168cm"}, {"label": "UNCS Test", "value": "A-Grade"}], "introduction": "Ex-7th Mobile Squad under Marcus. Joined the NDF at 16, like her father. Her squad's hardest worker until the White Maple incident got her kicked out. Her time with Kaidan's crew started changing that stubborn streak.", "stories": [{"title": "A Resume", "text": "Anastasia watched the STs rushing to the front lines as a girl. The NDF's propaganda echoed in her ears, telling her that these warriors were fighting gloriously for their families and for peace. However, they never told her when her father would return from the battlefield.\nAs time passed, the noble beliefs and grand visions in the news became her world. Her father, whom she would never see again, became her goal. Years later, she joined the NDF, swearing to fight for the people and for glory, and to follow in her father's footsteps."}, {"title": "A Friend", "text": "Ana's extraordinary faith has brought her unwavering perseverance and a fiery personality. The former made her an elite member of the 7th Mobile Squad, while the latter caused friction with some of her teammates. When a conflict between her ideals and reality emerged, Captain Marcus appeared in Ana's world and helped her solve many problems.\nIn this environment, the two began to communicate. Before she knew it, this superior had become an irreplaceable friend to her.", "comment": {"by": "Grant", "text": "So it turns out Marcus was the one who led this little girl astray. I knew they were both stubborn as mules."}}, {"title": "An Objective", "text": "Ana is very naive. She had never considered the hidden darkness behind this island, nor did she understand that her initial goal was just a fantasy. When she shared her ideals with Marcus, his genuine interest in her pure vision drew him in, and they spoke openly. As their dreams clashed and merged, Ana began to understand Marcus better. She trusted his judgment and believed in the righteousness of his path. Now, her only goal is to follow this leader she holds in such high regard."}, {"title": "A Warrant", "text": "The 7th Mobile Squad became the victim of a conspiracy... Marcus, who had always strived to protect everyone, went M.I.A... and Rosa, known as the Valkyrie, was hunted down by friendly forces in White Maple... Ana didn't know why everything she believed in had fallen apart in just a few days. She was burdened with unfounded accusations and was like a trapped beast, thrashing around in her cage, unable to see any hope or goal, and simply venting her helplessness and confusion.\n\"Your fearless courage protected us and led us to victory,\" Marcus had said to Ana during a brief rest after a battle.\nHowever, now she had no one left to protect.", "comment": {"by": "Dana", "text": "I know this feeling all too well. When we were being hunted by the NDF, I also lost my sense of direction for a while... but life goes on. You've gotta pull yourself together and keep moving forward."}}]}, "10102105": {"profile": [{"label": "Affiliation", "value": "Union of Northern Continental States"}, {"label": "Blood Type", "value": "O"}, {"label": "Height", "value": "182cm"}, {"label": "Likes", "value": "ST Boxing"}], "introduction": "UNCS council member, a rival to Blair. Dreams of a unified, equal Milkhama. Prepping impeachment under Raven's guard.\nBuilt like a tank under that suit. Clear-eyed about the risks but won't back down from his ideals as things heat up.", "stories": [{"title": "Evergreen", "text": "A politician's career is often short-lived, but for Arnold, fifty years feels like too long. Having been active in politics since he was sixteen, dedicating half a century to the peace cause as an anti-war advocate, he no longer has any desire for the power that so many crave. At least now, ten years after the border war ended, Milkhama has become the land of hope people dreamt of."}, {"title": "Before Retirement", "text": "On a summer night, after finishing up an ST battle and rubbing his sore back, Arnold self-deprecatingly said, \"Maybe it's time for me to retire.\" Due to his involvement in the freedom movements of neighboring countries in his early years, Arnold formed an inexplicable bond with mechs. Whether it was old-fashioned SLs or new STs, Arnold could find the purest joy in the collision of cold steel. However, nowadays, Arnold finds it difficult to maneuver mechs as freely as he did when he was young. Now, he's forced to settle for remotely controlled drones as a substitute for his former passion. He thought his later years would unfold quietly like this, but the new governor's order dragged him back into the heart of the storm.", "comment": {"by": "Raven", "text": "Senator Arnold later came up with the idea of delivering speeches while piloting ST. For those outside of Milkhama, there is nothing more captivating than these towering machines of steel."}}, {"title": "New Deployment Order", "text": "Blair Bluecher has been appointed the new Viceroy of the Federal Republic of Milkhama. After the Union Council approved the military's transfer recommendation, Arnold felt like he was waking up from an old dream. Despite the rebel resurgence in the Milkhama region, he never expected that the mastermind behind the \"Milthus Explosion Scandal\" would be selected as the new Viceroy of West Milkhama.\nCautious as ever, Arnold is aware that Blair's appointment must be part of some larger scheme, and he realizes that his retirement date may have to be postponed once again."}, {"title": "Setting Sail for Milkhama", "text": "Arnold anticipated that Blair's arrival could improve the situation in Milkhama. Instead, it worsened the already tense border situation and failed to quell the rebel uprising. The seasoned Arnold soon sensed that an unseen hand, hidden behind the shifting power dynamics, was stirring the pot in Milkhama.\nWith the determination to \"not let the tragedy of fifteen years ago repeat itself on Milkhama,\" Arnold, who had been fighting for peace for fifty years, boarded a ship to the island.", "comment": {"by": "Naomi", "text": "Instead of following the regular procedure of visiting the viceroy's office, Senator Arnold opted for independent action with the assistance of a few special agents, starting from Milthus... The security of the upcoming trip to Milkhama will be overseen by the General Security Administration, bypassing the NDF, and we will handle any intelligence security issues!"}}]}, "10102110": {"profile": [{"label": "Affiliation", "value": "Refugees"}, {"label": "Blood Type", "value": "A"}, {"label": "Height", "value": "165cm"}, {"label": "Specialty", "value": "Infiltration, Snipe"}], "introduction": "Berguzar leads border refugees, descended from the first Milkhamans. Guides her people from West Milkhama's war. Proud, determined. Fighting to restore dignity to those who built Milkhama with sweat and blood.", "stories": [{"title": "Milkhaman", "text": "Although Bella grew up in a refugee camp on the border of West Milkhama, her father always told her to be proud of her heritage. He told her that, as a native of Milkhama, she was a rightful heir to the island—especially with the Milkhama Citizenship Certificate granted by the Joint Government four decades prior. Anyone holding that certificate, he said, was one of the island's true owners. Young and naïve, Bella didn't fully understand what it meant to be a \"Milkhaman\"—until the collapse of the mines, the destruction of the camp, and the countless workers displaced by the ravages of war. It was then that Bella finally saw the island's true face, and the sharp fangs hidden beneath its veneer of prosperity."}, {"title": "Gold Panner Descendant", "text": "Forty years ago, discovering the mysterious mineral \"Arashi\" brought countless gold seekers to Milkhama from around the world, all harboring dreams of getting rich. They ventured into every mine in Milkhama, mining the toxic raw α ore in hazardous environments. Two superpowers also successively introduced immigration policies, encouraging more and cheaper labor to participate in this grand gold rush. As α ore was continuously mined, many pharmaceutical and heavy industry enterprises became corporate giants, while interest groups from these superpowers reaped significant profits from the island. Meanwhile, the laborers who contributed greatly to Milkhama's development received little more than meager \"Milkhama Citizen Certificates\" as their only reward.", "comment": {"by": "Kaidan", "text": "Without these laborers, there would be no Milkhama today... However, both superpowers now consider the rebellion of Milkhama's citizens to be the cause of the war... Do they have no shame?"}}, {"title": "Proof of Citizenship", "text": "Bella's citizenship did not bring her the pride she deserved. On the contrary, countless struggling laborers on the edge of survival lost their homes entirely after the border war, becoming a source of turmoil and danger within the Milkhama jurisdiction. In an operation classified as a sweep, Bella's father was killed by the NDF, and all her hopes and dreams for a better future were shattered by the cold barrel of a gun. It was in that moment that Bella truly understood—the pride and freedom of the Milkhaman people must be earned through their own struggle, not given as charity or empty promises by others."}, {"title": "Where to Now?", "text": "The wandering of refugees continues to this day, but Bella has now found a sense of direction deep in her heart. Under Bella's leadership, the refugees have taken in more Milkhamans displaced by war and assembled their own STs from abandoned parts. Bella believes that no matter what difficulties they may face in the future, unity and self-respect will always be the most precious treasure and the most potent strength of the Milkhamans.", "comment": {"by": "Professional Steel Trooper Tester", "text": "They should consider joining The Ashes. Only when all oppressed people unite will Milkhama indeed welcome a real dawn."}}]}, "10102115": {"profile": [{"label": "Affiliation", "value": "Dawnstar League"}, {"label": "Blood Type", "value": "A"}, {"label": "Height", "value": "183cm"}, {"label": "Title", "value": "Former researcher of the \"Hyper-Aptamer\" project"}], "introduction": "\"Cicero Wright - trusts power more than science. Don't mistake him for a regular researcher. Showed his hand when he fled UNCS with test subjects to East Milkhama. Yeah, he's valuable to the League, but keep him away from real power. Meanwhile, extract and copy his tech fast.\" —DLAF Leadership Notes", "stories": [{"title": "Research Begins", "text": "\"...Today, I met Viceroy Blair Bluecher at the NDF base. He is truly a bold man. However, his two companions... one a mediocre-looking doctor, and the other, Newman, seem to have some competence. But with just these two, it is impossible to advance the key project they call \"Hyper-Aptamer\"... Let me, the unparalleled genius of this generation, show them the potential of Arashium!\" — Cicero's Research Notes"}, {"title": "Signs of Betrayal", "text": "\"Something unexpected happened today. Cicero figured out my escape plan... But what surprised me even more was that he had the same idea. Perhaps it's because of the \"Hyper-Aptamer\" project. However, Cicero is too concerned about his own safety and refuses to take Ada and escape. Instead, he headed to the DL Jurisdiction. This also fits Blair's evaluation of him—possessed of wisdom but too narrow-minded... But at least, if something happens to me, Ada has someone to rely on...\" — Newman's Notes", "comment": {"by": "Winston", "text": "Cicero, Newman... You still need to awaken a thirst for progress, tying yourselves down with such small costs. I will use my passion... to accomplish what you cannot."}}, {"title": "Escape Direction", "text": "\"The main topic of this meeting is the asylum application of Cicero Wright, a key member of the UNCS research facility. I believe that our benefits of sheltering him after Dr. Cicero brought Diaz's valuable talent to the DL will far outweigh the potential risk of retaliation from the Union. Furthermore, considering the imminent bankruptcy of the NDF's \"Hyper-Aptamer\" project, now is the time for the DLAF to surpass the Union in terms of technology... and the young girl named Ada Diaz is also suitable for training as a valuable asset... to compete with the Union's Rosa Diaz.\" — DL Meeting Minutes", "comment": {"by": "Sylvie", "text": "Diaz... Is she the sister Rosa was trying to find and that Dr. Cicero took away?"}}, {"title": "The Taste of Power", "text": "\"Newman... when we first met, did you ever imagine this situation would come about? You were the most promising newcomer among us, but now your stupidity is burying you in that desert. Your proudest work, Diaz, is also in my hands. Your achievements will serve as be the stepping stone for me to climb the ranks of the Dawnstar League... Ahahaha! I said it before when we first met—I said I wouldn't lose to you. No one should ever underestimate me, Cicero Wright!\" — Recorded Communication Device Ramblings"}]}, "10102103": {"profile": [{"label": "Affiliation", "value": "The Epiphyllum"}, {"label": "Blood Type", "value": "A"}, {"label": "Height", "value": "150cm"}], "introduction": "\"Emily's too fragile for transfer. But she won't admit it, doesn't want to be a burden. Maybe she's strongest of us all, no strength but never breaks. That's the spirit Epiphyllum needs.\" —Sylvie's Letter to Hong", "stories": [{"title": "June, XC 113, Cloudy", "text": "My parents are always fighting about money and the little things in life. I want to stop them, but they always end up taking it out on me. The way they look at me... it's really scary. I get so scared that I can't say anything back, so I just go back to my room and pray over and over that it'll end soon... But every time they stop fighting and I open the door, all I see is the mess they've made. What should I do...?"}, {"title": "August, XC 113, Cloudy to Sunny", "text": "\"Mom and Dad haven't been fighting much lately, I think. At first, I wasn't sure, so I just watched them carefully. They still act like they don't want to talk much, but when they see me, they start being all nice. They must've made up! They said I'm just a kid, so I won't understand why. But next week, they're going to take me to meet someone who helped them—was he the one who made Mom and Dad friends again? I want to thank him!\""}, {"title": "September, XC 113, Rain", "text": "\"Today, Mom told me I can't stay with them anymore. Uncle Winston will take me to a place they say I'll like. I don't really know where it is, but seeing how happy they look, I couldn't help feeling a little excited. They kept saying Uncle Winston's a big help to our family. I've never seen them smile like that before. I hope they're happy after I leave...\"", "comment": {"by": "Hong", "text": "Hmph! Winston's just trying to use those hopeless parents to sell their own daughter!"}}, {"title": "February, XC 115, Unknown", "text": "\"How much time has passed since then...? Every time I wake up from a nightmare, I wonder about it, but I can't figure it out. Even when I ask, those uncles and aunties in white just give me such cold answers. My body hurts... it really hurts. Uncle Winston says it's a sign I'm getting stronger, which is good. But what does 'getting stronger' even mean? What am I getting stronger for...? I don't understand what I'm doing. Someone, please... save me.\"", "comment": {"by": "Hong", "text": "Emily... sorry we're late. It's all over now. No one will ever hurt you again."}}]}, "10102109": {"profile": [{"label": "Affiliation", "value": "Electric Eel Mercenaries"}, {"label": "Blood Type", "value": "O"}, {"label": "Height", "value": "172cm"}, {"label": "Imprisoned count", "value": "Twice (personal claimed)"}], "introduction": "Northwest jungle merc, ex-gang boss. Bad blood with Movme. Luck made him Frida's man, and he claims he's Electric Eel's number two. Crafty showoff declared victory when GKD left his turf.", "stories": [{"title": "The Greatest Mercenary", "text": "Michael Moura, the greatest mercenary in the world—strategist, tactician, military leader, conductor, and ST pilot. I was once the leader of the strongest mercenary team in the Northwest Jungle. Due to my tremendous and selfless spirit, the \"Electric Eel\" has become renowned as the strongest mercenary group in existence. Therefore, the Electric Eel is of course incredibly grateful to me and has invited me to join them, already referring to me as their second-in-command.", "comment": {"by": "Naomi", "text": "This entry was written by Michael Moura, also known as \"Fenrir.\" Additionally, the term \"conductor\" refers to person in an orchestra responsible for conducting and is not a specific military title."}}, {"title": "Royal Descent", "text": "Michael Moura grew up in a noble and wealthy family filled with love. His father was from the UNCS royal family, and his mother was a descendant of a DL political family. He could have become the ruler of one of the most significant countries in the world. Still, he was obsessed with the beauty and wonder of STs and empathized with the struggles of ordinary people. He followed his heart and gave up the right of inheritance to his UNCS royal fortune. And so, he came to Milkhama and became an ordinary mercenary.", "comment": {"by": "Naomi", "text": "The UNCS is an alliance of federal states that has never had a royal family."}}, {"title": "The Island's Heartthrob", "text": "After arriving at the Northwest Jungle, I brought order to the chaotic jungle and took over the local security management on behalf of the NDF. Through my firm and gentle leadership, I quickly became a beloved figure throughout West Milkhama. Even the UNCS Viceroy, Blair, expressed his considerable admiration for my efforts."}, {"title": "Starting Afresh", "text": "Later on, due to my assistance in resolving the security issues in the Northwest Jungle for the UNCS, Blair invited me to establish a special operations team for the Union. However, at that time, I had already retired. I politely declined, as I did not want to be involved in such mundane matters. However, the mercenary team's current leader, considering her team's future, secretly agreed to Blair's request. Out of respect for her, I decided to step forward once again to help the UNCS resolve issues related to the GKD Parcel Service."}]}, "10102111": {"profile": [{"label": "Affiliation", "value": "Union of Northern Continental States"}, {"label": "Blood Type", "value": "B"}, {"label": "Height", "value": "180cm"}, {"label": "Title", "value": "Senior Machinist"}], "introduction": "Born to tinker. The master mechanic who dreamed of research. Life pushed him to repairs instead. Lost his spark, except when faced with cutting-edge tech.", "stories": [{"title": "May 5, XC 95, Sunny", "text": "\"While these bipedal machines are impressive, they're far from the limit of Arashium alloy's potential. The possibilities are endless! For example, its magneto-rheological properties could revolutionize thermal energy conversion devices. Without a doubt, these properties can be extended to the aerospace field, enabling humanity to achieve feats never before possible! I'm determined to make these breakthroughs myself, which is why, after graduation, I plan to head to Milkhama to study and conduct research on the front lines!\""}, {"title": "January 14, XC 100, Snow", "text": "\"I don't care about labor uprisings or wars. Why should the NDF come and requisition our research institute and demand the assistance of our engineers in repairing their equipment? If they want to fight, they should do it themselves... and if they break something, they should fix it themselves! I didn't come to Milkhama for this crap!\"", "comment": {"by": "Institute Student", "text": "He was trying to chase the soldiers out of the lab with a wrench, but got knocked flat instead... I get why he did it, I really do, but what could we even do to fight back?"}}, {"title": "October 20, XC 115, Rain", "text": "\"Today, I unexpectedly found my diary from my younger years. It's been over a decade since I last wrote in it, and Milkhama and I have changed quite a bit. The research institute that I used to work at has started taking on new recruits, and STs have become commonplace. Arashium alloy has also begun to be used in other fields... However, as someone approaching forty and still working as a machinist to make a living, it no longer has anything to do with me.\""}, {"title": "December 22, XC 117, Cloudy", "text": "\"Recently, my workload suddenly increased significantly, and I was asked to handle certain parts I'd never seen before. They were probably parts from a new machine brought in by the NDF. But how can that structure be applied to these machines? Is the entire frame made of Arashium alloy!? This is really something—no, it's none of my concern anymore! Yes, instead of thinking about this, I should just finish my work early and go home.\""}]}, "10102101": {"profile": [{"label": "Affiliation", "value": "GKD"}, {"label": "Blood Type", "value": "B"}, {"label": "Height", "value": "165cm"}, {"label": "Full Speed", "value": "▇▇ knot/hour"}], "introduction": "They call her \"Captain of the Northwest.\" Harvey has the skill and connections to back it up. She believes in fair deals and stays positive when things go south. After that wild run with Kaidan's crew, she found her path and joined GKD.", "stories": [{"title": "Port", "text": "Speaking of ports, I can't help but think back to the strange twist of fate that brought me and the GKD Squad together. The whole thing wasn't exactly a pleasant memory—being mistaken as bait, misunderstandings, and all that... After all these years as a captain in Milkhama, I've never run into this many problems at once! But, well... when I think about that grand finale, I guess working with the GKD Squad isn't all that bad after all!"}, {"title": "Deck", "text": "\"If the GKD Squad is involved, it's not gonna end well!\" I've said it so many times, my mouth's practically worn out, but Kaidan and the others keep shoving these damn jobs my way. Sure, I did mention wanting a few bigger orders... but I didn't sign up for this level of chaos!", "comment": {"by": "Kaidan", "text": "Whenever you're taking that money, you certainly don't have that frown on your face..."}}, {"title": "Cargo Hold", "text": "Kaidan and Grant aren't always in happy-go-lucky mode. I've noticed that around a certain time, the three of them suddenly vanish without a trace. When I ask them why, they just say they're visiting an old friend. Later, Grant quietly told me that's a wound they can't touch, a pain they'll never forget. If it's got something to do with this island, I think I can guess some of the reasons. The island may look peaceful, but constantly erupts in conflict—Kaidan and his friends must have lost someone important because of it..."}, {"title": "Captain's Cabin", "text": "Alright, let's see what today's order is... Huh, another one for the border. Orders to the other side have been stacking up lately, and they're all weapons or at least something like that. What Kaidan said is true: the illusion of peace in Milkhama might not last much longer. But I'm sure the GKD Squad has already set a plan for the future. When the tides of war are impossible to resist, what's your move gonna be, boss? Guess I'll just have to wait and see.", "comment": {"by": "Grant", "text": "Um...what was our policy again? Oh, right, our \"policy\" is that there is no policy!"}}]}, "10102112": {"profile": [{"label": "Affiliation", "value": "Obsidian Group"}, {"label": "Blood Type", "value": "AB"}, {"label": "Height", "value": "184cm"}, {"label": "Memory Retention", "value": "7%"}, {"label": "Health Condition", "value": "Taste Disorder"}], "introduction": "\"The subject shows positive brain mod response. Tests cleared. No negative effects from memory/emotion wipes noted. Combat reliability meets baseline. Recommend live fire data collection.\" —Obsidian Internal Report", "stories": [{"title": "Warfire", "text": "Hawkwood was born into an ordinary family. His parents worked as frontline miners on Milkhama. They were not wealthy, but life was stable. That is, until one day, his father answered the call to join a labor protest and never came back. Not long after, the sudden outbreak of war claimed his last remaining family member. As a young child, Hawkwood wandered alone through the ruins of his home, where he crossed paths with a mercenary team sweeping through the battlefield."}, {"title": "Mire", "text": "Still a teenager, Hawkwood had already become the captain of the mercenary team's Assault Squad. Like the other members, he lay in ambush on the side of a desert road, listening to the live broadcast of the ceasefire meeting on the radio, waiting for the target convoy to appear—ready to take on one last job before peace arrived.\nHowever, this time, they had the wrong target... The security force escorting the transport convoy was the Obsidian Group."}, {"title": "Experiment", "text": "The researchers at Obsidian finally managed to calm Hawkwood down with a heavy dose of tranquilizers. Subsequent tests confirmed their suspicions—Hawkwood, whose extraordinary combat prowess had caught everyone's eye during the skirmish with the security unit, was perfectly compatible with their new technology. When he awoke from the complicated treatment, the only thing left in his mind was the name \"Hawkwood,\" along with an unwavering loyalty to fight for Obsidian until the bitter end.", "comment": {"by": "Obsidian Researcher", "text": "Deleting emotions and memories has effectively improved combat stability. This achievement warrants further exploration..."}}, {"title": "Change", "text": "His operations were repeatedly hindered by the \"GKD Squad,\" and working with Catherine and Lucia came with its own set of challenges... As a combat weapon, he was supposed to secure victory and prove the superiority of Obsidian technology. Yet, a series of setbacks had undermined him, eroding his confidence. It seemed to reignite an emotion he thought he'd long buried—anger."}]}, "10102113": {"profile": [{"label": "Affiliation", "value": "Obsidian Group"}, {"label": "Blood Type", "value": "B"}, {"label": "Height", "value": "165cm"}, {"label": "Title", "value": "Obsidian Group's Outstanding Liaison Officer of the Year"}], "introduction": "\"Want instant wealth? Status? Ultimate protection on killer Milkhama? Call ▇▇▇▇▇ for Lucia Voight's elite network! Obsidian Corp needs talent like you. Not interested? Keep my card. You will be.\" —Lucia's Merc Recruitment Card", "stories": [{"title": "Campus Rumors", "text": "\"Haha, have you heard? That ass-kisser Lucia, you know, the one who loves to gossip... Haha, she's been expelled. I wonder where she's gonna end up now. I never liked her, that rumor-spreading, ugly skank! She always hid behind whoever had the most power... It's only fair that she's been thrown under the bus... Hahaha!\" – White Maple High School BBS Message", "comment": {"by": "Dana", "text": "Hmph, someone who has been betrayed before... and is now willingly selling themselves out for Obsidian? You really haven't learned your lesson yet, have you?"}}, {"title": "Code Word", "text": "\"A new contact person arrived here recently, and of course, they're from that big company. They always offer the highest price around here. Hmph, if you ask me, it's weird that such a big company sent a nervous wreck like her to a place like this... Don't get me wrong, she's pretty good in a fight and knows how to talk the talk, since being a broker's not exactly an easy job, but if I were her boss, I'd move her to a position with more potential. This border's just a damn mud pit—totally wastes a smart person's real skills...\" — Mercenary Gossip"}, {"title": "CEO's Instructions", "text": "\"I heard the mercenary ops at the border have been running smoothly lately? Did you send someone new there? Yeah, I've heard of her. Supposedly young, tough to control, but seems to fit in well with the environment in Milkhama... Opportunistic and profit-driven, although none of those are exactly good traits, but right now, Obsidian needs people like that. If she makes a name for herself at the border, we can think about bringing her back to Milthus. I've got other jobs for her...\" — Message from Raphael Gideon to his Secretary", "comment": {"by": "Anonymous User", "text": "It's surprising that Gideon chose such a jumpy little brat as his confidante. He is no longer hiding his ambitions for the throne..."}}, {"title": "The Art of Brokering", "text": "\"Have you met the new liaison officer? She's the unlucky seventh to rotate this quarter, but don't let that fool you. Smart, sharp, and quick on her feet—not your usual puppet who just repeats orders. Why give a damn about her? Simple. She's got potential. Like the rest of us, she's just another cog in the company's machine, but there's ambition behind those eyes... Heh, for now, Tolas can still sweeten the deal. But if Obsidian ever has an off day, I wouldn't be surprised if she's the one to push the company over the edge.\" — Catherine's Message to Hawkwood"}]}, "10102106": {"profile": [{"label": "Affiliation", "value": "Union of Northern Continental States"}, {"label": "Blood Type", "value": "A"}, {"label": "Height", "value": "170cm"}, {"label": "Physical Status", "value": "Right eye blindness"}, {"label": "Current Military Rank", "value": "1st Lieutenant"}, {"label": "Special Honor", "value": "Best Instructor (Three Times)"}], "introduction": "NDF drill instructor. Master of combat and ST tactics. Makes boot camp hell because war's worse. They call her \"Devil Instructor,\" but she's saved more recruits than she's broken. Best Instructor in 3 years of running proves it.", "stories": [{"title": "A Talent for Combat", "text": "\"Mary, everyone has their own talent, such as singing, dancing, or what have you... You need to find yours and stick with it.\" My late mother's words echoed in my head as I knocked out a man's tooth for the first time. My hand was wrapped around his neck, flipping his fat body to the ground, watching him fade into unconsciousness from a lack of oxygen. Sirens wailed in the distance. Maybe my talent is fighting and running away, I thought as I fled the scene."}, {"title": "Farewell to the Past", "text": "On Milkhama, there is no history, and the Milkhamans do not even care about history—this is the conclusion I came to in my third year on the island. Even close friends in the NDF do not ask about each other's past. I like this kind of distant relationship, one that separates soldier Mary Rodriguez from the trembling girl hiding in that cabin. It constantly reminds me not to dwell on the past.", "comment": {"by": "Retired Union Serviceman", "text": "I remember one time we were out on a business trip and I heard Mary talking in her sleep at night. She had this frown on her face and was shouting, \"mom\" over and over. Sure, she looks tough, but I bet she had an even tougher childhood she doesn't want anyone to know about."}}, {"title": "Bloodstained Tag", "text": "The failure of that mission came at a heavy cost for the entire squad. As the only survivor who remained unscathed and conscious, I wrote a report close to a hundred pages long and, as the NDF's representative, delivered the belongings of our fallen comrades to their families. If our training had been more rigorous and our plans more precise... could they have all made it out alive? Two weeks later, I submitted my application to transfer to a military academy.", "comment": {"by": "Union Medic", "text": "When she was brought in that day, she was covered in blood and clutching seven or eight military ID tags that didn't belong to her, eyes wider than anything I'd ever seen. It was terrifying..."}}, {"title": "The Devil Instructor", "text": "\"The Devil Instructor\"... I know that's what those cadets call me behind my back, but I couldn't care less. I'm not here to make friends, I'm here to make survivors. Strict, hard training is the only way to make sure mistakes don't end in tragedy. I teach them everything I know—solid combat tactics, and when that doesn't work, I teach them how to run like hell. They hate it, they fight it, but they'll thank me later when they're still standing. I'd rather they curse me than end up dead or useless on the battlefield. That's something I remind myself of every day."}]}, "10102104": {"profile": [{"label": "Affiliation", "value": "Union of Northern Continental States"}, {"label": "Blood Type", "value": "A"}, {"label": "Height", "value": "188cm"}, {"label": "Physical Status", "value": "Healthy"}, {"label": "Current Military Rank", "value": "▇▇"}], "introduction": "\"Raven Bluecher, Blair's boy. Enfield Academy star, active NDF officer. Media calls him the perfect leader-warrior. Truth? Just daddy's sheltered kid.\" —Anonymous Cadet", "stories": [{"title": "Under the Monument", "text": "When I think of my father, the first thing that comes to mind is what he said to me when I was seven years old, standing beneath the border monument: \"You must become a warrior and fight for the UNCS!\" As for why he said that, I was too afraid to ask at the time, and now there's no point in asking again.", "comment": {"by": "Dana", "text": "A strict father and a filial son—what a cliché. The idea of being an \"obedient child\" is bound to shatter sooner or later, for one reason or another..."}}, {"title": "[Bluecher]", "text": "At the military academy, the Bluecher name is like a heavy crown, reminding me at all times that I have to put in more effort than everyone else to gain genuine recognition from them all. Dana Yano, a young woman who is faultless in every way, always seems to be secretly competing with me. Although chivalry dictates that ladies should be given priority in all things, I won't be stepping aside for her—especially not when it comes to proving myself!", "comment": {"by": "Dana", "text": "The envious and fearful gazes of my classmates, consistently scoring 0.5 points higher than me during assessments, the most promising cadet in the eyes of the instructors... Raven Bluecher, without that last name of yours, none of this would be yours!"}}, {"title": "First Day in the Armored Corps", "text": "Joining Major Stein's ranks is an honor for any soldier of the Armored Corps! Though Major Stein may seem hard to approach, the strength he shows in both training and combat is exactly what I aspire to. I hope one day to become a pilot as formidable as Major Stein. If I do, my father will finally see me in a new light...", "comment": {"by": "Dana", "text": "\"Humanity's strongest,\" William Stein... He was once one of the leaders I wanted to follow in the footsteps of, but unfortunately..."}}, {"title": "Subordination and Truth", "text": "Dad's been up to something lately. No... truth is, he's always kept secrets from me. Can't say for sure, but I get the feeling whatever he's working on is tied to this so-called \"classified research.\" What's the real deal here? It doesn't matter—I'm gonna find out for myself if it's the last thing I do."}]}, "10103117": {"profile": [{"label": "Affiliation", "value": "Bounty Hunter"}, {"label": "Blood Type", "value": "AB"}, {"label": "Height", "value": "176cm"}, {"label": "Favorite Food", "value": "Smoked Ox Jerky"}, {"label": "Heads Collected", "value": "372"}, {"label": "Partner", "value": "Melissa Hicks"}], "introduction": "\"Rebecca, Apex Hunter, raid specialist, Canary's partner.\nWild cowgirl pre-Canary, worked UNCS despite DL roots. She was a great solo fighter but dropped 70% of jobs following her whims.\nPartnership cut bad reviews by 90%, seems Canary's got her in line.\" —The Hunter's Guide", "stories": [{"title": "Getting Started", "text": "\"Miss Rebecca Klose, could you please confirm again that this ID card belongs to you? According to the current regulations, minors cannot apply for a bounty hunter license... No, no, I'm not suggesting that you become a bandit—I don't think children should... Look, you passed the test, and that proves you're qualified to become a bounty hunter. Please come back to collect your license three days from now.\" — Harpy Office Recording, July 24, XC 104", "comment": {"by": "Shawnee", "text": "I guarantee that nothing of that sort will happen in the Dawnstar League of today. The battlefield is no place for children."}}, {"title": "Cross-Border", "text": "\"Senior Bounty Hunter Klose, are you sure you want to transfer the collection range of this commission to the West Milkhama region? Although the war has been over for five years, as a citizen of the Dawnstar League and with extensive experience assisting military operations, your presence in the UNCS Jurisdiction remains... a sensitive subject. I'm sorry, I'll process the relevant procedures for you now, but please remember that your hometown will always welcome you back with open arms.\" — Harpy Office Recording, January 4, XC 106", "comment": {"by": "Fenrir", "text": "Taking on a job like hers, straddling the line of legality—it's a dangerous game. No one's gonna welcome someone crossing over from the other side of the island."}}, {"title": "Flexible", "text": "\"Rebecca! This is already the 18th time you've violated your contract... What did you say? You thought the employer was a jerk and didn't provide the information promised in the agreement, so you turned around and shot him? Remember, you need to complete a transaction if you want to make any money. You can't expect to succeed in this line of work if no one wants to hire you again!\" — Harpy Office Recording, March 21, XC 110", "comment": {"by": "Alyson", "text": "I'd kill for a crew full of characters like that. It'd certainly make things more interesting."}}, {"title": "Encounter", "text": "\"Welcome, Apex Bounty Hunter Rebecca, this mission takes you to the southern part of the Parill Desert. Tensions have risen between the autonomous military forces of the Doll Group and the UNCS in several nearby towns, and many civilians have requested help, hoping someone can offer them shelter... You want to know who the stationed officer is? Let me see... It's Hicks, the hero who made First Lieutenant during the Milkhama War...\" — Harpy Office Recording, March 1, XC 117"}]}, "10102108": {"profile": [{"label": "Affiliation", "value": "Union of Northern Continental States"}, {"label": "Blood Type", "value": "AB"}, {"label": "Height", "value": "169cm"}, {"label": "Title", "value": "Chief Researcher of the Hyper-Aptamer project"}], "introduction": "Winston Gresham, neuro expert, pioneered medical Arashium. Pushed radical experiments in UNCS Hyper program, breaking Newman's limits. Crazy science, but Valentina says he's decent enough.", "stories": [{"title": "Classified Record 1", "text": "Winston Gresham is a world-renowned neurology expert and the leading figure in the intersection of \"Arashium alloy\" and neurology. He is also the director of the No. 3 Research Institute of the UNCS. Known for his meticulous work ethic, sharp insight, and exceptional execution, Winston was highly praised for his professional and interpersonal skills before being invited to participate in the \"Hyper-Aptamer\" project. His reputation, both in his field and beyond, is nothing short of stellar. Proud of his role as a scientific leader, he often takes part in public events, showcasing his unwavering commitment to advancing research."}, {"title": "Classified Record 2", "text": "At the invitation of UNCS Viceroy Blair Bluecher, Winston joined the Union-Obsidian Joint Research Institute as an expert researcher. Here, he met two other colleagues—Cicero, a rising star in the field of Arashium research, and Newman, who later became known as a \"genius.\""}, {"title": "Classified Record 3", "text": "After joining the \"Hyper-Aptamer\" project, Winston's authority was challenged for the first time. Winston felt an insurmountable gap, whether it was Cicero's neural connection tech or Newman's Nova-Frame concept. Winston, who had never been willing to admit defeat, flung himself into a frenzy of extreme and reckless research, and the relationship between the three gradually shifted from mutual assistance and cooperation to competition, and even hostility. Everyone marveled at Dr. Newman's greatness when the Diaz sisters were found, and the Nova-Frame was completed. Winston finally realized who he was up against.", "comment": {"by": "Researcher", "text": "Since then, Director Winston has become a different person. He became more focused on his research, even gradually becoming less receptive to the viceroy's suggestions and neglecting his personal needs, such as sleep and food."}}, {"title": "Classified Record 4", "text": "Just as Winston had pushed himself to exhaustion, an unexpected turn of events disrupted the competition. Cicero and Newman, without Winston's knowledge or that of the entire UNCS Jurisdiction, led an escape plan... The result of the plan was the murder of Dr. Newman, and Cicero and Diaz's whereabouts became unknown. As the successor to their research, the viceroy ordered Winston to lead the follow-up work for the \"Hyper-Aptamer\" project. However, Winston no longer found joy in controlling the lab. On the contrary, his only desire was to surpass Newman. He would forge ahead with his own research, no matter the cost.", "comment": {"by": "Researcher", "text": "Director Winston, the \"Adaptor,\" has entered the final debugging phase. We will soon be able to officially deploy her onto the battlefield."}}]}, "10101102": {"profile": [{"label": "Affiliation", "value": "Pacific Company"}, {"label": "Blood Type", "value": "B"}, {"label": "Height", "value": "180cm"}, {"label": "Monthly Salary", "value": "Classified"}], "introduction": "Pacific Corp's most punctual guard. Could be Employee of the Month if he weren't such a slacker. He keeps to himself unless you want to talk to STs.", "stories": [{"title": "Area A   Checked", "text": "Adrien, a Pacific Company security guard, was originally a mercenary. He was quiet and lacked motivation, and even when he occasionally did speak, it was only to talk about work with his colleagues. His work ethic wasn't exactly stellar, but at least he completed his tasks on time. Compared to other pilots on this island, he's the definition of a man who keeps to himself.", "comment": {"by": "Security", "text": "Adrien's meticulous in his work—the guy never makes mistakes. And hey, if the boss says it's fine, who's to say otherwise?"}}, {"title": "Logistics Area      Checked", "text": "During breaks, Adrien usually retreats to a quiet spot to eat alone, never initiating conversation with anyone. But from what his colleagues have said, he's actually quite likeable. Someone once asked him out of curiosity why he eats alone, but he casually brushed them off, saying it merely saves him energy."}, {"title": "Monitoring Room      Checked", "text": "Adrien may seem indifferent to the world, but he surprisingly has a fondness for reading. His favorite genre is anything related to mechs, followed closely by nonfiction. Of course, he's flipped through pretty much every book in the break room. Occasionally, others ask to borrow books from him. As long as they don't dog-ear the pages, he's usually fine with it.", "comment": {"by": "Security", "text": "Most of the books in his collection are about STs or the real-life events of Milkhama Island, but still, he gives the impression of being completely unrelated to all that."}}, {"title": "Entrance      Checked", "text": "Even on his days off, Adrien mostly stays at home. This island attracts many ambitious people, some of whom are naturally curious about why he's here. He's not entirely indifferent, though, as seen from the piles of books scattered around his room—an indication of his keen interest in Arashium technology and the new generation of STs."}]}, "10101103": {"profile": [{"label": "Affiliation", "value": "The Ashes"}, {"label": "Blood Type", "value": "AB"}, {"label": "Height", "value": "167cm"}], "introduction": "Ask Ashes about Chloe Schmidt, they'll say she is a dedicated medic and a tough captain. Ask Yevgeny, he'll call her a true warrior. Ask her? Just a smile and \"who knows\" as she works.", "stories": [{"title": "Schmidt Clinic", "text": "When I was a kid, playing in the clinic my parents ran together was what I looked forward to most. Occasionally, when there were no patients to be seen, my dad would hold me in one arm while reading me obscure medical books that were far difficult for me to understand. I would laugh at his scribbled annotations. When the clinic was crowded, my mom would place me at the desk, tell the nurse to keep an eye on me, and then turn around to join my dad."}, {"title": "Mission Improbable", "text": "That night, the DL's target was a military base on the outskirts of White Maple City. My mother carried me to the shelter on an armored vehicle, holding me tightly as I cried. She told me that she and my father had a mission to complete. I refused to let go of her clothes... until she handed me a cold, sharp military knife. \"Take it, Chloe. It will protect you when we can't, but remember—a knife can both harm and save people.\" These were my mother's last words to me."}, {"title": "Twisted Fate", "text": "Afterward, I became a neutral doctor, treating all the civilians who came to me for help. I lived my life in a daze until one early morning, a group of guys wearing UNCS uniforms rushed into my clinic and took me back to the military camp without any explanation. I refused to treat anyone from the UNCS, so they locked me up and cut off my food supply. I thought it was the end for me—as I was starving to death. Then I heard gunshots, and the cell door opened. I struggled to lift my head and saw a long-haired man with a fierce look standing out in the hall."}, {"title": "Destined Military Doctor", "text": "Captain Chloe, Dr. Chloe... that's what the warriors of The Ashes call me. They come from all corners of Milkhama, most of them few with words to say. Still, they express their kindness in their own way—finely tuned STs, new medicines from unknown sources, a spotless clinic... Perhaps The Ashes will become my new home, I sometimes silently think to myself."}]}, "10101106": {"profile": [{"label": "Affiliation", "value": "The Principality of Ovett"}, {"label": "Blood Type", "value": "O"}, {"label": "Height", "value": "190cm"}, {"label": "Engineering ST License", "value": "Revoked"}], "introduction": "Ovett merchant runs booze and more to Milkhama. Plays the loud friendly trader, deals on profit not politics. Done jobs with GKD. Really a sharp operator working for Ovett's comeback.", "stories": [{"title": "Foreign Merchant", "text": "When I first came to Milkhama, everyone I did business with would ask me curiously why an Ovettian would travel all the way here. I could never give a solid answer, and would just brush it off with a \"I came to make money.\" That was until one night, barely keeping my head together after pulling an all-nighter, I muttered out, \"To revive Ovett\"... Hah, who would have thought those words would come out of my mouth? But from that moment on, I thought, maybe taking this idea seriously wasn't such a bad thing after all."}, {"title": "Booming Business", "text": "After business picked up, I formed connections with more prominent organizations. I began selling Ovett's specialty drinks and products to the local elite who indulge in such pleasures. I also purchased rare local items to bring back with me, like α ore and Arashium alloy. While the UNCS and DL impose strict restrictions on these goods, Milkhama isn't fully under their control... On this island, things are far more accessible, depending on how deep your pockets run.", "comment": {"by": "Naomi", "text": "Although that's true, Arashium alloy isn't something you can easily obtain just by throwing money at it. This old man definitely has some hidden connections no one knows about!"}}, {"title": "Storm", "text": "Traveling between the cities of the two superpowers, even those who are indifferent to the current situation should have noticed the propaganda of the NDF has increased significantly compared to previous years, the trade of resources such as metal and medicine is constantly being restricted, and the scrutiny of cross-border transportation has blatantly increased... The peace that has been maintained for nearly a decade may be about to change. Therefore, I have decided to develop trade relations with other forces I've never engaged with before. Even if I can't avoid the storm, at least I'll know which way the wind is blowing."}, {"title": "Penetration", "text": "The \"GKD Parcel Service,\" especially that young man named \"Kaidan Newman,\" has made quite a splash, despite only a few brief collaborations. Now, the UNCS, the DL, and even the mysterious Obsidian Group have started to take action against them. Even the underground mercenaries and merchants occasionally discuss events linked to them... The powder keg hidden on this island might just be about to be lit by those renegades."}]}, "10101108": {"profile": [{"label": "Affiliation", "value": "Union of Northern Continental States"}, {"label": "Blood Type", "value": "O"}, {"label": "Height", "value": "188cm"}], "introduction": "Jon Brewster, ex-NDF merc. War broke him. Lost too many friends. Now works the Northwest jungle. Known for keeping his word—rare for a merc in these parts.", "stories": [{"title": "Mercenary Era", "text": "Jon is by no means a desperado. In his mind, there is a clear hierarchy: first is his own life, followed by his companions, and lastly, money. Following this philosophy, Jon has led his teammates on the battlefield countless times to survive in desperate situations without making choices he might regret.", "comment": {"by": "Grant", "text": "Hell yeah! Surviving is the only shot you've got! Sure, the outsiders love to look down on the mercenary code, but to me? That's the number one rule for staying alive. What do you think, boss?"}}, {"title": "Partner", "text": "That said, not all his comrades would make it out unscathed. In the dead of night, Jon would see their faces. Many of them were forced to step onto the front lines for the sake of their families or survival, carrying hopes for the future but ultimately perishing in the dust. He'll never forget the burden his companions carried for a slim chance at peace. He must survive, along with their share, to welcome peace on Milkhama Island.", "comment": {"by": "Kaidan", "text": "Yeah... You can't stay lost in sorrow forever. They handed their lives over to us... so it's on us to carry their part and see the right future unfold!"}}, {"title": "Money", "text": "People often say, \"Money makes the world go round,\" and Jon couldn't agree more. Especially in these unstable times, making money is far more practical than worrying about appearances. It's not that he's obsessed with wealth—if you ask him why he wants to make money, he'll tell you: money is the only thing that might buy him a little peace of mind."}, {"title": "War and Peace", "text": "After the border war, Jon tried his hand at jobs outside of being a mercenary, but now, he's back in that familiar cockpit. The main reason he returned to the battlefield was his comrades. He couldn't bear to watch the ravaged land again, nor could he stand the thought of others sacrificing themselves for him."}]}, "10101105": {"profile": [{"label": "Affiliation", "value": "Union of Northern Continental States"}, {"label": "Blood Type", "value": "AB"}, {"label": "Height", "value": "170cm"}, {"label": "Total receipts", "value": "17,146,872 MHD (self records)"}, {"label": "Total Expenses", "value": "8,871,202 MHD (self records)"}], "introduction": "Kaylen Evans, UNCS Coast Guard, claims top connections. Greedy coward who hates combat. Dreams of cashing out and leaving Milkhama rich.", "stories": [{"title": "A Thousand Names", "text": "I simply cannot stand it when people try to give me these animal-based nicknames. It's nothing short of an indirect insult! I've done absolutely nothing to provoke anyone at school—I've merely used my resources, as any sensible person would. And yet, behind my back, they refer to me as a \"yellow rat\" or a \"stinking fox.\" It's totally unreasonable!", "comment": {"by": "Anonymous Middle-Aged Person", "text": "This scoundrel, huh... When he became a member of the student council, he collected lunch money from everyone—and he dared to call it a \"campus development fee\"!"}}, {"title": "Desired Location", "text": "Why join the NDF? For the money, of course. Why come to Milkhama? Someone told me there's money to be made all over this place. Hmph... that being said, when I actually arrived here, I realized I was too late—the smart ones had already taken the best positions, and all that was left was scraps."}, {"title": "Complex Connections", "text": "After all these years, I finally climbed to my current position with the help of that big shot! What I need to do next is establish connections with everyone in the coastal defense army and then wait for the money to come rolling in! I've done my research—there's not a single tough nut to crack here. If I spend a little cash and offer some minor perks, golden days are finally coming my way!"}, {"title": "Brewing Defection", "text": "The seas have been getting rough lately, and I keep getting dragged into combat missions. Tch... If it weren't for the pressure, I wouldn't step foot on a battlefield at all! That big shot is planning some large-scale action that could threaten the governor. Maybe it's time to seize this chance, switch sides, and join the governor's faction with all the intel I possess?", "comment": {"by": "Naomi", "text": "Hmm? Wait, could the important guy he's talking about be...?"}}]}, "10101107": {"profile": [{"label": "Affiliation", "value": "Dawnstar League"}, {"label": "Blood Type", "value": "A"}, {"label": "Height", "value": "166cm"}], "introduction": "Lily Stan, DLAF peacekeeping captain. Battle-hardened White Rose, troops trust her completely. Total faith in DLAF bringing peace to every corner of Milkhama.", "stories": [{"title": "Cum Laude", "text": "Whenever Lily Stan is mentioned, both the faculty and students at the military academy can't help but show a rare, relaxed smile and say a few words of praise. In drills, she's a brave and skilled soldier; during preparations, she's a meticulous and thoughtful squad leader; on leave, she's an understanding woman. As she puts it, the Dawnstar League symbolizes the flag of freedom, which always flies proudly in her heart."}, {"title": "Determination", "text": "Joining the peacekeeping forces and being stationed on Milkhama was Lily's choice after graduating. She could never forget the scene when she first set foot on the island—the city, still recovering from shelling, was in the midst of reconstruction, while refugees wandered aimlessly through the ruins, heads lowered, and distant cries of children echoing in the background. In that moment, Lily vowed to save this place and support the Dawnstar League in bringing lasting peace to the island.", "comment": {"by": "DL Peacekeeping Soldier", "text": "Senior Officer Lily, the \"White Rose\" of our forces!"}}, {"title": "Resident", "text": "Peacekeeping proved to be even more challenging than Lily had anticipated. Although the so-called war had officially ended years ago, occasional small-scale conflicts still threatened civilian survival, and refugee camps often faced shortages of essential supplies. Most of the soldiers who came to Milkhama with her had already returned home, but Lily refused to sign the redeployment order.", "comment": {"by": "DL Peacekeeping Soldier", "text": "I really don't understand what's so good about that island! I wish I'd never set foot in that damn place!"}}, {"title": "Abide", "text": "Lately, rumors have been circulating through the military, causing Lily to worry even more about the island's future. The current peace will be shattered, and a new war will come. She has a gut feeling that there's some truth behind these whispers, and the recent troop deployments from the DLAF to Milkhama only seem to confirm her fears. But despite it all, she'll continue to hold on until the ideal peace arrives."}]}, "10101101": {"profile": [{"label": "Blood Type", "value": "O"}, {"label": "Height", "value": "182cm"}, {"label": "Imprisoned count", "value": "One less time than Fenrir (self claimed)"}], "introduction": "Movme Bellows, Electric Eel freelancer. Loyal to Frida and hates Fenrir's guts. Shady past. Sly, greedy coward with no morals or ambition. Classic bottom-feeder.", "stories": [{"title": "Juvenile Delinquent", "text": "\"Movme Bellows, male, 17 years old, parents deceased. On the morning of May 19th, he caused an altercation on the streets of White Maple, resulting in two minor injuries. Since his detention, he has confessed to his crime. According to Article 53, Section 4 of the Criminal Law of the Union of Northern Continental States, he is sentenced to two years for intentional harm.\" — White Maple City Supreme Court", "comment": {"by": "Prison Guard", "text": "The offender has shown resistance to discipline, has performed labor duties unwillingly, showed no remorse while serving his rehabilitation sentence, and was twice placed in solitary confinement."}}, {"title": "The End of Innocence", "text": "\"Movme Bellows, male, 28 years old, was admitted to our hospital on August 16th with shoulder penetration wounds, scalp lacerations, and numerous other injuries. Our hospital has been commissioned by the NDF to assess the extent of his injuries. The evaluation concludes that the injuries are classified as level one light injuries. After treatment, the patient is out of danger and has been handed over to the NDF for further handling.\" — Rayneburg University Medical Center", "comment": {"by": "Street Thug", "text": "That kid's asking for it! He gets a couple of insults thrown his way and decides to throw down with a guy in uniform? He deserves whatever he gets!"}}, {"title": "Electric Eel Cohort", "text": "[Movme, age unknown, biography unknown. Specializes in stealing and fighting. Poor psychological resilience, prone to losing control under pressure. Introduced by the chief to join the Southern Detachment after Operation 503, under the direct management of the chief. Commission to be determined.] — Electric Eel Mercenary Regiment Information Registration Form"}, {"title": "External Member", "text": "[I, Movme, am out of the Electric Eel! From now on, I ain't takin' orders from Frida no more, and I'm cutting ties from Fenrir and the whole damn mercenary crew! If we ever link up again, the money's gotta be straight—count it in person, for crying out loud! I stand by my word, no turning back!] — Electric Eel Mercenaries File Book", "comment": {"by": "Electric Eel Member", "text": "This kid says he's out of the organization, but he's still following the boss around, nodding his head and kissing up all day long!"}}]}, "10101104": {"profile": [{"label": "Affiliation", "value": "Bounty Hunter"}, {"label": "Blood Type", "value": "O"}, {"label": "Height", "value": "178cm"}, {"label": "CD Collections", "value": "1047 Disks"}], "introduction": "Pip Beswick, mystery bounty hunter. Music lover, born wanderer. Free spirit who treats bounties like shopping lists. The moral compass spins differently. Oddly fixated on Kaidan's GKD.", "stories": [{"title": "Forgotten Homeland", "text": "The first time I did someone's dirty work for them was around thirteen years old. It wasn't a glamorous job, but I still remember that woman's blue eyes. Damn, they were mesmerizing... After that, business picked up, with regulars coming in and out. Then... well, there was that time I was working to some tunes, and without thinking, I made a mistake and got rid of someone important. Had to pack up and leave in a hurry that night. Honestly, I can't even remember how old I was when I left the country. Eh... whatever, that stuff doesn't matter anymore. ♪"}, {"title": "Cavalry Hunter", "text": "I love the wandering pilot guild in Milkhama! Although they kept laughing while processing my paperwork, they gave me a good list and taught me how to operate an ST! Oh, I love Milkhama's STs! Sitting in the cockpit, the people under my feet are as cute and helpless as little cats and dogs. With the 360-degree surround sound, I can zip through missions with a swoosh! Post-war Milkhama is such a great place! ♪", "comment": {"by": "Experienced Bounty Hunter", "text": "When asked for his name, this kid just glanced at an old newspaper posted on the wall and answered without thinking. Hahaha, \"Pip\" and \"Beswick\"? Those two kicked the can just recently!"}}, {"title": "Superficial Success", "text": "These days, mercenary squads of all sizes are popping up all over the island, offering everything from A to Z. They've even started snatching up the big orders I used to get, leaving me with only the small stuff. And don't get me started on those so-called legit logistics companies—they might look above board, but they're secretly gunning for my business too! Kid, honestly, I wouldn't mind if things got even more chaotic around here. At least that way I could rake in some serious cash, hahaha...♪"}, {"title": "Enchanting Chaos", "text": "Now things are getting interesting! Lately, there's been a real buzz in Milkhama, with rebels stirring things up and the NDF making big moves. Word is, the new recruits who took down the UNCS's Valkyrie are hanging around the jungle area. They've even set up a pretty solid logistics company and are running their own show! Woohoo♪! I'd love to cross paths with those guys if I get the chance!"}]}, "10101109": {"profile": [{"label": "Affiliation", "value": "Dawnstar League"}, {"label": "Blood Type", "value": "B"}, {"label": "Height", "value": "200cm"}, {"label": "Reason for Incarceration", "value": "Intentional Injury (Revised to Not Guilty)"}], "introduction": "DL trucker hauls anything for a price. Quiet but fierce, personally fought off hijackers multiple times. Senses the storm coming to Milkhama. Planning his survival and escape route home.", "stories": [{"title": "April 2, XC 104, Sunny", "text": "\"In the second year after I came to Milkhama, I was sent to prison. The charge was intentional injury, with the court ruling that I had severely injured a person I had never even met before... I pleaded guilty but denied all accusations linking the incident to my boss. A large sum of money also appeared in my parents' account back in my distant hometown—just as I had agreed with my boss. This was my decision, and what I had to do... was to spend seven years of my life here.\""}, {"title": "August 3, XC 109, Cloudy", "text": "\"I was released from prison two years earlier than initially planned... I heard that my boss's true colors were revealed, and the truth came out, leading to my acquittal. As I left, the prison was abuzz. Some were cursing loudly, others sighing in relief. I understood what they were thinking—resenting the heavy lessons I'd handed out to every troublemaker, yet also afraid of the dozens of terrifying scars on my body.\"", "comment": {"by": "Prison Guard", "text": "I find it really hard to believe he's innocent. If you'd seen him beating up those problem prisoners without uttering so much as a word, you'd agree with me too."}}, {"title": "January 21, XC 116, Heavy Rain", "text": "\"I've been running private goods transport for years, and it's obvious my regular routes are becoming less and less safe. It used to be just some local bullies looking to intercept shipments, but now I'm seeing entire squads of rebels, commanding military-grade STs. On top of that, security checkpoints are popping up more and more along the way... With the weight and those complex anti-demagnetization, fire-resistant containers, I know I can't afford to be careless with the stuff I'm hauling in this truck of mine.\""}, {"title": "April 15, XC 118, Cloudy", "text": "\"Weapons, medicine, intelligence, human resources... they're not only circulating within the DL, but more and more are being sent to the UNCS and even the rebels. Many of my acquaintances have recognized the danger and left the industry, causing prices to climb higher and higher. This is good news for me... Even if Milkhama is on the brink of a new war, it's nothing to do with me. All I need to do is make enough money and return to my homeland.\""}]}, "10101110": {"profile": [{"label": "Affiliation", "value": "UNCS Winston Research Institute"}, {"label": "Blood Type", "value": "A"}, {"label": "Height", "value": "165cm"}, {"label": "Education", "value": "Master of Biomedical Engineering"}, {"label": "Steel Trooper Operation Subjects", "value": "Unqualified"}], "introduction": "Ovett native. Enfield Academy grad. All business, all study. Topped tech theory and became Winston's apprentice. Now, it helps research bio-mech fusion.", "stories": [{"title": "August 17, XC 111, Sunny", "text": "\"Today's the day of the research institute visit! I was so excited I barely slept all night and left early in the morning. I begged the researcher to take me to areas off-limits to students. I was completely mesmerized by the prototype machines locked behind bulletproof glass, staring at them for so long that I didn't even notice someone standing behind me. 'Would you be interested in pursuing research in this field?' the person asked with a smile. Of course, I nodded eagerly. But, I wonder... who was that person?\""}, {"title": "February 16, XC 113, Rain", "text": "\"Failed again... If I could, I'd skip every single class related to ST combat. I don't think I'll ever understand why those guys in military school are so obsessed with it. Sweating like crazy... It's honestly the most boring thing I can imagine! At least tomorrow we've got a theory exam... Phew, I guess I really do prefer wearing a white coat and working with machines.\"", "comment": {"by": "Naomi", "text": "If possible, I want to be a hacker who only deals with data..."}}, {"title": "July 8, XC 117, Rain", "text": "\"Today marks exactly one week since I arrived at the Winston Research Institute. Though I had heard of the renowned Dr. Winston before, I couldn't help but marvel when I saw the prototypes made from Arashium alloy. It's a shame Dr. Newman, the initiator of this research, is no longer around. Progress could've been even faster if he were still here. If only I could learn everything and take this technology back with me...\""}, {"title": "September 25, XC 117, Cloudy", "text": "\"Our research has encountered an unprecedented bottleneck. The higher-ups are very dissatisfied with our progress, and Dr. Winston always has a furrowed brow. I heard that the situation outside remains unstable. Today, I even received an encrypted email from the NDF telling us to 'be ready to move at any time.' What will the future hold...? How much longer can 'she' wait for me...?\"", "comment": {"by": "Naomi", "text": "Huh? \"She\"...? Are you talking about your own mother?"}}]}, "10103187": {"profile": [{"label": "Affiliation", "value": "掠食者小队"}, {"label": "Blood Type", "value": "A"}, {"label": "Height", "value": "172cm"}, {"label": "曾属组织", "value": "缄默会"}, {"label": "Body Modification Level", "value": "1%"}], "introduction": "「摩根娜·斯莱斯，掠食者小队精锐，希迪恩社长的心腹。平时慵懒散漫、言辞圆滑；在任务中却判若两人，行动高效、判断精准，展现出不逊于黑障中队精英的优秀素养。我们曾怀疑她与社长推行的『更生计划』有关，但后续情报显示她身上没有任何岚质改造迹象。\n她的早年履历迷雾重重，仅可确定其加入掠食者前曾在奥维特公国境内长期停留。有传闻称她曾隶属于杀手组织『缄默会』，因任务失败而逃亡米赫玛转投社长麾下，但相关记录缺失，具体经历无法完全核实。近期与禁军方向接触增多，多次以掠食者行动名义与外部势力发生战斗，行动存在明显偏向，目前尚无法确定其目的。\n总体评估：能力顶尖，情绪稳定，但对黑曜石缺乏归属感，忠诚仅系于希迪恩社长的个人情分，属可控范围内的不稳定因素。建议持续观察其对外接触，暂不惊动。」——黑曜石内部监察报告", "stories": [{"title": "缄默会", "text": "「摩根娜来的时候还很小，被人贩子拖进来的，身上还带着挨过打的痕迹。这没什么特别的，缄默会里大多是这样的孩子——被遗弃的、被拐卖的，又或者本就是孤儿……我们早就看惯了。不过她的反应倒是和其他孩子不太一样，不哭也不闹，就站在屋子中间，用那双眼睛把周围的人一个一个看过去，安静得像在记什么账。\n后来没多久，她就开始了训练。这里的训练可不轻松，淘汰率高得惊人，受伤更是家常便饭，但她学得飞快……刀法、身法、伪装、潜入，样样都像天生就会，就连机兵驾驶都能很快上手。教她的老人说，这丫头这辈子就是做杀手的命。\n再后来，她所在的小组去执行了第一次任务。回来时她手上沾着血，脸上一丝表情都没有。其他孩子吐了半夜，她第二天照常训练，手稳得像没发生过任何事。有人觉得她冷血，我倒觉得是她聪明，聪明到小小年纪就已经看明白——在缄默会，心软的人是活不长的。\n等她长到十八岁时，已经是年轻一代里最利落的那把刀，几乎所有人都认定她会成为组织未来的绝对王牌。」——缄默会某杀手口述"}, {"title": "潜伏", "text": "「当时的我还只是一个新人情报员，负责南边几个不起眼小镇的情报收集工作，根本不会想到某一天玛格丽塔长官会亲自召见我，还给了我一个绝密任务——接应缄默会的杀手摩根娜，帮助她接近沃洛科夫家族。\n我本想借着这个机会好好表现一番，就事无巨细地为摩根娜制定了一整套潜伏方案，她没有反对也没有接受。直到行动正式开始，我才明白她才是经验更加丰富的那一方。她没有按我计划的那样假扮行商，而是将这个身份安给了一个早已转移的情报员，就此引开了公国探子的视线。她自己则伪装成旅行者，在镇上开了个学堂赚点旅费，掩护做得滴水不漏，还很快和当地人熟络了起来。\n过了一个多月，她的汇报里开始出现『索妮娅』这个名字——根据玛格丽塔长官的情报，我们知道索妮娅就是沃洛科夫家族之主藏在这的私生女，而摩根娜也如计划那样成功接近了她。摩根娜不止一次说起那孩子聪明、会看人眼色，但在家族里活得像个影子。我起初没当回事，以为她在评估利用价值，直到后来我才明白，摩根娜其实早就拿到了我们需要的关键情报。她在那孩子身上花的那些心思，并不都是任务需要的。\n恐怕就是因为这，在明确那个孩子拥有成为禁军潜质的那一刻起，她就决定站到我们的对立面了吧。」——奥维特革命军某情报员的报告"}, {"title": "掠食者", "text": "「早期的掠食者小队和现在不同，没有大规模部队，没有先进机兵，就只有几个没法留在阳光下的人聚拢在希迪恩社长身边，替他处理一些棘手的任务，我和摩根娜就是那时候认识的——当时社长从奥维特回来，将这个遍体鳞伤的女人交给我治疗，还特意嘱咐我不对她进行更生改造。她恢复得很快，和大家相处得也很融洽，对自己的过去也不会遮遮掩掩，所以我很快就知道了她来到米赫玛岛之前的故事。\n她曾是隶属缄默会的杀手，由于奥维特革命军的委托而潜伏到沃洛科夫家族周边刺探军事情报，还特意演了场戏当起了老师。她演得很好，很快就拿到了有价值的情报，可她也没想到，演到最后自己似乎将『老师』这个身份当了真。为了保护那个被革命军长官盯上的女孩，她放弃了任务，与自己的雇主为敌。\n这么一来，奥维特她是无论如何也待不下去了。革命军当她是间谍，缄默会当她是叛徒，两拨人都在找她，而社长就是在那时候收留了她。事实证明社长的眼光总是很准，虽然摩根娜时常抱怨工作繁忙，还成天盘算着哪天金盆洗手，找个安静的地方安度晚年……但不得不承认，她确实比谁都懂得这一行的活法，每个任务都完成得干净利落。我也就此多了一个活得足够久、能聊些心里话的朋友。\n不过关于那孩子后来究竟如何了，她从不提，我也不会去问……这是我们这些只能活在黑暗里的家伙最基本的默契。」——掠食者小队某高级研究员口述"}, {"title": "去向", "text": "「久疏问候，艾琳长官。我按照您的吩咐盯了摩根娜·斯莱斯一年，现在向您汇报我的阶段性调查结果。\n作为一名掠食者，摩根娜的表现几乎挑不出毛病。凡是交到她手上的任务，件件完成得干净利落、不留痕迹，这种手段不像是在寻常佣兵堆里练出来的。而且她还具备相当优秀的反侦察意识，如果不是有潜伏在掠食者内部的同伴协助，我可能在半年前就已经暴露了。虽无直接证据，但『她曾隶属缄默会』这一点恐怕并非谣言。\n不过最让我在意的不是她的能力，而是她近来的动向。她以掠食者小队的名义与多个外部势力有所接触，其中有您很重视的猎豹物流，也有长期在暗中活动的叶夫根尼·高曼，这很可能是得到了希迪恩社长的某种授意。\n另外，根据本土的情报，奥维特公国禁军特种侦察营已经派人渗透进了米赫玛岛，而同时期内摩根娜去向不明的行程明显增多——她究竟是想替谁办事、办什么事，我无法妄断，只能如实报告。\n是否需要加派人手加以控制，还请您示下。」——黑曜石监察员的报告节选"}], "cn": true}};
